(59, 'VIETNAM & CAMBODIA', NULL, '7781000140', NULL, 'VIETNAM & CAMBODIA', '2019-02-25', 9, 0, 1, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HA NOI ARRIVAL  [DINNER]\",\"date\":\"25-02-2019 Monday\",\"todo\":\"Arrive in Ha Noi, the tour guide pick up and transfer to hotel.  Afternoon, start with the city tour includes such sights as Ho Chi Minh\'s Mausoleum and his house on stilts, the One Pillar Pagoda, the Temple of Literature, the Quanh Thanh Temple and the Tran Quoc Pagoda on the edge of West Lake.Dinner at the Indian restaurant.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HA NOI \\u2013 HA LONG BAY \\u2013 HA NOI  [BREAKFAST + LUNCH + DINNER]\",\"date\":\"26-02-2019 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"An early start to leave Hanoi by 07:00 for Halong Bay. Enjoy the journey through the rich farmlands of the Red River Delta and the scenery of rice fields, water buffalo and everyday Vietnamese village life. Arrive in Halong and board a private junk for a 4 - hour cruise on the emerald green waters of Halong Bay, among the 3,000 spectacular limestone islands. A fresh seafood lunch will be served on board. In the middle of the afternoon head back to Halong, then on to Hanoi. Arrive in Hanoi around 19:00 in the evening and transfer back to hotel. Dinner at the Indian restaurant.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HA NOI \\u2013 HO CHI MINH  [BREAKFAST + LUNCH + DINNER]\",\"date\":\"27-02-2019 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"Breakfast at the hotel.  Transfer to the airport for flight to Ho Chi Minh. Arrival, tour guide pick up and transfer to hotel.After lunch visit the former Presidential Palace, from there on you will go on foot (the car will be available at all times) to visit the major sights of colonial Ho Chi Minh City: the Notre Dame Cathedral, Old Saigon Post Office, Dong Khoi Street (formerly Rue Catinat), Continental Hotel, Opera House and City Hall. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh City.Dinner at the Indian restaurant.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HO CHI MINH \\u2013 MEKONG \\u2013 HO CHI MINH  [BREAKFAST + LUNCH + DINNER]\",\"date\":\"28-02-2019 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"Breakfast at hotel. 08.30 am in the morning, take 2 hour drive southwest of Ho Chi Minh City to the Mekong Delta which is known as the rice bowl of Vietnam. Upon arrival, take a boat cruise around islets and tropical orchards through the canal of Vam Xep to reach a small islet, followed by a relaxing walk along shady and palm fringed trails passing by local villages where you can see their peaceful daily life. Stop en route to visit a bee farm, sip special tea with honey and sample fruits with a local family and share their stories of life in the Mekong Delta. Visit a small coconut workshop, just to get a glimpse of typical family run business in this area.  Lunch at the local restaurant. Walk to a lane where a horse-drawn cart awaits you to transfer to visit handicraft village, a coconut candy factory, enjoy tropical fruit, traditional music and then relaxation with rowing boat through the narrow under shade palm, tree-lined canals of Mekong River before returning to My Tho by motorized boat. Back Ho Chi Minh. Dinner at the Indian restaurant.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HO CHI MINH \\u2013 CU CHI TINNEL \\u2013 HO CHI MINH   [BREAKFAST + LUNCH + DINNER]\",\"date\":\"01-03-2019 Friday\",\"todo\":\"Breakfast at hotel. 8:30.\\nAfter breakfast transfer to Enjoy visit the famous Cu Chi Tunnels, an incredible underground tunnel network constructed by Vietnamese resistance fighters during the long struggle for independence. Lunch at the Indian restaurant. Free for shopping. Dinner at the Indian restaurant.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HO CHI MINH \\u2013 PHNOMPENH BY BUS  [BREAKFAST + DINNER]\",\"date\":\"02-03-2019 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"After breakfast, transfer to the bus station for bus to Phnompenh depart at 8:00am Upon arrival in Phnom Penh bus, you will welcome by our driver and then transfer you to hotel for check in. Dinner at the Indian restaurant. Overnight at Phnom Penh.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"PHNOM PENH   [BREAKFAST + LUNCH + DINNER]\",\"date\":\"03-03-2019 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"Breakfast at hotel. This morning we explore the stunning Royal Palace complex, home to the Cambodian royal family and a symbol of the nation. We begin amid the beautiful royal gardens, landscaped with tropical plants and studded with gleaming spires. We enter the Throne Hall where the royal receptions are held and the Cambodian king\'s coronation took place. We then pass the Napoleon III Pavilion made from iron, a gift from the French emperor in the 19th century. We continue to the Silver Pagoda, named after the 5000 silver tiles covering the floor, each weighing 1kg. Inside are some of the country\'s most cherished treasures, including a life-size gold Buddha studded with 9584 diamonds, the largest weighing 25 carats. There is also a delicate emerald Buddha made of baccarat crystal, which gives the temple its Khmer name of Wat Preah Keo (Temple of the Emerald Buddha).  We leave the Royal Palace and continue to the nearby National Museum, home to the world\'s finest collection of sculpture from the Angkor period. The exquisite building was completed between 1917 and 1920 and features a lush courtyard garden surrounded by collections from the pre-Angkor, Angkor and post-Angkor periods. We concentrate on the incredible sandstone sculpture from Angkor, as well as the intricate bronzes.  We come face to face with the horrific crimes of the Khmer Rouge. Tuol Sleng was a former high school that the Khmer Rouge turned into a centre for interrogation, torture and death.  Today it is a museum of torture and serves to remind visitors of the terrible atrocities that came to pass in Cambodia. 17,000 people passed through the gates of this prison and only seven lived to tell the tale.  \\n\\nWe travel to the Russian Market, one of the premier shopping destinations in the Cambodian capital. Known as Psar Tuol Tom Pong, it earned its nickname in the 1980s, when Russians were the only tourists in Cambodia. A rambling place, it is bursting with bargains, including handicrafts, carvings, silk and textiles, clothing and footwear, and lots of pirated software, CDs and DVDs, not forgetting enough motorcycle parts to assemble a homemade moped.  We then make for Wat Phnom, a symbol of the city. Located on one of the few hills in this pancake-flat capital, the first pagoda was originally built in 1373 to house Buddha statues discovered in the Mekong by a woman named Penh. This gives us the modern name of the city, Phnom Penh or Hill of Penh. Cambodians come to the shrine to pray for luck in love and life, employment and exams, so there it is always a bustling place.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"PHNOM PENH \\u2013 SIEM REAP  [BREAKFAST + LUNCH + DINNER]\",\"date\":\"04-03-2019 Monday\",\"todo\":\"Breakfast at hotel. Transfer by private car from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap. Arrival Siem Reap and transfer to hotel for check-in. We travel out to the mighty Tonle Sap Lake to visit the floating village of Chong Kneas. Nestled under the hill of Phnom Krom, this floating community moves location with the waters of the lake. During the wet season when the lake swells to five times its size, the village is near Phnom Krom, but during the dry season, it moves as much as 4km from the hill. Everything floats on water in this living fishing community. There are floating schools, floating shops, floating petrol stations, even floating karaoke bars. Many of the houses are floating fish farms with large pens of fish underneath. For those that are interested, we can also make a stop at the Gecko Environment Centre to learn more about lake, which is like the heartbeat of Cambodia, providing sustenance to millions of Khmers. Overnight in Siem Reap.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":9,\"index\":8,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SIEM REAP   [BREAKFAST + LUNCH + DINNER]\",\"date\":\"05-03-2019 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"Breakfast at hotel We travel to Ta Prohm which has been abandoned to the elements, a reminder that while empires rise and fall, the riotous power of nature marches on, oblivious to the dramas of human history. Left as it was \\u2018discovered\\u2019 by French explorer Henri Mouhout in 1860, the tentacle-like tree roots here are slowly strangling the surviving stones, man first conquering nature to create, nature later conquering man to destroy.  After soaking up the unique atmosphere of Ta Prohm, we continue to the giant pyramid of Takeo, one of the highest temples in the Angkor area. Built at the end of the 10th century, it was never completed. Some scholars contend this was due to an inauspicious lightning strike during construction. Others have suggested the high quality sandstone was simply too hard to carve in detail.  \\nWe journey out to the Mother of all temples, Angkor Wat. Believed to be the world\'s largest religious building, this temple is the perfect fusion of symbolism and symmetry and a source of pride and strength to all Khmers. \\n\\nBuilt in the 12th century by King Suryavarman II, this is most famous temple at Angkor. We stay at Angkor Wat to enjoy a picnic breakfast. As the crowds return to their hotels, we venture into Angkor Wat to enjoy its magnificence in peace and quiet. We begin by unraveling the mysteries of the bas-reliefs that tell of tales from Hindu mythology and of the glories of the Khmer empire. Stretching for almost one kilometre, these intricate carvings are a candidate for the world\\u2019s longest unbroken piece of art. Following in the footsteps of the devout and the destructive before us, we then continue to the upper levels of the inner sanctuary. The final steps to the upper terrace of Angkor are the steepest of all, as pilgrims of old were to stoop on their pilgrimage to encounter the Gods. Finally the pinnacle, the sacred heart of Angkor Wat, a blend of spirituality and symmetry so perfect that few moments will measure up. In the afternoon, we visit the immense walled city Angkor Thom that was the masterpiece of King Jayavarman VII. Following the occupation of Angkor by the Chams from 1177 to 1181, the new king decided to build an impregnable fortress at the heart of his empire. The scale is simply staggering and we are immediately overwhelmed by the audacity of Jayavarman on arrival at the city\\u2019s gates. The causeway is lined by an intricate bridge depicting the Churning of the Ocean of Milk from Hindu mythology in which the devas (gods) and asuras (devils) play tug of war with a naga (seven-headed serpent) to obtain the elixir of immortality.  We begin our visit at the Terrace of the Leper King. This intricately carved platform was the royal crematorium and the statue that was originally thought to be the leper king is now believed to be Yama, the god of death. We continue along the Terrace of Elephants, originally used as a viewing gallery for the king to preside over parades, performances and traditional sports. At the southern end lies the Baphuon, once of the most beautiful temples at Angkor, dating from the reign of Uditayavarman 1 in the 11th century. It has undergone a massive renovation by the French and is now once again open for viewing. Our climax is the enigmatic and enchanting temple of the Bayon. At the exact centre of Angkor Thom, this is an eccentric expression of the creative genius and inflated ego of Cambodia\\u2019s most celebrated king. Its 54 towers are each topped off with the four faces of Avalokiteshvara (Buddha of Compassion), which bear more than a \\npassing resemblance to the king himself. These colossal heads stare down from every side, exuding power and control with a hint of compassion, just the mix required to keep a hold on such a vast empire. Before clambering upwards, we unravel the mysteries of the bas-reliefs, with their intricate scenes of ancient battles against the Chams and their snapshot of daily life during the Angkor period. Overnight at Siem Reap.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":10,\"index\":9,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DEPARTURE FROM SIEM REAP  [BREAKFAST]\",\"date\":\"06-03-2019 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"Breakfast at hotel.  \\nFree leisure until driver pick up and then you will transfer to airport for your next destination flight.\"}]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '<ul><li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li><li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li><li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li><li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li><li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li><li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li><li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li><li>For more details click <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\">here</a></li></ul>', '[]', '<ul><li>2 Nights accommodation&nbsp; in Hanoi at 4* Hotel.</li><li>3 Nights accommodation&nbsp; in Ho Chi Minh City at 4* Hotel.</li><li>2 Nights accommodation&nbsp; in Phnom Penh at 4* Hotel.</li><li>2 Nights accommodation&nbsp; in Siem Reap at 4* Hotel.</li><li>Daily meal as per itinerary.</li><li>All tour and transfers as per above itinerary by AC Coach.</li><li>Vietnam &amp; Cambodia visa fee.</li><li>Travel insurance for duration of the tour.</li><li>Service of Tour manager Ex-<strong> Kolkata.</strong></li><li>All applicable taxes.</li></ul><p><b>Please note:-</b></p><ul><li>No any services on hold the same will be subjected to availability at the time of booking.</li><li>Tour is subjected to depart with minimum 25 full paying person.</li><li>Sequence of itinerary may change how ever inclusions will remain same.</li></ul>', '<ul><li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li><li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li><li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li><li><strong>5% GST.</strong></li></ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":null,\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":0},\"cost_price\":0}', 'MZQ/056/0122018', 133000, 133000, 0, '2018-12-29 13:02:59', '2018-12-29 13:02:59', 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0),
(60, 'IHAT, Lucknow', 'Mr Biswajit Das', '7544006056', 'biswajit.das@ihat.in', 'GANGTOK', '2019-02-14', 4, 0, 30, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"BAGDOGRA AIRPORT - GANGTOK (130 Kms \\/ 4.5 Hrs)\",\"date\":\"09-02-2019 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"On arrival at Bagdogra Airport, (IXB) (413 Ft \\/ 126 Mts) you will be met by our office Executive who will assist you to board your vehicle to Gangtok\\n(5412 Ft \\/ 1650 Mts,). \\nOver night at Hotel. [Dinner]\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"GANGTOK\",\"date\":\"10-02-2019 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"Full day conference.\\nNo Vehicle Services.\\nOver night at Hotel. [ Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner ]\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"GANGTOK\",\"date\":\"11-02-2019 Monday\",\"todo\":\"Half day conference and in Evening Gala Dinner.\\nNo Vehicle Services.\\nOver night at Hotel. [ Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner ]\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"GANGTOK \\u2013 TSHANGU LAKE AND BABA MANDIR EXCURSION\",\"date\":\"12-02-2019 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"After breakfast, in the morning, start for excursion to Tshangu Lake (12400 Ft \\/ 3780 Mts \\/ 43 Kms in 03 Hrs one way from Gangtok) & Baba Mandir (13100 Ft \\/ 3994 Mts \\/ 16 Kms in 01 Hrs one way from Tshangu Lake. Situated at a height of 12400 Ft \\/ 3780 Mts \\/ 43 Kms in 03 Hrs one way, with an average depth of 50 ft. The cool water of the Lake is perfectly attuned with the scenic beauty around. Back to Gangtok.\\nOver night at Hotel. [ Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner ]\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"GANGTOK - BAGDOGRA AIRPORT (130 Kms \\/ 4.5 Hrs)\",\"date\":\"13-02-2019 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"After Breakfast transfer to Bagdogra Airport  (IXB) (413 Ft \\/ 126 Mts, ) for your onward journey.\\n[ Breakfast ]\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Lucknow (LKO)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"634\",\"dep_date\":\"14 Feb 2019\",\"arv_date\":\"14 Feb 2019\",\"dep_time\":\"08:30 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"10:20 AM\",\"fare\":\"197099\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Bagdogra (IXB)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"433\",\"dep_date\":\"14 Feb 2019\",\"arv_date\":\"14 Feb 2019\",\"dep_time\":\"01:50 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"03:00 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Bagdogra (IXB)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"6132\",\"dep_date\":\"18 Feb 2019\",\"arv_date\":\"18 Feb 2019\",\"dep_time\":\"02:55 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"04:00 PM\",\"fare\":\"238465\"},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Lucknow (LKO)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"856\",\"dep_date\":\"18 Feb 2019\",\"arv_date\":\"18 Feb 2019\",\"dep_time\":\"06:35 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"08:25 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"14\\/02\\/2019\",\"city\":\"GANGTOK\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL LEMON TREE\",\"room_type\":\"SUPERIOR ROOM\",\"rooms\":15,\"meal\":\"ap\",\"nights\":4,\"check_out\":\"18\\/01\\/2019\"}]', '<ul><li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li><li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li><li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li><li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li><li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li><li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li><li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li><li>For more details click <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\">here</a></li></ul>', '[]', '<ul><li>Return Airfare to Bagdogra&nbsp;<b>Ex- Lucknow.</b></li><li>Accomodation on Twin Sharing&nbsp;<b>(15 Double Rooms).</b></li><li>Meet &amp; Greet upon arrival at Airport.</li><li>Welcome drink on arrival (nonalcoholic)</li><li>Accommodation in Superior/Deluxe&nbsp;rooms</li><li>Complimentary standard Wi-Fi in Bedrooms</li><li>Buffet Breakfast, Lunch &amp; Dinner at a Coffee Shop.</li><li>Conference Hall with amenities including Flipchart /Whiteboard, writing pads, pens, candies &amp; water.</li><li>02 bottles of packaged drinking water in the room.</li><li>Tea/ Coffee makers in the room.</li><li>Free Use of recreational facilities.</li><li>All Transfer &amp; Sightseeing by&nbsp;<b>AC Luxury Vehicle (Innova/Xylo/Similar)</b></li><li>All applicable Transfers &amp; Sightseeing by Specified vehicle which will&nbsp;<u>not be at disposal and will be exclusively used for the guest as per the itinerary only (on point to point basis). This vehicle will also change sector wise.</u></li><li>Meal Plan as per the Itinerary<b>.</b></li></ul>', '<ul><li>Cost for supplementary service, optional Tours, Up-gradation Charges, Guide, Sightseeing entrance fees.</li><li>Cost for Airfare, Train fare, Insurance Premiums, Rafting Charges.</li><li>Cost for service provided on a personal request.</li><li>Cost for personal expenses such as laundry, bottled water, soft drinks, incidentals, porter charges, tips etc.</li><li>Difference in cost arising due to extra usage of vehicle, other than scheduled &amp; mentioned in the itinerary.</li><li>Difference in cost arising due to mishaps, political unrest, natural calamities like - landslides, road blockage, etc. In such case extra will have to be paid on the spot by the guest directly.</li><li><b>5% GST.</b></li></ul><p><b><u>SUPPLEMENT / ADDITIONAL CHARGES:</u></b></p><ul><li>The supplement cost for&nbsp;<i><u>01 English &amp; Hindi speaking Trip leader</u></i>&nbsp;will&nbsp;<u>be</u><b>&nbsp;<i>INR 2000.00 + 05%GST&nbsp;</i></b>per day.</li><li><i><u>Sightseeing Entry Fee</u></i>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<b><i>INR 350.00 + 05%GST</i></b>&nbsp;per pax (Can be included incase guest is opted for Service of Trip Leader only)</li><li><b><i><u>Nathula Pass visit is an optional</u></i></b><i><u>&nbsp;tour</u></i>&nbsp;for which there will be a supplement cost of&nbsp;<b><i>INR 4500.00 + 05% GST</i></b>&nbsp;per vehicle including permit charges. Please note that Nathula Pass visit&nbsp;<u>(subjected to permit availability)</u>. For more details kindly refer the detailed itinerary given below.</li><li>Additional Breakfast: <b>Rs 500 AI</b></li><li>&nbsp;Additional Lunch/Dinner: <strong>Rs&nbsp;</strong><b>1000 AI</b></li><li>Hi Tea:<b> INR 350 AI</b> (1 veg , 1 non veg, 2 Dessert and Tea/Coffee with cookies)</li><li><b><u>Cocktail Snacks:</u></b>&nbsp;2 Veg &amp; 2 Non Veg snacks(excluding mutton preparation) @ <b>Rs. 450 AI</b>&nbsp;per person (for maximum 90 minutes.)</li><li>DJ Charges: <strong>INR 20000 AI</strong> including all charges.</li><li>Projector Charged: <strong>Rs 350 AI</strong></li><li>Cordless mike: <strong>Rs 750 AI</strong> each</li><li>Collar Mike : <strong>Rs 900</strong> each&nbsp;</li><li>Regional dance performance Charges: <strong>INR 25000 AI</strong> including all charges.</li></ul><p><strong>NOTE:</strong></p><ul><li>Music allowed till 10 pm only.</li><li>Food and liquor will be served till 10:30 pm only.</li></ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"15\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":435564,\"transport_cost\":\"56175\",\"land_cost\":\"450000\"},\"cost_price\":941739,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 141260.85\",\"selling_price\":1082999.8500000000931322574615478515625}', 'MZQ/057/0122018', 930000, 31000, 0, '2018-12-31 10:48:01', '2019-01-19 12:02:09', 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0),
(61, 'IHAT, Lucknow', 'Mr Biswajit Das', '7544006056', 'biswajit.das@ihat.in', 'SHILLONG', '2019-02-09', 4, 0, 30, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"GUWAHATI AIRPORT - SHILLONG (98 KMS \\/ 2.5 HRS)\",\"date\":\"09-02-2019 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"On arrival at Guwahati Airport,  you will be met by our office Executive who will assist you to board your vehicle to Shillong. \\nOver night at Hotel. [ Dinner ]\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SHILLONG\",\"date\":\"10-02-2019 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"Full day conference.\\nNo Vehicle Services.\\nOver night at Hotel. [ Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner ]\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SHILLONG\",\"date\":\"11-02-2019 Monday\",\"todo\":\"Half day conference and in Evening Gala Dinner.\\nNo Vehicle Services.\\nOver night at Hotel. [ Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner ]\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SHILLONG - CHERRAPUNJEE - SHILLONG (60 KMS \\/ 2.5 HRS )\",\"date\":\"12-02-2019 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"After morning breakfast Visit Nohkalikai falls, Seven sister falls, Eco park, Mawsmai cave, Arwah cave(15 minutes of trekking to the main spot), Dainthellen falls etc. On the way visit Elephant falls, Shillong peak and Mawkdowk view point where you can go for Zip lining.\\nOvernight at Shillong. [ Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner ]\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DEPARTURE FROM SHILLONG\",\"date\":\"13-02-2019 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"After Breakfast transfer to Guwahati Airport for your onward journey. [ Breakfast ]\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Lucknow (LKO)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"244\",\"dep_date\":\"09 Feb 2019\",\"arv_date\":\"09 Feb 2019\",\"dep_time\":\"12:20 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"02:00 PM\",\"fare\":null},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Guwahati(gauhati) (GAU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"292\",\"dep_date\":\"09 Feb 2019\",\"arv_date\":\"09 Feb 2019\",\"dep_time\":\"04:10 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"05:25 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Guwahati(gauhati) (GAU)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"394\",\"dep_date\":\"13 Feb 2019\",\"arv_date\":\"13 Feb 2019\",\"dep_time\":\"12:25 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:45 PM\",\"fare\":null},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Lucknow (LKO)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"856\",\"dep_date\":\"13 Feb 2019\",\"arv_date\":\"13 Feb 2019\",\"dep_time\":\"06:35 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"08:25 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"09\\/02\\/2019\",\"city\":\"SHILLONG\",\"hotel_name\":\"THE HERITAGE CLUB TRIPURA CASTLE\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE  ROOM\",\"rooms\":15,\"meal\":\"ap\",\"nights\":4,\"check_out\":\"13\\/02\\/2019\"}]', '<ul><li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li><li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li><li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li><li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li><li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li><li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li><li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li><li>For more details click <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\">here</a></li></ul>', '[]', '<ul><li>Return Airfare&nbsp;<strong>Ex- Lucknow.</strong></li><li>05 AC Innova/Xylo/Similar vehicle as per the Itinerary&nbsp;<b>(AC will not operate in Hills)</b>.</li><li>Accommodation on 15 Double sharing room for 04 nights</li><li>Meal plan APAI <strong>(As per the Itinerary)</strong>.</li><li>Daily one litre of mineral water</li><li>All parking and road tolls&nbsp;</li></ul>', '<ul><li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li><li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li><li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li><li><strong>5% GST.</strong></li></ul><p><b><u>ADDITIONAL CHARGES</u></b></p><ul><li>Conference hall available for maximum 30 pax seating capacity for 01 ½ day complimentary.</li><li>LCD projector with PA system&nbsp;<strong>@10000&nbsp;+ GST (18%)</strong> per day</li><li>Local dance (Khasi,Garo &amp; Jaintia Tribes) for 30 Minutes&nbsp;<strong>@36000&nbsp;+ GST (18%)</strong></li><li>Hall charge for musical event&nbsp;<strong>@16000&nbsp;+ GST (18%)</strong></li><li>Bonfire not available</li><li>Cocktail starter available&nbsp;<strong>@599&nbsp;+ GST (5%) </strong>per person for 2 hours service</li><li>Corkage charge&nbsp;@<strong>1000&nbsp;+ GST (18%)</strong> per bottle.</li></ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"10\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":0,\"land_cost\":\"55000\",\"hotel_cost\":\"600480\"},\"cost_price\":655480,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 65548\",\"selling_price\":721028}', 'MZQ/058/0122018', 1005000, 33500, 0, '2018-12-31 10:48:31', '2018-12-31 12:14:41', 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0),
(62, 'MR GAURAV BARNWAL', NULL, '9832245020', 'gauravburnwal.gb@gmail.com', 'SHIMLA & MANALI', '2019-01-22', 6, 0, 4, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DELHI - SHIMLA (361 KMS \\/ 08 HRS)\",\"date\":\"22-01-2019 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"Arrive Delhi Airport and depart for Shimla by road. Shimla the state capital of Himachal Pradesh is surrounded by pine deodar, oak and rhododendron forests. Shimla was also the summer capital of the British Raj. Arrive Shimla and check into your hotel.\\nAs the day falls, you may return to your hotel overnight stay. (DINNER)\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SHIMLA LOCAL SIGHTSEEING\",\"date\":\"23-01-2019 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"Morning post breakfast enjoy an excursion to Kufri & later visit Naldehra & Walk through the Mall Road. \\nOvernight at Hotel.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SHIMLA - MANALI (250 KMS \\/ 09 HRS)\",\"date\":\"24-01-2019 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"After early breakfast get transferred to Manali. \\nOvernight at Hotel\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"MANALI LOCAL SIGHTSEEING\",\"date\":\"25-01-2019 Friday\",\"todo\":\"This morning visit Hadimba Temple, Vashisth Kund, Manu Mandir, Arjun Gufa and Tibetan Monastery & Handicraft Centre. Rest of the day is at leisure. \\nOvernight at Hotel.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"MANALI LOCAL SIGHTSEEING\",\"date\":\"26-01-2019 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"Post Breakfast visit Solang Valley. Overnight at Hotel OR Optionally visit Rohtang Pass (On Own).\\nOvernight at Hotel.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"MANALI - CHANDIGARH ((310 KMS \\/ 08 HRS)\",\"date\":\"27-01-2019 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"After breakfast, depart for Chandigarh enroute visit Kullu Valley & Sukhna Lake. \\nOvernight at Hotel.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"CHANDIGARH - DELHI  (259 KMS \\/ 05 HRS)\",\"date\":\"28-01-2019 Monday\",\"todo\":\"Visit Rock Garden & get transferred to Delhi Airport for onward journey.\"}]', '[]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"22\\/01\\/2019\",\"city\":\"SHIMLA\",\"hotel_name\":\"MARIGOLD SAROVAR PORTICO\",\"room_type\":\"SUPERIOR ROOM\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"24\\/01\\/2019\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"24\\/01\\/2019\",\"city\":\"MANALI\",\"hotel_name\":\"THE MANALI INN\",\"room_type\":\"SUPERIOR ROOM\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"27\\/01\\/2019\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"27\\/01\\/2019\",\"city\":\"CHANDIGARH\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"28\\/01\\/2019\",\"rooms\":2}]', '<ul><li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li><li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li><li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li><li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li><li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li><li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li><li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li><li>For more details click <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\">here</a></li></ul>', '[]', NULL, '<ul><li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li><li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li><li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li><li><strong>5% GST.</strong></li></ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":null,\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":0},\"cost_price\":0}', 'MZQ/059/012019', 0, NULL, 0, '2019-01-08 16:23:00', '2019-01-08 16:23:00', 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0),
(63, 'MR MANOJ KUMAR BARNWAL', NULL, '9835334563', 'baranwalmk@gmail.com', 'CHARDHAM YATRA', '2019-06-03', 9, 0, 12, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HARIDWAR - BARKOT (180 KMS \\/ 08 HRS)\",\"date\":\"03-06-2019 Monday\",\"todo\":\"Arrival to Haridwar pickup from Airport \\/ Railway Station proceeds to Barkot. On the way visit Kempty Fall near Mussoorie (By Pass Only). Evening arrival to Barkot check in to Hotel \\/ Camp.\\nAfter dinner overnight stay at hotel.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"BARKOT - JANKI CHATTI - YAMUNOTRI - BARKOT  (40 KMS DRIVE \\/ 06 KMS TREKKING \\/ 09 HRS)\",\"date\":\"04-06-2019 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"Today early morning starts from Barkot to Janki Chatti to visit Yamunotri Temple (Breakfast Packed). On arrival to Janki Chatti the base point of Ymunotri, booked Pony & Palki from here. If you are fit enough you can do trekking also, quite a stiff trek. Arrival to Yamunotri visit the holy temple of Goddess Yamunotri (3120m), present temple was built by Maharani of Jaipur Gularia Devi in 19th century. Natural hot water springs around the temple are main attraction for pilgrims. After the pooja \\/ darshan return journey to Barkot.\\novernight stay at hotel.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"BARKOT - UTTARKASHI (100 KMS \\/ 05 HRS)\",\"date\":\"05-06-2019 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"Today after breakfast checkout from hotel proceed to Uttarkashi, on the way visit Prakateshwar - Mahadev temple near Brhamkhal. On arrival to Uttarkashi (1158m) check in to hotel, in evening visit Kashi -Vishwanath Temple.\\nOvernight stay in Uttarkashi.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"UTTARKASHI - GANGOTRI - HARSIL - UTTARKASHI (200 KMS \\/ 11 HRS)\",\"date\":\"06-06-2019 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"Early Morning 5: am proceed to visit Gangotri Temple. Along with Bhagirathi River the journey of Gangotri becomes a wonderful journey. Beautiful valleys, small rivers, waterfalls local villages, worth to visit over here.  On arrival to Gangotri Temple (3050m) visit the holy temple of Goddess Ganga, pooja \\/ darshan.  The present temple of Gangotri was built in 18th century by Gurkha commander Amar Singh Thapa. After the visit comeback to Uttarkashi overnight stay in Uttarkashi.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"UTTARKASHI - GUPTKASHI - SITAPUR (250 KMS \\/ 09 HRS)\",\"date\":\"07-06-2019 Friday\",\"todo\":\"Today after early morning breakfast check out from hotel and proceed to Sitapur. Evening arrival to Sitapur transfer to hotel, \\nafter dinner overnight stay in Sitapur.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SITAPUR - KEDARNATH - SITAPUR (12 KMS DRIVE \\/ 16 KMS TREKKING \\/ 12 HRS)\",\"date\":\"08-06-2019 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"Early morning 4 am procced to Sonprayag the reservation counter for booking Pony & Palki for Kedarnath journey, next 5 Kms drive  by local taxi to Gaurikund, Kedarnath trek starts from here (Pony & Palki services available from here only), best to do it otherwise trekking is not possible in same day. A very hard trekking rout for reaching up to Kedarnath temple. On arrival to Kedarnath (3585m) visit the ancient holy temple of Lord Shiva amongst the 12th Jyotirlings of Lord Shiva 11th is situated over here. After the pooja \\/ darshan return journey to Sitapur \\novernight stay in Sitapur .\\n\\nFor Helicopter Visit:\\nEarly morning 5: am drive to helipad to board the helicopter for Kedarnath. On arrival to Kedarnath helipad,walk able distance about 500m reaching up to Kedarnath temple (3585m). Visit over hrere \\/ Pooja \\/ Abhishek \\/ Darshan. After the visit over return journey by helicopter to Sitapur \\/ Guptkashi helipad, pickup & transfer to hotel overnight stay.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SITAPUR - BADRINATH (250 KMS \\/ 09 HRS)\",\"date\":\"09-06-2019 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"Today after early morning breakfast proceed to Badrinath, en route visit Narsingh Swami Temple at Josimath.  In evening arrival to Badrinath (3400m), transfer to hotel next visit Badrinath Temple for evening Arati \\/ Darshan. After the visit over come back to hotel.\\nOvernight stay in Badrinath.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"BADRINATH - JOSHIMATH - PIPALKOTI (85 KMS \\/ 04 HRS)\",\"date\":\"10-06-2019 Monday\",\"todo\":\"Early morning 4 am today visit Badrinath Temple for Abhishek\\/ Alankar darshan.  The present holy temple of Badrinarayana was built by Adi Guru Shankaracharya during 7th century. The main idol of Lord Vishnu is built of black stone known as \\u201cSalegram\\u201d. Before the visit of Badrinarayan temple one must take a holy dip inside \\u201cTaptkunda\\u201d a natural hot water spring situated outside the temple.  After the darshan of temple also perform the pooja\\/tarpan outside the temple near Brhamkapal.  After lunch checkout from hotel drive to Mana the last village of India on Tibet-Border visit over here. Later on proceed to Pipalkoti on the way visit Shankaracharaya Math at Joshimath.  In evening arrival to Pipalkoti (1260m).\\nOvernight stay in hotel in Pipalkoti.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":9,\"index\":8,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"JOSHIMATH - PIPALKOTI - HARIDWAR (250 KMS \\/ 09 HRS)\",\"date\":\"11-06-2019 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"Today morning after breakfast proceed to Haridwar, Evening arrival to Haridwar check in to hotel, later on visit Har ki Pauri for Ganga Aarti \\/ Darshan. Comeback to hotel dinner overnight stay in Haridwar.\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":10,\"index\":9,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DEPARTURE FROM HARIDWAR\",\"date\":\"12-06-2019 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"After breakfast checks out from hotel and drop to Airport \\/ Railway station. \\nJourney concludes with everlasting memories of Chardham\\u2026.!!!!\"}]', '[]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"03\\/06\\/2019\",\"city\":\"BARKOT\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL ADITYA PALACE \\/ SIMILAR\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE ROOM\",\"rooms\":6,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"05\\/06\\/2019\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"05\\/06\\/2019\",\"city\":\"UTTARKASHI\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL GANGAPUTRA \\/ SIMILAR\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE ROOM\",\"rooms\":6,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"07\\/06\\/2019\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"07\\/06\\/2019\",\"city\":\"SITAPUR\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL JPG PALACE \\/ SIMILAR\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE ROOM\",\"rooms\":6,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"09\\/06\\/2019\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"09\\/06\\/2019\",\"city\":\"BADRINATH\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL NANDADEVI \\/ SIMILAR\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE ROOM\",\"rooms\":6,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"10\\/06\\/2019\"},{\"id\":4,\"check_in\":\"10\\/06\\/2019\",\"city\":\"PIPALKOTI\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL ALKANANDA \\/ SIMILAR\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE ROOM\",\"rooms\":6,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"11\\/06\\/2019\"},{\"id\":5,\"check_in\":\"11\\/06\\/2019\",\"city\":\"HARIDWAR\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL KHANNA PALACE\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE ROOM\",\"rooms\":6,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"12\\/06\\/2019\"}]', '<ul><li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li><li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li><li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li><li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li><li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li><li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li><li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li><li>For more details click <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\">here</a></li></ul>', '[]', '<ul><li>Accommodation as mention above</li><li>Meal Plan as mentioned above</li><li>A/C Vehicle, Tempo Traveler 12 / Seated</li><li>State Tax, Toll Tax, Driver DA, Parking</li><li>All sightseeing &amp; transfers as per itinerary only</li></ul>', '<ul><li>Air Fare/Train fare</li><li>Auto / Ropeway / Pony / Palki / Helicopter / Rafting / Bungee Jumping &amp; other not mention adventure activities.</li><li>Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips &amp; gratuity, mineral water, soft &amp; hard drinks</li><li>Entrance Fees &amp; Guide charges.</li><li>Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, which is directly payable on the spot).</li><li>Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation &amp; land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure.</li><li>Service Tax.</li><li>Anything which is not included in the inclusion</li><li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li><li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li><li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li><li><strong>5% GST.</strong></li></ul><p><b>Supplementary cost : Pay by Guest Directly</b></p><ul><li>Helicopter Charges For Kedarnath Visit Both Side&nbsp;<b>@ 9500/-Per Pax&nbsp;&nbsp;Approx. Extra</b></li><li>Pony Cost For&nbsp;Yamunotri visit Both Side&nbsp;<b>@ 2000/-Per Pax Approx. Extra</b></li><li>Palki Cost For Yamunotri visit Both Side&nbsp;<b>@ 5000/- Per Pax Approx. Extra</b></li><li>Pony Cost For&nbsp;&nbsp;Kedarnath visit Both Side&nbsp;<b>@ 4000/-Per Pax Approx. Extra</b></li><li>Palki Cost For Kedarnath visit Both Side&nbsp;<b>@ 8000/- Per Pax Approx. Extra</b></li><li>Special Darshan Slip to Kedarnath Temple&nbsp;<b>@ 1500/-Per Pax Approx. Extra</b></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"13\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":0,\"land_cost\":\"238770\"},\"cost_price\":238770,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 31040.1\",\"selling_price\":269810.099999999976716935634613037109375}', 'MZQ/060/012019', 278400, 23200, 0, '2019-01-09 11:34:30', '2019-03-13 17:18:22', 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0);
