(266, 'MR RAMJEE PANDEY', NULL, '9431181496', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'Char Dham Yatra', '2022-05-06', 10, 0, 4, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Haridwar (Arrival)\",\"date\":\"06-05-2022 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Meet our driver at Delhi Airport and proceed to Haridwar Hotel. Check into the hotel after arrival in Haridwar. Evening visit Mansa Devi Temple &amp; Ganga aarti at Har Ki Pauri. Overnight stay at Haridwar.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>An Evening at Ganga Aarti Haridwar:&nbsp;The Ganga Aarti in Hardwar\\u2019s Har-ki-Pauri is one of the famous rituals in India. It starts at around 6.30 pm after sunset, with large crowds gathered around both the banks of a canal that carries the waters of the Ganges. Loudspeakers blare songs in praise of&nbsp;Ganga Maiya&nbsp;and Shiva.&nbsp;The time Aarti sees a bustle of activity on the ghats A pack of diya comes fully equipped and is self-sufficient! It has a wick lamp surrounded by flowers It lasted for around 30 min.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Haridwar - Barkot\",\"date\":\"07-05-2022 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>The morning after breakfast transfer to Barkot via Mussoorie.En route visit Mussoorie Lake &amp; Kempty Fall in Mussoorie. Later drive to Barkot. On arrival, check in at the hotel in Barkot for dinner &amp; overnight stay.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Barkot - Yamunotri - Barkot\",\"date\":\"08-05-2022 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Early morning after breakfast (packed breakfast), drive to Jankichatti \\/ Phoolchatti &amp; trek from here to Yamunotri (6kms) (Either by walk or by horse or by Doli at own cost). After taking bath in Jamunabai Kund\\u2019s warm water and cook rice by packing it in a cloth and dipping it in the hot water of the hot kund. Pilgrims take this cooked rice home as \\\"Prasad\\\". Having Darshan of \\u201cYamunaji\\u201d return to Jankichatti by trek. Overnight stay at Barkot.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Hanuman Chatti:&nbsp;The confluence of Hanuman Ganga &amp; Yamuna River.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Yamunotri Temple:&nbsp;Maharani Gularia of Jaipur built the temple in the 19th Century. It was destroyed twice in the present century and rebuilt again.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Surya Kund:&nbsp;There are a Number of thermal springs in the vicinity of the temple, which flow into numerous pools. The most important of these is Surya Kund.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Divya Shila:&nbsp;A rock pillar, worshipped before entering the Yamunotri Temple.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Yamunotri- Yamunotri is situated in the western region of the Garhwal Himalayas and is at a height of 3,235 meters above sea level. Yamunotri is the source of the river Yamuna. The shrine of Yamunotri is located on the Bandar Poonch peak.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Barkot - Uttarkashi\",\"date\":\"09-05-2022 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning after leisurely breakfast, drive to Uttarkashi. Check into the hotel arrival in Uttarkashi. Evening visit Kashi Vishwanath Temple in Uttarkashi. Overnight stay at Uttarkashi.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Uttarkashi:&nbsp;Situated at the bank of river Bhagirathi. The temple of Lord Vishwanath is located here where a massive iron trident is erected. The other important temples situated here are Ekadash Rudra, Bhairav, Gyaneshwar, and Goddess Kuteti Devi.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Uttarkashi - Gangotri - Uttarkashi\",\"date\":\"10-05-2022 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Early morning (packed breakfast) drive to Gangotri(3048 mts), en-route at Gangnani take a holy dip in Garam Kund, have bath drive to Gangotri via beautiful Harsil Valley. Harsil is famous for its natural beauty and for the majestic views of the Deodar trees and mountains. On arrival at Shree Gangotri, take a holy dip in the sacred river Ganges which is also called Bhagirathi at its origin. Perform Pooja and Darshan, after that relax for some time in the lovely surroundings. Later drive back to Uttarkashi. Overnight stay at Uttarkashi.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Gangotri- Gangotri is the place high in the Garhwal Himalayas from where the holy Ganges originates. According to the legend, it was here the Ganga descended on the earth when Lord Shiva released the mighty river from the locks of his hair. The temple of Gangotri, dedicated to Goddess Ganga stands on the bank of the river.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Uttarkashi \\u2013 Guptkashi\",\"date\":\"11-05-2022 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning after breakfast, drive to Guptkashi via Moolgarh &amp; Lambgoan. Enroute you can see the beautiful river Mandakini at Tilwara. The Mandakini River comes from Kedarnath, drive alongside the river to reach Guptkashi, visit ArdhNarishwar Temple in Guptkashi. Check into the hotel arrival in Guptkashi. Overnight stay at Guptakashi.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guptkashi \\u2013 Shri Kedarnath ji\",\"date\":\"12-05-2022 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning after breakfast drive to Helipad, reach Kedarnath by helicopter,&nbsp;visit Kedarnath ji Temple &amp; perform Pooja. In the evening also&nbsp;visit Adi Shankaracharya Samadhi behind the Temple. Back to Sitapur\\/ Guptkashi by helicopter. Overnight stay at Camp\\/Hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Shri Kedarnath-&nbsp;is a majestic sight, standing in the middle of a wide plateau surrounded by lofty snow Covered peaks. The temple of Kedarnath, located at a height of 3,581 mts, stands at the head of the Mandakini river. The present temple, built in the 8th century by Adi Shankaracharya, stands adjacent to the site of an earlier temple built by the Pandavas. The inner walls of the assembly hall are decorated with figures of various deities and scenes from mythology. Outside the temple door, a large statue of the Nandi Bull stands as guard. It is said that devotees who die here become one with Shiva himself.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guptkashi - Shri Badrinath\",\"date\":\"13-05-2022 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning after breakfast, drive to Shri Badrinath. Check in to the hotel arrival in Shri Badrinath. Pilgrims after having a bath in the Taptkund have the Darshan of&nbsp; Badrivishal &amp; Aarti in the evening. Brahamakapal is significant for Pinddan Shraddh of ancestors (Pitrus). There are other interesting sightseeing spots like Mana, Vyas Gufa, Maatamoorti, Charanpaduka, Bhimkund and the \\u201cMukh\\u201d of the Saraswati River. Just within the three kms of Badrinathjee. Overnight stay at Shri Badrinath.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Shri Badrinath- Shri Badrinath is one of the most important of all the four(Char) Dhams in India. This temple is located between the Nar &amp; Narayan mountain ranges and in the shadow of the Nilkantha peak at the height of 3,133 mts. It is the most popular of Vishnu pilgrimages among the five Badries, also known as Vishal Badri.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Tapt Kund:&nbsp;Natural thermal springs on the bank of the river Alaknanda, where it is customary to bathe before entering the Badrinath temple.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Narad Kund:&nbsp;A recess in the river, near Tapt Kund, forming a pool from where the Badrinath idol was recovered.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Mata Murty Temple:&nbsp;Devoted to the mother of Sri Badrinathji. Other important temples include SeshNetra Temple, Urvashi Temple, and Charanpaduka.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Mana Village:&nbsp;Inhabited by an Indo-Mongolian tribe, it is the last Indian village before Tibet.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Bhim Pul:&nbsp;On the other side of Mana village, a massive rock forming a natural bridge lies<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>over the roaring Saraswati River. It presents a spectacular view of water thundering down through the narrow passage under the rock and is believed to have been placed there by Bhim, the second eldest among the five Pandava brothers.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Vyas Gufa (cave):&nbsp;Near Mana Village, this is a rock cave where Ved Vyas is believed to have composed the Mahabharata and the pauranic commentaries.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":9,\"index\":8,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Shri Badrinath \\u2013Rudraprayag\",\"date\":\"14-05-2022 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning after breakfast, driver for Rudraprayag via Pipalkoti. Visit on the way Narsingh Temple in Joshimath later drive back to Rudraprayag via Joshimath. Check into the hotel arrival in Pipalkoti\\/ Joshimath\\/ Srinagar\\/ Rudraprayag. Overnight stay at Pipalkoti\\/ Joshimath\\/ Srinagar\\/ Rudraprayag.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Rudraprayag:&nbsp;One of the holy prayag of five famous prayag of Uttarakhand. Confluence of River Alaknanda and Mandakini.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Narsingh Temple: This is an ancient temple of Lord Vishnu in Narsingh Avtar and main temple of Joshimath. When Badrinath temple remain closed during winter every year, one idol of Lord Badri is brought to Narsingh temple and worshiped for six months.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":10,\"index\":9,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Rudraprayag - Haridwar\",\"date\":\"15-05-2022 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning after breakfast, drive for Haridwar via Rishikesh.Rishikesh\\u2019place of sages\\u2019 is a celebrated spiritual town on the bank of Ganga and is surrounded by Shivalik range of the Himalayas on three sides. It is said that when Raibhya Rishi did hard penances, God appeared by the name of \\u201d Hrishikesh \\u201d and this area hence firth came to be known as Rishikesh. Later visit RishikeshTemples Sight Seeing \\u2013 LaxmanJhulla, Ram Jhulla. Stay at Haridwar.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":11,\"index\":10,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Haridwar (Departure)\",\"date\":\"16-05-2022 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning, after breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Haridwar Railway Station\\/Airport.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"752\",\"dep_date\":\"06 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"06 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"08:55 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"11:00 AM\",\"fare\":\"18131\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"753\",\"dep_date\":\"16 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"16 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"05:55 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"07:40 PM\",\"fare\":\"15982\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"06\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Haridwar\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel One Earth\",\"check_out\":\"07\\/05\\/2022\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"07\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Barkot\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"09\\/05\\/2022\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Milan\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"09\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Uttarkashi\",\"hotel_name\":\"Geetanjali Resort\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"11\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"11\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Guptkashi\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Kedar Palace\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":2,\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"13\\/05\\/2022\",\"meal\":\"map\"},{\"id\":4,\"check_in\":\"13\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Badrinath\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Laxmi Divine\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"14\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":5,\"check_in\":\"14\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Rudraprayag\",\"hotel_name\":\"Jwalpa Palace\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"15\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":6,\"check_in\":\"15\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Haridwar\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Siya Ram\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"16\\/05\\/2022\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <strong>Ex Ranchi</strong>.</li>\n	<li>Accommodation on Double sharing in a Neat, clean &amp; hygienic Hotels.</li>\n	<li>All Transfers &amp; Sightseeing by <strong>Toyota Innova</strong>.<em>(A.C. will not work on Hills)</em></li>\n	<li>All point-to-point sightseeing as per the given program is possible in the time frame.</li>\n	<li>All toll, tax, parking &amp;&nbsp;driver allowances.</li>\n	<li>Daily <strong>Breakfast and Dinner.</strong></li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Laundry</li>\n	<li>Entrance fees</li>\n	<li>Ropeway, Guide, Porter &amp; Pony</li>\n	<li>Entry Tickets / VIP Darshan Tickets</li>\n	<li>Kedarnath Helicopter Tickets</li>\n	<li>Any up gradation in Airline class or hotel room category</li>\n	<li>Any extra expense such as route change, Date change, Accommodation facilities, etc incurred due to the unforeseen, unavoidable forced Majeure&nbsp;circumstances during the tour.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, '<p>Normal Cancellation Policy:-</p>\n\n<p># &nbsp;Between 30 and 15 days of departure - 50% of tour cost<br />\n# &nbsp;Between 14 days and 7 prior to the date of departure - 75%<br />\n# &nbsp;Between 6 days and In case of no show - 100%</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Cancellation policy in times of Covid 19</p>\n\n<p># In case of Lockdown imposed by the Government or any change in&nbsp; SOP\'s from the government, if a tour gets postponed the amount shall be adjusted in future booking&nbsp;for the same guest, subject to availability. Rates may differ as per the season.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p># In case guests do not wish to travel in the future, then Rs.1500/ + GST shall be charged per person as our service charges.</p>\n\n<p># Refund shall be managed only after receiving&nbsp;from our vendors and concerned&nbsp;hotels. Though we will expedite this process to best of our capability</p>', '{\"profit_percent\":\"14\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":34113,\"land_cost\":\"147000\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":181113,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 25355.82\",\"selling_price\":206468.8200000000069849193096160888671875}', 'MZQ/0262/032022', 207400, 51850, 0, '2022-03-22 12:00:21', '2022-05-04 15:11:54', 1, 1, '\"<p><strong>Supplementary Cost :-&nbsp;Helicopter Ticket<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Ex Phata \\/ Sirsi \\/ Guptkashi Rs.6000\\/ - to Rs.9500\\/ per person Subject to availably at the time of booking<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Heli Tickets for Kedarnath To &amp; Fro. Rates valid up to per person body weight 80 Kg. Above that directly payable at helipad&nbsp;@ Rs.150\\/ per Kg<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Terms &amp; Conditions:-<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\n<p>#&nbsp;50% advance to be deposited at the time of booking confirmation.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>#&nbsp;Balance 50% before 15 days from the&nbsp;Tour&nbsp;Starts.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>#&nbsp;Check In \\/ Checkout time at all the properties would be as per the hotel.<br \\/>\\n#&nbsp;All the above-mentioned rates are per person rates.<br \\/>\\n#&nbsp;Rooms holding shall be for a period of 24 hours only.<br \\/>\\n#&nbsp;The above rates are applicable strictly for resident Indian citizens only.<br \\/>\\n#&nbsp;Any amendment in the booking Rs.500 Per Person is chargeable as communication charges.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>#&nbsp;All disputes are subject to Haridwar Jurisdiction.<\\/p>\"', 0, 0),
(267, 'MRS PRAKRITI FOGLA', 'BNI EXPLORERS', '9075285113', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'NEPAL', '2022-04-08', 5, 1, 2, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu\",\"date\":\"08-04-2022 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Meeting at airport upon arrival by Office Personnel. Transfer to hotel. Kathmandu is the capital of Nepal and the Kathmandu Valley is the political and cultural heart of the Kingdom. The urban sprawl that makes up modern Kathmandu is in fact two cities, Patan and Kathmandu.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu\",\"date\":\"09-04-2022 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>This morning&nbsp;you will be taken&nbsp; for a visit of the Hindu culture in Nepal,&nbsp;Pashupatinath.&nbsp; This is the place where holy saddhus pray.&nbsp;The&nbsp;Pashupatinath Temple&nbsp;is a famous, sacred&nbsp;Hindu temple&nbsp;dedicated to&nbsp;Pashupatinath&nbsp;and is located on the banks of the&nbsp;Bagmati River&nbsp;5 kilometres north-east of&nbsp;Kathmandu Valley&nbsp;in the eastern city of&nbsp;Kathmandu&nbsp;the&nbsp;capital&nbsp;of&nbsp;Nepal. This temple is considered one of the sacred temples of&nbsp;Hindu&nbsp;faith .The temple serves as the seat of the national deity, Lord&nbsp;Pashupatinath. This temple complex is on&nbsp;UNESCO World Heritage Sites\'s list Since 1979.&nbsp;This \\\"extensive Hindu temple precinct\\\" is a \\\"sprawling collection of temples, ashrams, images and inscriptions raised over the centuries along the banks of the sacred Bagmati river\\\".&nbsp;We then continue to the holiest shrine for the Buddhist culture in Nepal,&nbsp;Bouddhanath, with its large stupa, this is the place where all devout Buddhists come for a pilgrimage. After completion of these two spots, you will be taken&nbsp;take you for a visit to&nbsp;Patan.&nbsp;Also known as&nbsp;&nbsp;Lalitpur&nbsp; , the city of beauty is separated from Kathmandu only by the Bagmati River and is the second largest town in the valley. Lalitpur is fragmented from other cities due to its substantive architectural ancient masterpieces. Patan\'s central Durbar Square is absolutely packed with temples: Its an architectural center point with a far greater concentration of temples per sq. meter than in Kathamandu or Bhaktapur.&nbsp;Within&nbsp; the city also lies the Tibetan refugee center, home to most of the valley\'s Tibetan population.&nbsp; While technically refugees, the Tibetans are some of the wealthiest people in the valley because of the carpet industry they operate.&nbsp; For those looking to bring home a fine Tibetan carpet, this is the place to shop. You will then go to&nbsp;Swayambhunath&nbsp;the golden spire of the 5th-century Swayambhu stupa is adorned with a colorful fluttering of prayer flags; it crowns a hill overlooking the Kathmandu Valley and offers fantastic views over the city of Kathmandu. Swayambhunath is one of the most recognizable symbols in Nepal and the painted eyes of Buddha watch all who ascend the worn stone steps.&nbsp;( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 06 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu - Pokhara\",\"date\":\"10-04-2022 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Drive to Pokhara. Pokhara is 210 kms from Kathmandu and is a 7 hours drive approx. From Pokhara town (2,352 feet) in good weather there are splendid views right from the hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>On the way you have an option at an extra cost of doing the river rafting ( Inr. 2000 per person if required ) or visit the Manakamna Temple \\u201c Goddess of Fulfilling Wishes\\u201d where you are taken by a cable ride of 10 mins ( Inr. 500 per person for the cable car tickets if required ). Overnight at hotel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pokhara\",\"date\":\"11-04-2022 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>This morning you will go for a excursion trip to&nbsp;Sarangkot.&nbsp;Sarangkot is the most popular tourist destination from where the tourist can enjoy the great view of the Pokhara Valley and the magnificent view of the mountains. Sarangkot is only 13 kms from Lake Side, Pokhara. Sarangkot is the highest view point for a sunrise and it is just 1592m high. Sarangkot is&nbsp; cooler than Pokhara. Sarangkot can be reached easily by 45 to 60&nbsp;minutes by a car ride to the top from Pokhara. Many tourists come to Sarangkot for sunrise view and go back.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>From Sarangkot, on the northern direction we can see Dhaulagiri in the far west. Annapurna range is visible when the weather is clear on the same side. On the southern direction the village overlooks the city of Pokhara and its lake on the north-western outskirts of the city. ( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 03 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>This afternoon you will visit&nbsp;Bindebasini Temple. This is one of the oldest temples in Pokhara was a part of Kaski Kingdom, the main deity of the temple,Goddess Durga, was brought from India . Apart from the peace and tranquility that can be felt in this region, the premises of the temple offers a good view of the Himalaya on a clear day. The temple is in the area of the bazaar, hence,a journey of the old bazaar can be combined with a visit to the temple. Sightseeing to&nbsp;Devi\\u2019s fall, also known as Patale Chango is an awesome waterfall lying 2 km southwest of Pokhara. During summer and rainy season, the waterfall takes its real form, with gushing water splashing and making its way through the rocks. Just opposite of Devi\\u2019s fall, on the other side of the road, there is&nbsp;Gupteshwor Cave. This cave is popular for the different natural forms made from limestone deposits. Photography is strictly prohibited inside the cave. Overnight at hotel.&nbsp;( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 03 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\\n\\n<h1>&nbsp;<\\/h1>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pokhara - Kathmandu\",\"date\":\"12-04-2022 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Drive back to Kathmandu retracing the same path &amp; transfer to hotel. Rest day at leisure.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>One can indulge in shopping or visit the casinos trying their lady luck on your own. Overnight at hotel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu - Airport\",\"date\":\"13-04-2022 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning will be comparatively free and closer to the time of your flight, you will be transferred to the airport in time to board your flight for onward journey.<\\/p>\"}]', '[]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"08\\/04\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Kathmandu\",\"hotel_name\":\"ON OWN\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"10\\/04\\/2022\",\"room_type\":\"ON OWN\",\"rooms\":1},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"10\\/04\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Pokhara\",\"hotel_name\":\"5* Hotel Pokhara Grande\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"12\\/04\\/2022\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE ROOM + 01 EXTRA BED\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"12\\/04\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Kathmandu\",\"hotel_name\":\"ON OWN\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"13\\/04\\/2022\",\"room_type\":\"ON OWN\",\"rooms\":1}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":11}]', '<p># 02 nights accommodation in Pokhara with Breakfast</p>\n\n<p># 02 international airport transfers by an A/c vehicle</p>\n\n<p># Sightseeing as per the itinerary in Kathmandu and Pokhara by&nbsp;an A/c vehicle exclusively</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;( Guide and entrance fee not included payable directly )</p>\n\n<p># Transportation Kathmandu / Pokhara / Kathmandu by an A/c vehicle</p>\n\n<p># Presently applicable hotel taxes.</p>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"15\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":\"37775\",\"land_cost\":null},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":37775,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 5666.25\",\"selling_price\":43441.25}', 'MZQ/0263/032022', 43500, 18500, 6500, '2022-03-23 11:47:35', '2022-03-23 11:52:28', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(268, 'ANIL GADODIA', 'BNI SHIVAM', '9431115118', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'LADAKH', '2022-05-06', 6, 0, 6, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Arrive Leh\",\"date\":\"06-05-2022 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Arrival at Leh Kushok Bakula Airport (This must be one of the Most Sensational Flights in the World. On a clear day from one side of the aircraft can be seen the distant peaks of K2, Nanga Parbat, Gasherbrum, and on the other side of the aircraft, so close that you feel you could reach out and touch it, is the Nun Kun massif.) Upon arrival, you will meet by Multi Zone Travels&nbsp;representative and transfer to Hotel for Check-in. Complete Day for rest and leisure to acclimatize followed by Welcome tea or Coffee at the Hotel.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overnight at Hotel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Leh - Excursion to Sham Valley (50 Kms \\/ 03-04 Hr)\",\"date\":\"07-05-2022 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After breakfast, you drive downstream along the River Indus on Leh \\u2013 Kargil Highway. And start our sightseeing with the Hall Of Fame (Museum Constructed by Indian Army) near Leh is worth a visit for every Indian, and proceed further to Gurudwara Patthar Sahib at an altitude of 3600 Mtrs about 22 kms from Leh was constructed in memory of Guru Nanak Dev ji Nestled deep in the Himalayas, A drive of another 4 km took us to Magnetic Hill which defies the law of gravity. As you move ahead from Magnetic Hills, just before Nimmu Village, there comes a famous Confluence Of Two Rivers Indus River coming from Tibet (left) and Zanskar River coming from&nbsp;Zanskar Valley&nbsp;(right). Zanskar River is known for its famous Chadar Trek. Later we drive back to Leh. Evening visit to Leh Palace, Shanti Stupa &amp; Leh Market.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overnight at Hotel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Leh\\u2013Nubra Valley via Khardung La 18,390 FT. (120 Kms \\/ 4 \\u2013 5 Hrs)\",\"date\":\"08-05-2022 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Post breakfast we drive to Nubra Valley. The road journey from Leh to Nubra Valley passes over Khardung La (The Highest Motorable Road In The World) at 5,602 Mtrs \\/ 18,390 Ft, around 39 km from Leh. From the pass, one can see all the way south over the Indus valley to seemingly endless peaks and ridges of the Zanskar range, and north to the giants of the Saser massif. Nubra Valley is popularly known as Ldumra or the valley of flowers. It is situated in the north of Ladakh between the Karakoram and Ladakh ranges of the Himalayas. The average altitude of the valley is 10,000 Ft. above sea level.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Upon arrival in Nubra, we check in at our Camp OR Hotel. Evening we drive to Hunder where you have the opportunity to ride on a Bactrian camel (double humped) amidst the sand dunes of this high-altitude desert with snowcapped mountains on the horizon. Between Hunder and Diskit you come across sand dunes beside the road. Seen in isolation you could well be amongst the sand dunes of the Thar Desert in Rajasthan. On the return stop at Diskit which is the headquarters town of the Nubra Valley. Stroll around the bazaar observing the shops and local people going about their daily chores. Diskit is famous for 515 years old Buddhist Monastery, lying magnificently situated on a hilltop, facing the entire Valley. Later we drive back to Camp for Dinner.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overnight at the Camp.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Nubra Valley to Pangong Lake (170 Kms \\/ 7 Hrs)\",\"date\":\"09-05-2022 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Post breakfast we drive towards Pangong Tso via Agham &amp; Shyok Valley. Some of the road patches in areas are extremely tough (towards the Nubra side) in terms of road conditions but no doubt the journey is very scenic!&nbsp; Later after crossing this adventurous part we drive further towards Durbuk &amp; Tangtse for Pangong you pass through a few small villages of Changthang and finally, you can have a sudden view of the Pangong lake situated at 14,000 feet (4,267 m). This famous blue brackish Lake of Pangong is 5\\/6 Kms wide and over 133 Kms long with half of its running on the other side of the \\\"Indo China Border\\\". One rarely feels so close to nature and the environment and the scenery are unforgettable. After the success of 3 Idiots, this beautiful natural location has attracted more tourists from all over the world. Upon arrival, we check-in at our Camp Near Pangong lake.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overnight at the Camp.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pangong Lake to Leh Via Changla (140 Kms \\/ 6 Hrs)\",\"date\":\"10-05-2022 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Morning at leisure to explore the beauty of the lake and later we drive back to Leh via Changla Pass 5486 Mtrs enroute visiting Thiksey an impressive complex rising tier upon tier on a hill above the village and another 5 Kms Driving through a picturesque landscape we reach to Shey Palace, The ancient capital of Ladakh&nbsp; &amp;3 Idiots Rancho School. Drive further to Leh and check-in at our hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overnight at Hotel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Leh \\u2013 At Leisure\",\"date\":\"11-05-2022 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Complete Day at Leisure to explore the destination on your own.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overnight at Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Depart Leh (Fly Out)\",\"date\":\"12-05-2022 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" \\/><\\/p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Tour concludes. Multi Zone Travels thank you for your patronage and ensures a punctual transfer to Domestic Airport to catch the flight for your onward Destination.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"5043\",\"dep_date\":\"06 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"06 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"07:45 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"09:30 AM\",\"fare\":71922},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Leh (IXL)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"2797\",\"dep_date\":\"06 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"06 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"10:55 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Leh (IXL)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"602\",\"dep_date\":\"12 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"12 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"09:20 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"10:50 AM\",\"fare\":70980},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"753\",\"dep_date\":\"12 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"12 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"05:55 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"07:40 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"06\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"LEH\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel The Zen\",\"room_type\":\"Premium Room\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"08\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"08\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"NUBRA\",\"hotel_name\":\"The Verda White Sand Resort\",\"room_type\":\"Luxury Cottages\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"09\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"09\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"PANGONG\",\"hotel_name\":\"Pangong Retreat Camp\",\"room_type\":\"Luxury Tent\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"10\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"10\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"LEH\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel The Abduz\",\"room_type\":\"Executive Club\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"12\\/05\\/2022\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<p>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Return Airfare <strong>Ex-Ranchi.</strong></p>\n\n<p>.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Assistance upon arrival at KushokBakula Rinpoche Airport</p>\n\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Traditional welcome in the Hotel with Welcome Drink (Hot Tea / Coffee / Kahwa) on arrival</p>\n\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;04&nbsp;Nights Accommodation in Leh on double sharing Basis as per the Itinerary</p>\n\n<p>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;01 Night Accommodation in Nubra Valley on Double sharing Basis as per the Itinerary</p>\n\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;01 Night Accommodation in Pangong Lake on double&nbsp; sharing Basis as per the Itinerary</p>\n\n<p>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; Meal Plan - MAPAI (Breakfast + Dinners</p>\n\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Morning Tea / Coffee with Biscuits on the day of departure</p>\n\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Return airport and round trip transfers along with all sightseeing tours by&nbsp;Non-Ac Innova Crysta&nbsp; as per the Itinerary</p>\n\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Inner Line Permit (Wildlife, Red Cross &amp; Environment fees)</p>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"15\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":142902,\"land_cost\":\"258225\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":401127,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 60169.05\",\"selling_price\":461296.0499999999883584678173065185546875}', 'MZQ/0264/032022', 461400, 76900, 0, '2022-03-29 11:51:42', '2022-03-29 11:51:42', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `quotation` (`id`, `guest_name`, `ref_name`, `mobile_no`, `email`, `destination`, `tentative_date`, `nights`, `children`, `adults`, `itineraries`, `flights`, `trains`, `hotels`, `terms_conditions`, `children_ages`, `inclusion`, `exclusion`, `payment_policy`, `cancellation_policy`, `costing`, `ref_id`, `total`, `adult_cost`, `child_cost`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_confirmed`, `hide_note`, `other_details`, `is_feedback_sent`, `is_feedback_received`) VALUES
(269, 'MR ANUP AGARWAL', 'BNI', '9431101780', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'Char Dham Yatra', '2022-06-10', 11, 0, 8, '[{\"title\":\"Friday\",\"day\":\"Day 1\",\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Dehradun \\u2013 Haridwar ( 50 kms\\/1.25Hrs)\",\"date\":\"10-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>Meet our driver at Dehradun Airport&nbsp;and drive to Haridwar. Check into the hotel on arrival in Haridwar.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Evening visit Mansa Devi Temple &amp; Ganga aarti at Har Ki Pauri. Overnight stay at Haridwar.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>An Evening at Ganga Aarti Haridwar:&nbsp;The Ganga Aarti in Hardwar\\u2019s Har-ki-Pauri is one of the famous rituals in India. It starts at around 6.30 pm after sunset, with large crowds gathered around both the banks of a canal that carries the waters of the Ganges. Loudspeakers blare songs in praise of&nbsp;Ganga Maiya&nbsp;and Shiva.&nbsp;The time Aarti sees a bustle of activity on the ghats A pack of diya comes fully equipped and is self-sufficient! It has a wick lamp surrounded by flowers It lasted for around 30 min.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Saturday\",\"day\":\"Day 2\",\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Haridwar - Barkot (210kms\\/7-8Hrs) Height: 1352 MTS\",\"date\":\"11-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning after breakfast transfer to Barkot via Mussoorie.En-route visit Mussoorie Lake &amp; Kempty Fall in Mussoorie. Later drive to Barkot. On arrival, check-in at the hotel in Barkot for dinner &amp; overnight stay.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Sunday\",\"day\":\"Day 3\",\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Barkot - Yamunotri - Barkot {42kms Drive\\/5 kms Trek (One Side)} Height:3165 MTS\",\"date\":\"12-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>Early morning after breakfast (packed breakfast), drive to Jankichatti \\/ Phoolchatti &amp; trek from here to Yamunotri (6kms) (Either by walk or by horse or by Doli at own cost). After taking bath in Jamunabai Kund\\u2019s warm water and cook rice by packing it in a cloth and dipping it in the hot water of the hot kund. Pilgrims take this cooked rice home as \\\"Prasad\\\". Having Darshan of \\u201cYamunaji\\u201d return to Jankichatti by trek. Overnight stay at Barkot.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Hanuman Chatti:&nbsp;The confluence of Hanuman Ganga &amp; Yamuna River.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Yamunotri Temple:&nbsp;Maharani Gularia of Jaipur built the temple in the 19th Century. It was destroyed twice in the present century and rebuilt again.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Surya Kund:&nbsp;There are a Number of thermal springs in the vicinity of the temple, which flow intonumerous pools. The most important of these is Surya Kund.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Divya Shila:&nbsp;A rock pillar, worshipped before entering the Yamunotri Temple.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Yamunotri- Yamunotri is situated in the western region of the Garhwal Himalayas and is at a height of 3,235 meters above sea level. Yamunotri is the source of the river Yamuna. The shrine of Yamunotri is located on the Bandar Poonch peak.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Monday\",\"day\":\"Day 4\",\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Barkot - Uttarkashi (100 kms\\/4Hrs) Heights: 1158 MTS\",\"date\":\"13-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>The morning after leisurely breakfast, drive to Uttarkashi. Check into the hotel arrival in Uttarkashi. Evening visit Kashi Vishwanath Temple in Uttarkashi. Overnight stay at Uttarkashi.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Uttarkashi:&nbsp;Situated at the bank of river Bhagirathi. The temple of Lord Vishwanath is located here where a massive iron trident is erected. The other important temples situated here are Ekadash Rudra, Bhairav, Gyaneshwar, and Goddess Kuteti Devi.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Tuesday\",\"day\":\"Day 5\",\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Uttarkashi - Gangotri - Uttarkashi (120kms\\/5 hrs each side) Heights: 3142 MTS\",\"date\":\"14-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>Early morning (packed breakfast) drive to Gangotri(3048 mts), en route at Gangnani take a holy dip in Garam Kund, have bath drive to Gangotri via beautiful Harsil Valley. Harsil is famous for its natural beauty and for the majestic views of the Deodar trees and mountains. On arrival at Shree Gangotri, take a holy dip in the sacred river Ganges which is also called Bhagirathi at its origin. Perform Pooja and Darshan, after that relax for some time in the lovely surroundings. Later drive back to Uttarkashi. Overnight stay at Uttarkashi.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Gangotri- Gangotri is the place high in the Garhwal Himalayas from where the holy Ganges originates. According to the legend, it was here the Ganga descended on the earth when Lord Shiva released the mighty river from the locks of his hair. The temple of Gangotri, dedicated to Goddess Ganga stands on the bank of the river.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Wednesday\",\"day\":\"Day 6\",\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Uttarkashi \\u2013 Guptkashi\\/Sitapur (290kms\\/8-9hrs)\",\"date\":\"15-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>The morning after breakfast, drive to Guptkashi via Moolgarh &amp; Lambgoan. En route, you can see the beautiful river Mandakini at Tilwara. The Mandakini River comes from Kedarnath, drive alongside the river to reach Guptkashi, and visit ArdhNarishwar Temple in Guptkashi. Check into the hotel arrival in Guptkashi.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Guptakashi.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Thursday\",\"day\":\"Day 7\",\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guptkashi\\/Sitapur \\u2013 Shri Kedarnath ji(By Helicopter Own Cost) (32kms Drive) Heights: 3584 MTS\",\"date\":\"16-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>The morning after breakfast drive to Helipad, reach Kedarnath by helicopter,&nbsp;visit Kedarnath ji Temple &amp; perform Pooja. In the evening also&nbsp;visit Adi Shankaracharya Samadhi behind the Temple.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Camp\\/Hotel @ Kedarnath.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Shri Kedarnath-&nbsp;is a majestic sight, standing in the middle of a wide plateau surrounded by lofty snow Covered peaks. The temple of Kedarnath, located at a height of 3,581 mts, stands at the head of the Mandakini river. The present temple, built in the 8th century by Adi Shankaracharya, stands adjacent to the site of an earlier temple built by the Pandavas. The inner walls of the assembly hall are decorated with figures of various deities and scenes from mythology. Outside the temple door, a large statue of the Nandi Bull stands as guard. It is said that devotees who die here become one with Shiva himself.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Friday\",\"day\":\"Day 8\",\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kedarnath - Guptkashi (32kms Drive)\",\"date\":\"17-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>The morning after breakfast, drive to Guptkashi.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>OverNight stay at Guptkashi.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Saturday\",\"day\":\"Day 9\",\"index\":8,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guptkashi\\/Sitapur- Shri Badrinath (220kms\\/7Hrs) Heights: 3133 MTS\",\"date\":\"18-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>The morning after breakfast, drive to Shri Badrinath. Check in to the hotel arrival in Shri Badrinath. Pilgrims after having a bath in the Taptkund have the Darshan of&nbsp; Badrivishal &amp; Aarti in the evening. Brahamakapal is significant for Pinddan Shraddh of ancestors (Pitrus). There is other interesting sightseeing spot like Mana, Vyas Gufa, Maatamoorti, Charanpaduka, Bhimkund, and the \\u201cMukh\\u201d of the Saraswati River. Just within the 03&nbsp;km of Badrinathjee. Overnight stay at Shri Badrinath.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Shri Badrinath- Shri Badrinath is one of the most important of all the four(Char) Dhams in India. This temple is located between Nar &amp; Narayan mountain ranges and in the shadow of the Nilkantha peak at the height of 3,133 mts. It is the most popular of Vishnu pilgrimages among the five Badries, also known as Vishal Badri.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Tapt Kund:&nbsp;Natural thermal springs on the bank of the river Alaknanda, where it is customary to bathe before entering the Badrinath temple.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Narad Kund:&nbsp;A recess in the river, near Tapt Kund, forming a pool from where the Badrinath idol was recovered.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Mata Murty Temple:&nbsp;Devoted to the mother of Sri Badrinathji. Other important temples include SeshNetra Temple, Urvashi Temple, and Charanpaduka.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Mana Village:&nbsp;Inhabited by an Indo-Mongolian tribe, it is the last Indian village before Tibet.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Bhim Pul:&nbsp;On the other side of Mana village, a massive rock forming a natural bridge lies<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>over the roaring Saraswati River. It presents a spectacular view of water thundering down through the narrow passage under the rock and is believed to have been placed there by Bhim, the second eldest among the five Pandava brothers.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Vyas Gufa (cave):&nbsp;Near Mana Village, this is a rock cave where Ved Vyas is believed to have composed the Mahabharata and the pauranic commentaries.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Sunday\",\"day\":\"Day 10\",\"index\":9,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Shri Badrinath \\u2013 Srinagar (77\\/46\\/187\\/155 kms 7-9 hrs) Heights: 895 MTS\",\"date\":\"19-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning after breakfast, driver for Srinagar via Pipalkoti. Visit on the way Narsingh Temple in Joshimath later drive back to Rudraprayag via Joshimath. Check into the hotel arrival in Srinagar. Overnight stay at Srinagar.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Rudraprayag:&nbsp;One of the holy prayag of five famous prayag of Uttarakhand. Confluence of River Alaknanda and Mandakini.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Narsingh Temple: This is an ancient temple of Lord Vishnu in Narsingh Avtar and main temple of Joshimath. When Badrinath temple remain closed during winter every year, one idol of Lord Badri is brought to Narsingh temple and worshiped for six months.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Monday\",\"day\":\"Day 11\",\"index\":10,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Srinagar - Dehradun (145kms\\/3.5-4hrs)\",\"date\":\"20-06-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>The morning after breakfast, drive for Dehradun.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>On Arrival Checkin Into Hotel &amp; you all can explore Dehradun City on your own.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":12,\"index\":11,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Dehradun Departure\",\"date\":\"21-06-2022 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After Breakfast, Checkout from Hotel &amp; proceed to Dehradun Airport to catch your Return Flight.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"752\",\"dep_date\":\"10 Jun 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"10 Jun 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"08:55 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"11:00 AM\",\"fare\":\"57306\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Dehradun (DED)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"617\",\"dep_date\":\"10 Jun 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"10 Jun 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"01:45 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"02:45 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Dehradun (DED)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"618\",\"dep_date\":\"21 Jun 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"21 Jun 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"03:20 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"04:20 PM\",\"fare\":\"51219\"},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"753\",\"dep_date\":\"21 Jun 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"21 Jun 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"05:55 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"07:40 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"10\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Haridwar\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Godwin\",\"check_out\":\"11\\/06\\/2022\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":4,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"11\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Barkot\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"13\\/06\\/2022\",\"hotel_name\":\"Mountain Bird Cottage\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":4,\"meal\":\"map\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"13\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Uttarkashi\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Shakshi\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":4,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"15\\/06\\/2022\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"15\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Guptkashi\",\"hotel_name\":\"White Haven Luxury Camp\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":4,\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"16\\/06\\/2022\",\"meal\":\"map\"},{\"id\":4,\"check_in\":\"16\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Kedarnath\",\"hotel_name\":\"White House (Basic Accomodation in Dharamshala))\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":4,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"17\\/06\\/2022\"},{\"id\":5,\"check_in\":\"17\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Guptkashi\",\"hotel_name\":\"Camp Nirvana\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":4,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"18\\/06\\/2022\"},{\"id\":6,\"check_in\":\"18\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Badrinath\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Amritara By Awad\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"rooms\":4,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"19\\/06\\/2022\"},{\"id\":7,\"check_in\":\"19\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Srinagar\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel River Side Resort\",\"rooms\":4,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"20\\/06\\/2022\",\"rate\":null},{\"id\":8,\"check_in\":\"20\\/06\\/2022\",\"city\":\"Dehradun\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Sarovar Portico\",\"room_type\":\"Superior Room\",\"rooms\":4,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"check_out\":\"21\\/06\\/2022\",\"rate\":\"17600\",\"nights\":1}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare Ex-Ranchi.</li>\n	<li>Neat, clean, hygienic accommodation on Double / Triple sharing as per preferences &amp; group size.</li>\n	<li>Inclusive of transport services (Ex Ranchi)</li>\n	<li>All point-to-point sightseeing as per the given program is possible in the time frame.</li>\n	<li>All toll, tax, parking, and driver allowances are included.</li>\n	<li>Daily Breakfast and Dinner except for Dehradun(Only Breakfast).</li>\n	<li>All taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Laundry</li>\n	<li>Entrance fees</li>\n	<li>Ropeway, Guide, Porter &amp; Pony</li>\n	<li>Entry Tickets / VIP Darshan Tickets</li>\n	<li>Kedarnath Helicopter Tickets</li>\n	<li>Any up gradation in Airline class or hotel room category</li>\n	<li>Any extra expense such as route change, Date change, Accommodation facilities, etc incurred due to the unforeseen, unavoidable forced majeure&nbsp;circumstances during the tour.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, '<p>Normal Cancellation Policy:-</p>\n\n<p># &nbsp;Between 45 days and 30 days of departure - 50% of tour cost<br />\n# &nbsp;Between 30 days and 15 prior to the date of departure - 75%<br />\n# &nbsp;Between 15 days and In case of no show - 100%</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Cancellation policy in times of Covid 19</p>\n\n<p># In case of Lockdown imposed by the Government or any change in SOPs from the government, if a tour gets postponed the amount shall be adjusted in future booking&nbsp;for the same guest, subject to availability. Rates may differ as per the season.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p># In case guests do not wish to travel in the future, then Rs.5000/ + GST shall be charged per person as our service charges.</p>\n\n<p># Refund shall be managed only after receiving&nbsp;from our vendors and concerned&nbsp;hotels. Though we will expedite this process to the best of our capability</p>', '{\"profit_percent\":null,\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":108525,\"land_cost\":\"346800\",\"hotel_cost\":\"17600\",\"transport_cost\":null},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":472925,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 0\",\"selling_price\":556000,\"profit_figure\":\"83075\",\"percent_of_amount\":\"17.00%\"}', 'MZQ/0265/032022', 556000, 69500, 0, '2022-03-29 20:07:47', '2022-06-07 14:24:48', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(270, 'MR RAVISH JINDAL', 'BNI CELEBRITIES', '9437194464', 'btcjindal@gmail.com', 'KASHMIR', '2022-05-15', 5, 2, 4, '[{\"title\":\"Sunday\",\"day\":\"Day 1\",\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Arrive in Srinagar\",\"date\":\"15-05-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>Upon arrival, meet our representative and take a transfer to the hotel\\/houseboat. Spend the day at leisure on boulevard road which is one of the most famous roads in Srinagar for tourists and is situated around Dal lake surrounded by Zabarwan mountain ranges, also enjoy a 1 hr shikara ride in Dal Lake at Nehru Park on boulevard road.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay in Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Monday\",\"day\":\"Day 2\",\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Srinagar - Sonmarg \\u2013 Srinagar (85 kms \\/ 2:30 hours approximately)\",\"date\":\"16-05-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast leave with a full day excursion for Sonmarg \\u201cThe meadow of gold. Situated at an altitude of 9000 Ft. Sonmarg is at a distance of 84 Kms from Srinagar is also called \\u201cThe meadow of gold\\u201d. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. The place is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lake. Ponies can be hired for the trip up to Thajiwas glacier, which is a major local attraction during the summer.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Drive back from Sonmarg to Srinagar. Overnight stay in Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Tuesday\",\"day\":\"Day 3\",\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Srinagar - Pahalgam (86 kms \\/ 2:30 hours approximately)\",\"date\":\"17-05-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After Breakfast Drive to Pahalgam \\u201cValley of Shepherds\\u201d. On arrival check in at Hotel In Pahalgam enjoy nature and admire the beauty of this quiet place and be in awe of the serene surroundings. One can also enjoy a pony ride to nearby places like Chandanwadi (on a direct-hire basis) or if you are an avid nature lover you may take pleasure in a peaceful walk along the River Lidder. Pahalgam is famous for some trekking routes also &amp; is the base camp for Amarnath Pilgrimage.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay in Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Wednesday\",\"day\":\"Day 4\",\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pahalgam \\u2013 Gulmarg (120 kms \\/ 4:00 hours approximately)\",\"date\":\"18-05-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast drive to Gulmarg \\u201cMeadow of Flowers\\u201d 2730 Mts. above sea level. The distance of 60 km will be covered in about 2 hrs. Gulmarg has one of the best Ski slopes in the world and the highest golf course in the world with 18 holes. One can also have a view of Nanga Parbhat if the weather permits. The view enroute from Tangmarg to Gulmarg is fascinating. One can also have a short trek up to Khilangmarg which can be covered in about 3 to 4 hrs or enjoy the scenic view of Kongdori on a Cable Car Known as Gondola (on your own).<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay in Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Thursday\",\"day\":\"Day 5\",\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Gulmarg - Srinagar (56 kms \\/ 2:00 hours approximately)\",\"date\":\"19-05-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast, drive to Srinagar and enjoy the site scene of the famous Mughal Gardens<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Cheshma Shahi \\u201cRoyal Spring\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Shalimar \\u201cGarden&nbsp;of&nbsp;Love\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Nishat&nbsp;Garden&nbsp;\\u201cGarden of Pleasure\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Shankaracharya&nbsp;Temple.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>On return visit a local Handicrafts Showroom for hand-knotted specialty silken carpets, shawls, jewelry ornaments.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay in Houseboat<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Friday\",\"day\":\"Day 6\",\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Srinagar - Onward destination.\",\"date\":\"20-05-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast enjoy the morning in Srinagar and get ready for transfer to the Srinagar airport to board your scheduled flight for your onward destination.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Tour ends...<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"752\",\"dep_date\":\"15 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"15 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"08:55 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"11:00 AM\",\"fare\":90684},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Srinagar (SXR)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"643\",\"dep_date\":\"15 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"15 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"11:45 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:10 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Srinagar (SXR)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"204\",\"dep_date\":\"20 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"20 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"09:35 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"11:10 AM\",\"fare\":\"52086\"},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"6198\",\"dep_date\":\"20 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"20 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"04:20 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:10 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"15\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"SRINAGAR\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Royal Arabia\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE AC\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"17\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"17\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"PAHALGAM\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Royal Park\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE AC\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"18\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"18\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"GULMARG\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Paristaan Resort\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE AC\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"19\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"19\\/05\\/2022\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Royal Arabia\",\"city\":\"SRINAGAR\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE AC\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"20\\/05\\/2022\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":4},{\"age\":8}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <strong>ExRanchi.</strong></li>\n	<li>Hotel / HouseBoat accommodation on&nbsp;<strong>02 Dbl Room</strong> + <strong>01 Child Without bed +&nbsp;01 Child Extra bed</strong></li>\n	<li>CP&nbsp;(<strong>Breakfast </strong>)&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>Arrival&nbsp; &amp; Departure Srinagar Airport / Railway Station.</li>\n	<li>01 Private Innova for transfers as per Itinerary.&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>Day trip to Sonmarg</li>\n	<li>SS Mughal Gardens, Shankara Achariya Temple&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>01 Hour Shikara Ride in Dal lake</li>\n	<li>SS of Badamwari Garden in Srinagar</li>\n	<li>Medical Kit in Taxi</li