l>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"15\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":42803,\"land_cost\":null,\"hotel_cost\":120650,\"transport_cost\":\"33500\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":196953,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 29542.95\",\"selling_price\":226495.9500000000116415321826934814453125}', 'MZQ/0272/042022', 225900, 112950, 0, '2022-04-20 13:01:43', '2022-05-02 15:53:48', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `quotation` (`id`, `guest_name`, `ref_name`, `mobile_no`, `email`, `destination`, `tentative_date`, `nights`, `children`, `adults`, `itineraries`, `flights`, `trains`, `hotels`, `terms_conditions`, `children_ages`, `inclusion`, `exclusion`, `payment_policy`, `cancellation_policy`, `costing`, `ref_id`, `total`, `adult_cost`, `child_cost`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_confirmed`, `hide_note`, `other_details`, `is_feedback_sent`, `is_feedback_received`) VALUES
(277, 'MR CHETAN AGARWAL', 'BNI CELEBRITIES', '7978465033', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'KASHMIR', '2022-04-27', 5, 0, 4, '[{\"title\":\"Wednesday\",\"day\":\"Day 1\",\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Arrive in Srinagar\",\"date\":\"27-04-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>Upon arrival, meet our representative and take a transfer to the hotel\\/houseboat. Spend the day at leisure on boulevard road which is one of the most famous roads in Srinagar for tourists and is situated around Dal lake surrounded by Zabarwan mountain ranges, also enjoy a 1 hr shikara ride in Dal Lake at Nehru Park on boulevard road.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay in Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Thursday\",\"day\":\"Day 2\",\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Srinagar - Sonmarg \\u2013 Srinagar (85 kms \\/ 2:30 hours approximately)\",\"date\":\"28-04-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast leave with a full day excursion for Sonmarg \\u201cThe meadow of gold. Situated at an altitude of 9000 Ft. Sonmarg is at a distance of 84 Kms from Srinagar is also called \\u201cThe meadow of gold\\u201d. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. The place is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lake. Ponies can be hired for the trip up to Thajiwas glacier, which is a major local attraction during the summer.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Drive back from Sonmarg to Srinagar. Overnight stay in Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Friday\",\"day\":\"Day 3\",\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Srinagar - Pahalgam (86 kms \\/ 2:30 hours approximately)\",\"date\":\"29-04-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After Breakfast Drive to Pahalgam \\u201cValley of Shepherds\\u201d. On arrival check in at Hotel In Pahalgam enjoy nature and admire the beauty of this quiet place and be in awe of the serene surroundings. One can also enjoy a pony ride to nearby places like Chandanwadi (on a direct-hire basis) or if you are an avid nature lover you may take pleasure in a peaceful walk along the River Lidder. Pahalgam is famous for some trekking routes also &amp; is the base camp for Amarnath Pilgrimage.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay in Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Saturday\",\"day\":\"Day 4\",\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pahalgam \\u2013 Gulmarg (120 kms \\/ 4:00 hours approximately)\",\"date\":\"30-04-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast drive to Gulmarg \\u201cMeadow of Flowers\\u201d 2730 Mts. above sea level. The distance of 60 km will be covered in about 2 hrs. Gulmarg has one of the best Ski slopes in the world and the highest golf course in the world with 18 holes. One can also have a view of Nanga Parbhat if the weather permits. The view enroute from Tangmarg to Gulmarg is fascinating. One can also have a short trek up to Khilangmarg which can be covered in about 3 to 4 hrs or enjoy the scenic view of Kongdori on a Cable Car Known as Gondola (on your own).<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay in Hotel<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Sunday\",\"day\":\"Day 5\",\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Gulmarg - Srinagar (56 kms \\/ 2:00 hours approximately)\",\"date\":\"01-05-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast, drive to Srinagar and enjoy the site scene of the famous Mughal Gardens<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Cheshma Shahi \\u201cRoyal Spring\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Shalimar \\u201cGarden&nbsp;of&nbsp;Love\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Nishat&nbsp;Garden&nbsp;\\u201cGarden of Pleasure\\u201d<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Shankaracharya&nbsp;Temple.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>On return visit a local Handicrafts Showroom for hand-knotted specialty silken carpets, shawls, jewelry ornaments.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay in Houseboat<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Monday\",\"day\":\"Day 6\",\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Srinagar - Onward destination.\",\"date\":\"02-05-2022\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast enjoy the morning in Srinagar and get ready for transfer to the Srinagar airport to board your scheduled flight for your onward destination.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Tour ends...<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"2094\",\"dep_date\":\"27 Apr 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"27 Apr 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"12:35 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"02:30 PM\",\"fare\":47740},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Srinagar (SXR)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"6081\",\"dep_date\":\"27 Apr 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"27 Apr 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"04:45 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:25 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Srinagar (SXR)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"AirAsia India\",\"fno\":\"559\",\"dep_date\":\"02 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"02 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"01:25 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"05:25 PM\",\"fare\":47748}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"27\\/04\\/2022\",\"city\":\"SRINAGAR\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Rose Petal \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE AC\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"29\\/04\\/2022\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"29\\/04\\/2022\",\"city\":\"PAHALGAM\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Mount View \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE AC\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"30\\/04\\/2022\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"30\\/04\\/2022\",\"city\":\"GULMARG\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Royal Park \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE AC\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"01\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"01\\/05\\/2022\",\"hotel_name\":\"Super Deluxe Houseboats\",\"city\":\"SRINAGAR\",\"room_type\":\"DOUBLE AC\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"02\\/05\\/2022\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <strong>ExRanchi.</strong></li>\n	<li>Hotel / HouseBoat accommodation on&nbsp;<strong>02 Dbl Room.</strong></li>\n	<li>MAP&nbsp;(<strong>Breakfast + Dinner&nbsp;</strong>)&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>Arrival&nbsp; &amp; Departure Srinagar Airport / Railway Station.</li>\n	<li>01 Private <strong>Innova</strong> for transfers as per Itinerary.&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>Day trip to Sonmarg</li>\n	<li>SS Mughal Gardens, Shankara Achariya Temple&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>01 Hour Shikara Ride in Dal lake</li>\n	<li>SS of Badamwari Garden in Srinagar</li>\n	<li>Medical Kit in Taxi</li>\n	<li>All applicable taxes.</li>\n	<li>Driver Charges, Toll, Parking included&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>Meeting &amp; Assistance on Arrival&nbsp;/Departure .</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any Kind of Personal Expenses or Optional Tours / Extra Meals Ordered</li>\n	<li>Anything not specifically mentioned under the head “Prices included”.</li>\n	<li>The Services of Vehicle is not included on leisure&nbsp;days&nbsp;&amp; after finishing the sightseeing tour as per the Itinerary</li>\n	<li>Guide fee, Camera fee &amp; any monument &nbsp;Entrances</li>\n	<li>Medical &amp; Travel insurance</li>\n	<li>Any changes you may choose to make during your tour</li>\n	<li>Additional costs due to flight cancellation, roadblocks, etc.</li>\n	<li>Gondola Ticket, Pony/Sledge riding at Gulmarg / Pahalgam / SonmargEntrance fee, Local Guide, Shikara Ride</li>\n	<li>Trip to Thajiwas Glacier &amp; Zero point in Sonamarg,</li>\n	<li>Trip to Chandanwari, Aru, Betaab valley, etc.</li>\n	<li>Any Loss/expenses incurred by unforeseen circumstances e.g. flight delays/cancellations, road blockage, vehicle breakdown strikes, etc</li>\n	<li>Chained Vehicles From tangmarg to Gulmarg &amp; Gulmarg to Tangmarg in case of Snow</li>\n	<li>Chained vehicles in Sonmarg in case of Snow</li>\n</ul>', NULL, '<ul>\n	<li>Date of booking to 31 days before travel the cancellation charges will be 25% of the tour cost</li>\n	<li>30 to 16 days before travel - cancellation charges will be 50% of the tour cost</li>\n	<li>15 to 8 days before travel - cancellation charges will be 75% of the tour cost</li>\n	<li>0 to 7 days before travel - cancellation charges will be 100% of the tour cost. No refund shall be given</li>\n	<li>Please Note:&nbsp;Cancellation policy is subject to change. It depends on the hotel policy.</li>\n	<li>In peak season (example: long weekends, festival season, summer vacation, etc.) most of the hotels charge 100% cancellation.</li>\n</ul>', '{\"profit_percent\":\"13\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":95488,\"hotel_cost\":null,\"land_cost\":\"116000\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":211488,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 27493.44\",\"selling_price\":238981.4400000000023283064365386962890625}', 'MZQ/0273/042022', 238000, 59500, 27800, '2022-04-23 11:36:59', '2022-05-04 11:42:14', 0, 1, '\"<p><em><strong>SUPPLEMENTS FOR OTHER OPTIONS:-<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7Professional Tourist Guide: &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rs. 2500 Per Day<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7River Rafting on Indus | Zanskar:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Rs. 2000 Per Person approx<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7Transport Till Rafting Point from Sangam&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Rs. 1,000.00 (One Way)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7Motorbike hire for full day:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Rs.1,800.00 Per Bike + Fuel<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7Pedal down the highest motorable road on a cycle:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Rs.1,500 per Pax including transport (min 4 pax)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7Camel Ride in Nubra Valley&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rs. 500 Per Person (approximately)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7ATV Ride in Nubra Valley&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rs. 1200 Per Person (approximately)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7Hall of Fame sound &amp; Light show (Vehicle Cost)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Rs. 1500.00 (Return)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7Cultural Dance Program:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rs. 12,000 Per Program<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7Oxygen Cylinder Charges: &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rs. 800 Per Day (approximately)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<table>\\n\\t<tbody>\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\n\\t\\t\\t<h2 style=\\\"font-style:italic;\\\">SPECIAL NOTE: COVID19<\\/h2>\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>NOTE:&nbsp;Guest should carry COVID -19 negative test report 96 hours prior to arrival date.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Travelers who have had both vaccination and 15 days have passed since the last dose are not required to furnish a negative report. They can come with a hard copy of the vaccination certificate.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\u2714&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;To avoid high altitude sickness Diamox tablet can be taken prior to coming to Leh but only after consulting with your doctor.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\u2714&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once you land in Leh Kindly wear a jacket to avoid high altitude sickness.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\u2714&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transport: As per the SOPs and guidelines regarding the commercial transport 5 people are permitted to travel in Innova, 8 people in Tempo Traveller. Please convey the same to the group as well to eliminate the last-minute confusion.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\u2714&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Hotels: We have been using hotels that are strictly following the health and hygiene SOPS suggested by MHA and WHO. The SOPS are attached for your kind reference. Please go through the same.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\u2714&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Traveller: Post COVID-19 the entire globe has changed so has been the travel. We have tried to compile the SOPs for the travelers as well and kindly share the same with the traveler as well.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\u2714&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Itinerary:&nbsp; Please note sightseeing and excursion will be strict as per the norm laid by the MHA and Monasteries and other attractions opening and entry is subject to the guidelines suggested by MHA and local administration. You may find few sightseeing points non-operational which have been mentioned in the itinerary kindly accept as it is on the given day.<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\n\\t<\\/tbody>\\n<\\/table>\"', 0, 0),
(278, 'MR P K LAL DAS', NULL, '9431356124', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'NORTH EAST', '2022-05-20', 9, 0, 2, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guwahati Arrival\",\"date\":\"20-05-2022 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Meet and greet on arrival at Guwahati Airport and transfer to Hotel. On arrival check in to the hotel. Evening is free for leisure.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Guwahati.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guwahati \\u2013 Bhalukpong (255 Kms \\/ 6 hrs.)\",\"date\":\"21-05-2022 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After early breakfast drive to Bhalukpong. On arrival check in to the hotel. Evening is free for leisure.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Bhalukpong.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Bhalukpong \\u2013 Dirang (140 kms \\/ 7 hrs)\",\"date\":\"22-05-2022 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After early breakfast drive to Dirang. On the way visit Tipi Orchidarium situated on the banks of the river Bharali, a place over 500 orchids, on display there are some rare species of orchid. Arunachal has largest range of orchids in the country then take a break to visit Nag Temple. Continue your drive and do not forget to keep your cameras handy as you cross beautiful waterfalls and get some spectacular views.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>On arrival check in to the hotel. Afternoon visit Apple orchard &amp; Kiwi Farm (depending upon season), Dirang Monastery and Kalachakra Monastery. Dirang is also famous for hot water springs where people take bath to cure skin ailments. Overnight stay at Dirang<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Note: Every Indian tourist visiting Arunachal Pradesh has to obtain ILP (Inner Line Permit) at Bhalukpong border before entering the state against submission of photo identity card and two copies of passport size photographs.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Dirang Sightseeing\",\"date\":\"23-05-2022 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast, set in to explore Dirang. Visit Dirang Monpa tribal villages, experience the locale flavour - head out on village walks and interact with local villagers to enhance your experience. Then proceed to Sangti Valley, situated along the shores of Sangti river, 25 km from Bomdila. The Sangti Valley is one of the seasonal homes of the majestic creature called the black-necked crane that flies across from China and perhaps Leh.&nbsp; Later visit the The National Research Centre on Yak is located above the main town. The centre also has a yak firm at Nyukmandung about 31 km from Dirang. You can also visit Apple orchard &amp; Kiwi Farm (depending upon season), Li-ung Gonpa and Kalachakra Monastery right into its laps. Dirang is also famous for hot water springs where people take bath to cure skin ailments.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Dirang.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Dirang \\u2013 Tawang (130 kms \\/ 7 hrs.)\",\"date\":\"24-05-2022 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After early breakfast proceed to Tawang the Land of Hidden Paradise. On the way enjoy the beauty of Sela Pass (13700 Ft) a border line between two districts i.e Tawang &amp; West KamengTawang, Sela Lake a small lake, which remains frozen for most of the year. Further drive to 10 kms visit Jaswantgarh War Memorial - a memorial to the brave soldier who single handily tried to hold of approaching Chinese from the pass during the 1962 Indo-Chinese war.&nbsp; Later visit majesty of Nuranng Falls where scenes from the SRK-Madhuri Dixit starrer \\u201cKoyla\\u201d were shot.&nbsp; Arrive &amp; check in to the hotel. Evening is free for leisure.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Tawang.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Tawang Local Sightseeing\",\"date\":\"25-05-2022 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast visit Tawang Monstery world famous seventeenth century Tawang Monastery, also known as Galden Namgyal Lhatse which overlooks the wide Tawang Valley at a height of 10,000 ft. The monastery is a vast complex of 65 buildings housing Lamas and antique scriptures written in gold letters and ancient scripture, images and has an eight meters high gilded Buddha statue. It is the largest monastery in the Himalayan region and the second oldest monastery in Asia. Five hundred lamas live in its residential buildings and it is rich in.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Later visit Urgeling Gompa, 6th Dalai Lama\\u2019s birth place who is the only Indian to have risen to such a high position in Gelupka Sect of Buddhism so far. Inside the monastery there are several Stupas (Vihar) and people from all walks of life visit this place during Buddhist new year to get the blessing for the coming year. Then proceed to the War Memorial which is dedicated to the martyrs of the 1962 Sino-Indian war. The memorial is 40-foot-high and like a stupa in design. It is locally called \\u2018Namgyal Chortan\\u2019. The&nbsp; names of 2420 martyrs imprinted in gold on 32 black granite plagues.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>You can also visit the craft center in Tawang sells beautiful masks, hand woven carpets, jewellery in silver, coral and amber, \\u2018chubas\\u2019 the local dressand delightful affordable mementos. Evening at leisure.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Tawang.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Tawang Local Sightseeing - High altitude lakes and Bumla Pass\",\"date\":\"26-05-2022 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today morning after early breakfast, you will drive to visit high altitude lake called as Shonga-tser Lake, popularly known as Madhuri Lake located 35, kms away from Tawang near the China Border. The drive to Sangestser Lake is full of thrill and one can still see the war bankers that had been used during the Chinese aggression in 1962. Nestled amidst the pristine mountains and picturesque surrounding, It was formed in the aftermath of the 1950 earthquake. Prior to the earthquake, this piece of land used to be employed as the grazing ground for the cattle. The evidence of it can be seen in the protruding trunks of the dead trees from the middle of the lake. The lake has been under supervision of Army men, who have also arranged for a cafeteria nearby. Tourists can relish on the delicious Momos, Maggis topped with a cup of tasty coffee or tea. Tourists can also take to trekking around the lake while enjoying the gentle lashes of the pleasant breeze around. You can drive further to Bumla Pass which is located about 37 km away from Tawang at the Indo-China border over 15,200 ft above sea level. During return take a photo stop at the beautiful PTSO lake enroute (17 kms away from Tawang, Pangong Tang Tso Lake popularly known as PT Tso which is an extremely scenic drive with bird\\u2019s eye view of the township below). Later in the afternoon drive back to hotel. Rest of the evening at leisure.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight at hotel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Tawang \\u2013 Bomdila (170 kms \\/ 8 hrs.)\",\"date\":\"27-05-2022 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast transfer to Bomdila (8,200 ft.) - the headquarter of West Kameng District of Arunachal Pradesh and also known for its Buddhist monasteries. It has a lot of attractions for the visitors for its cool climate. On arrival check in to the hotel. Later visit Gontse Rabgyaling Monastery (Upper Gonpa), Thub-Chog Gatsel Ling Monastery (Lower Gonpa). Bomdila offers wonderfully panoramic view of Himalayan landscapes and snow-clad ranges. Evening you can visit the local market.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Bomdila.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":9,\"index\":8,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Bomdila \\u2013 Guwahati (307 kms \\/ 7 hrs.)\",\"date\":\"28-05-2022 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After Breakfast transfer to Guwahati. On arrival check in at your hotel. Evening free for individual activities.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Overnight stay at Guwahati.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":10,\"index\":9,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guwahati Departure\",\"date\":\"29-05-2022 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast visit Kamakhya Temple (Notes -Timing 08:00 A.M till 01:00 P.M &amp; 3:00 P.M till its gets dark). Transfer to Guwahati Airport \\/ Railway Station for your onward journey.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Note: Temple visit will depend on your departure time. It May be done on previous day.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"7562\",\"dep_date\":\"20 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"20 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"09:05 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"10:30 AM\",\"fare\":13226},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Guwahati(gauhati) (GAU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"6156\",\"dep_date\":\"20 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"20 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"03:10 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"04:30 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Guwahati(gauhati) (GAU)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"394\",\"dep_date\":\"29 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"29 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"12:50 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:55 PM\",\"fare\":13278},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"7234\",\"dep_date\":\"29 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"29 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"04:20 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"05:50 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"20\\/05\\/2022\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Royale De Casa \\/ Similar\",\"city\":\"GUWAHATI\",\"room_type\":\"Double\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"21\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"21\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"BHALUKPONG\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Prashanti Cottages \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Double\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"22\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"22\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"DIRANG\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel The Mandala \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Double\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"24\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"24\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"TAWANG\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Yangzom \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Double\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"27\\/05\\/2022\"},{\"id\":4,\"check_in\":\"27\\/05\\/2022\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"28\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"BOMDILA\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Tsepal Yangzom \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Double\"},{\"id\":5,\"check_in\":\"28\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"GUWAHATI\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Royale De Casa \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Double\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"29\\/05\\/2022\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <strong>Ex-Ranchi.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>09&nbsp;Nights</strong> Accommodation in <strong>3* Deluxe </strong>Hotels.</li>\n	<li>Buffet/Fixed Menu <strong>Breakfast.</strong></li>\n	<li>Airport Transfers &amp; Sightseeing by Private Sanitized <strong>Swift Dzire.(</strong><em>AC will not work in Hilly Areas</em><strong>)</strong></li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li><strong>GST @5%</strong></li>\n	<li>Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips &amp; gratuity, mineral water, soft &amp; hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding and porterage.</li>\n	<li>Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary.</li>\n	<li>Entrance Fees &amp; Guide charges.</li>\n	<li>Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road&nbsp;blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, which is directly payable on the spot).</li>\n	<li>Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation &amp; land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure.</li>\n	<li>Room Heater Charges</li>\n	<li>Insurance.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"19\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":26504,\"land_cost\":\"116000\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":142504,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 27075.76\",\"selling_price\":169579.76000000000931322574615478515625}', 'MZQ/0274/042022', 169400, 84700, 0, '2022-04-23 18:39:12', '2022-04-23 18:39:12', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(280, 'MR VIKASH SAHU', NULL, '6200689387', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'UTTRAKHAND', '2022-04-29', 5, 0, 2, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"ARRIVAL DELHI - MUSSOORIE\",\"date\":\"29-04-2022 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>Reach Delhi and meet a representative who will help you get transferred to Mussoorie.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Upon reaching Mussoorie, check-in to the hotel and take some rest.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Later in the evening, you can explore around the hotel or take a stroll across the pretty streets and landscapes of the hill station.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Return back to the hotel.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Overnight stay in Mussoorie.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"MUSSOORIE LOCAL SIGHTSEEING\",\"date\":\"30-04-2022 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>After having a hearty breakfast, head out to explore the beautiful town of Mussoorie.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Visit famous <strong>Kempty waterfalls <\\/strong>which&nbsp;is 15Kms approx. from Mussoorie.It is a popular tourist point in Mussoorie.&nbsp;<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>You can also visit <strong>Cloud Ends<\\/strong> (at your own cost) which is 7Kms approx. from Mussoorie. It is the highest point of Mussoorie offering an awesome view to tourists.&nbsp;<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Have lunch (at your own cost) and visit <strong>Camels Back Road <\\/strong>which is around 3Kms where rocks are shaped like a hump of camel at the end of the road.&nbsp;<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Later visit <strong>Gun Hill Point<\\/strong> which is the second highest point in Mussoorie. You can also enjoy the view through a cable car at your own cost. It offers a complete view of Mussoorie.&nbsp;<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>In the evening visit <strong>Gun hill road <\\/strong>and <strong>mall road<\\/strong> for shopping.&nbsp;<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Return back to your hotel.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Overnight stay in Mussoorie.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"MUSSOORIE SIGHTSEEING - DEHRADUN\",\"date\":\"01-05-2022 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>Wake up early morning in the laps of mountains.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Enjoy a delicious morning breakfast and check-out.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Head out for the sightseeing tour to <strong>Dhanaulti.<\\/strong><\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Visit some of the famous places like <strong>Surkanda Devi Temple<\\/strong>, <strong>Kaudia Forest and Chamba<\\/strong>.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Visit <strong>Eco Park of Dhanaulti <\\/strong>which features a plethora of flora as well as the native Deodar, Oak &amp; Rhododendron trees, also housing endangered birds adding to its natural beauty.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Check-in @ Dehradun Hotel.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Overnight stay in Dehradun.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DEHRADUN - RISHIKESH + HARIDWAR\",\"date\":\"02-05-2022 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>Wake up to a beautiful sunrise, have a delicious breakfast.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Start off for the most exciting day of the tour as you drive your way to Rishikesh &amp; Haridwar.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li><strong>Shivpuri,<\\/strong> <strong>Laxman Jhula<\\/strong> and get face to face with the thrilling rapids in the glaciated Ganga.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><strong>cliff jump<\\/strong> into the cold water of the river and can also enjoy having a bowl of hot Maggi during the short stopover while rafting.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><strong>Chanda devi , Mansa devi <\\/strong>one can take a ropeway to skip walking and get a city view while sitting on the ropeway, it shall be a small ride for Mansa Devi and Chanda devi temple.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><strong>Ganga Aarti at Har ki pauri<\\/strong> where the priests perform prayers with bowls of fire and the ringing of the temple bells.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Return back to Dehradun.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Overnight stay at the hotel in Dehradun.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DEHRADUN LOCAL\",\"date\":\"03-05-2022 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>Visit some of the famous places like <strong>robbers cave<\\/strong> famous for river flows through a narrow, cave like gorge and enjoying views of the disappearing river.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Get the blessing of a positive divine at <strong>Tapkeshwar temple <\\/strong>is one of the most famous temples dedicated to Shiva, situated by the forest side, the main shivalinga at the temple is inside a natural cave.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Reach <strong>Sahastradhara<\\/strong> afterwards which has thousand fold spring famous for its water, take a dip in the water which is said to cure skin diseases.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Get mesmerized after visiting <strong>Buddha Temple<\\/strong> at Clement Town: It is known as one of the biggest Buddhist centers in the country. It is one of those Tibetan temples which is known for its monumental, art-filled stupa &amp; 103-ft. statue of the Buddha.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Don\'t miss a chance to visit the famous Bazar <strong>Paltan Bazar<\\/strong> and check out the various items on display.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Afterwards return back to hotel for overnight stay in Dehradun.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DEHRADUN - DELHI\",\"date\":\"04-05-2022 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>Wake up in the morning, have a hearty breakfast, pack your bags and complete the check-out formalities.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Head out to Delhi and conclude the tour with loads of memories that you can cherish for a lifetime.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"}]', '[{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"752\",\"dep_date\":\"29 Apr 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"29 Apr 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"08:55 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"11:00 AM\",\"fare\":\"8932\"},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"Vistara\",\"fno\":\"753\",\"dep_date\":\"04 May 2022\",\"arv_date\":\"04 May 2022\",\"dep_time\":\"05:55 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"07:40 PM\",\"fare\":\"7667\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"29\\/04\\/2022\",\"city\":\"MUSSOORIE\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL TULIP INN GREEN CASTLE\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE ROOM VALLEY\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"01\\/05\\/2022\",\"rate\":\"12000\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"01\\/05\\/2022\",\"city\":\"DEHRADUN\",\"hotel_name\":\"HOTEL CLARKS COLLECTION\",\"room_type\":\"DELUXE ROOM\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"04\\/05\\/2022\",\"rate\":\"13450\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details