ation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":2}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Train fare <strong>Ex-Ranchi (3AC Class)</strong>.</li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nights</strong> Accommodation in Well appointed Air-Conditioned Room</li>\n	<li>Two bottles of mineral water every day.</li>\n	<li>Buffet/Fixed Menu <strong>Breakfast &amp;&nbsp;Dinner</strong>.</li>\n	<li>Free Wi-Fi to all our in-house guests.</li>\n	<li>All Taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"25\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":5000,\"land_cost\":null,\"hotel_cost\":14000,\"transport_cost\":null},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":19000,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 4750\",\"selling_price\":23750}', 'MZQ/0407/0102023', 23800, 11900, 0, '2023-10-26 09:24:52', '2023-10-28 08:15:03', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `quotation` (`id`, `guest_name`, `ref_name`, `mobile_no`, `email`, `destination`, `tentative_date`, `nights`, `children`, `adults`, `itineraries`, `flights`, `trains`, `hotels`, `terms_conditions`, `children_ages`, `inclusion`, `exclusion`, `payment_policy`, `cancellation_policy`, `costing`, `ref_id`, `total`, `adult_cost`, `child_cost`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_confirmed`, `hide_note`, `other_details`, `is_feedback_sent`, `is_feedback_received`) VALUES
(413, 'MR S PAL', 'MECON', '9470193754', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'EUROPE', '2024-04-29', 15, 0, 4, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Paris\",\"date\":\"29-04-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Welcome to Europamundo! Upon arriving at the airport, we will be waiting to transfer you to your hotel. Check the information boards in the hotel reception area for details of the welcome meeting with your guide and fellow travelers. Welcome to Europamundo! Upon arriving at the airport, we will be waiting to transfer you to your hotel. Check the information boards in the hotel reception area for details of the welcome meeting with your guide and fellow travelers.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Paris\",\"date\":\"30-04-2024 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Transfer to Versailles Palace. Funicular ride included to Montmartre district. City tour in Paris. Early in the morning, we will leave for Versailles, the immense palace of the kings of France. After that, we will return to Paris at lunch time where we provide a transfer to the Montmartre district. We will ascend by funicular to the hill and admire the spectacular view of Paris from the top. This neighborhood is known for its painters, artists, and its cabarets\\u2026 Sit down for lunch and enjoy a magical atmos- phere. Then, a scenic guided tour to discover the history, main boulevards and the breathtaking monuments of Paris will take place. Return to hotel. Optionally you can attend a variety show.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Paris\",\"date\":\"01-05-2024 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Eiffel Tower and boat cruise in the City of Lights. We go to the center of Paris, starting by the Eiffel Tower area. You will have the opportunity to go up to the second floor of this remarkable metal monument (ticket includ- ed). Then, we enjoy a boat cruise along the River Seine, which divides the north of Paris from the south. Enjoy a free afternoon to explore as you choose.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Paris - Lyon\",\"date\":\"02-05-2024 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Vineyards in Beaune and Bourgog- ne region. Funicular ride in Lyon. Today we travel to the center of France, to the Bourgogne region, famous for its wines. Making a stop in SEMUR EN 2,089 \\u20ac 16 days from ZURICH\\/SWITZERLAND FLORENCE\\/ITALY AUXOIS, a small medieval town listed surrounded by im- pressive walls. After this we will visit BEAUNE, located in the center of the Bourgogne region, with its streets full of flowers, hospice and wine museum all points of interest. Continuing on, we will arrive to LYON in the mid-afternoon, the capital of Roman Gallia on the banks of the Rh\\u00f4ne (its historic center has been declared a World Heritage site). We include a funicular climb to Notre Dame de Fourvi\\u00e8re where we have a great view of the city. Enjoy some leisure time to walk around. Part of the groups will be accommodated in Chambery, a city near Lyon. In these cases, we will leave at the end of the afternoon for CHAMBERY and accommodation. We will then have some time early in the morning to visit the capital of Savoy, a medieval-style city with beauti- ful historic center and a large castle.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Lyon - Zurich\",\"date\":\"03-05-2024 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Scenic tour around the lakes and vineyards of Switzerland. A beautiful stage awaits us as we set off for Switzerland. Arrival in GENEVA. The guide will take us to the Palais des Nations (the European headquarters of the United Nations), the beautiful \\u201cJardin Anglais\\u201d (with its quaint flower clock), and the \\u201cJet d\\u00b4Eau\\u201d, the tallest fountain in Europe. After lunch, we will continue travelling through Switzerland by the beautiful Leman and Neuchatel lakes. We will drive the scenic road alongside the three large lakes, with their magnificent vineyards overlooking the mountains. We will stop in NEUCHATEL, where you can enjoy a walk by the lake, the historic town center or visit its beautiful, 10th century castle. We will then head to ZURICH. Arrival in the late afternoon. Note: depending on the number of passengers travelling from Geneva to Z\\u00fcrich, this part of the trip might be done by train - in which case, there will be no stop in Neuchatel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Zurich- Rapperswill- Zurich\",\"date\":\"04-05-2024 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Zurich. Cruise on the Lake Zurich. Train. With our guide, we will have a tour of ZURICH, the most populated city of Switzerland, and the country\\u2019s finan- cial and cultural capital. The city of the banks has twice been declared the city with the best quality of life in the world. Afterwards, we will include a cruise of almost two hours on Lake Z\\u00fcrich. The boat makes brief stops to allow us to see the villages on the way. We get off in RAPPERSWILL, a picturesque little village overlooked by its mediaeval castle. We go back to Zurich by train and appreciate the efficiency and punctuality of the Swiss railways. Note: Depending on the number of travelers, the trans- fers to the center and from the station may be made on public transport.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Zurich - Grindelwald - Lucerne - Zurich\",\"date\":\"05-05-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Admire the fantastic landscapes. Cable car included to Grindelwald. Lunch included. Today\\u00b4s journey has beautiful landscapes with high mountains and lakes. Breathtaking scenery in the region of Interlaken. We will stop in GRINDELWALD where we will have time for a coffee before taking the cable car up to mountain. We will walk along the winding path which will lead us to the suspended bridge. Dare to walk across the bridge amongst the fantastic scenery enjoying glaciers all around us. We will have lunch up in the mountain (included) before heading back down. We continue to LUCERNE, one of the most beautiful cities in Switzerland. In the evening we have time to stroll around, enjoying the city and to have dinner before re- turning to the hotel in Zurich. Note: The guide will offer you the possibility of a full day optional visit, leaving in the morning and, after some free time to discover Lucerne, we take a rotating cable car to reach the top of Mount Titlis. At the alpine summit, at over 3000m above sea level, you will enjoy breathtaking views of the glacier and the Alps.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Zurich - Lugano- Morcote - Milan\",\"date\":\"06-05-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Spectacular alpine landscapes, quaint villages and lakes. We will leave Zurich early in the morning and cut across the Alps in order to reach the Italian-speaking part of Switzerland. Alongside the route we will get to see beautiful lakes and snow-capped mountains. LUGANO. Arrival in the cosmopolitan capital of the Italian Swit- zerland built next to its beautiful lake. Time to have a stroll and grab lunch. Next, we will reach the enchant- ing little town of MORCOTE famous for its flowery stone houses. We will then travel to Italy. Arrival in MILAN where the guide will take us to the impressive Duomo Square. Here you will find a variety of local and inter- national restaurants to have dinner at. Transfer to the hotel. ROME\\/ITALY LUCERNE\\/SWITZERLAND.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":9,\"index\":8,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Milan- Pisa- Rome\",\"date\":\"07-05-2024 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Coast of Liguria, Leaning Tower of Pisa. Today we continue our journey towards PISA. On a little tourist train, we will travel to the Piazza Dei Miracoli (Square of Miracles), where there will be time to admire one of the most alluring and beautiful art complexes in Italy, including the well-known Leaning Tower of Pisa. Then, we continue to ROME, arriving at the end of the day.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":10,\"index\":9,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Rome\",\"date\":\"08-05-2024 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>City tour of Rome. Imperial Forums (admission price included). Evening transfer to the Trastevere area. In the morning, we have a scenic tour, which will be a great introduction to \\u201cThe Eternal city\\u201d. We will visit the tiny state of the Vatican, the epicenter of Christianity in the world. You will be able to visit St. Peter\\u2019s Basilica. We include the entrance to the Imperial Forums, an im - pressive architectural complex formed by monumental buildings and squares, center of the political activity of Imperial Rome. At the end of the evening we arrange a transfer to Trastevere area for a stroll in the narrow cobbled streets of the district with hidden treasures, such as some modest medieval churches, small shops with the most peculiar of objects or scenes of daily life. Many trattorias (informal Italian eating establishments) and osterias (inns) imbued with the Italian spirit will be ready to serve you local dishes. Other restaurants serving Indian, Chinese and international food can be found in this area. Return to hotel. Note: on many occasions during the low season, as well as in some specific dates of the rest of the year, instead of the entrance to the Imperial Forums, we will enter the Roman Colosseum, symbol of Rome.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":11,\"index\":10,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Rome - Florence\",\"date\":\"09-05-2024 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Tour with a local expert from Florence. View from Piazzale Michelangelo. Today we will leave Rome, heading north. This route has beautiful landscapes. Arriving in FLORENCE, we head straight to the impressive Piazzale Michelange - lo. In the evening we take a tour with a local expert, walking through the historic center, taking in places such as the Ponte Vecchio, the Duomo, and Plaza del - la Signoria. This city is truly an outdoor museum. Enjoy some leisure time to explore. In the evening you will have time for dinner, as, in this district you can find many restaurants serving international cuisine.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":12,\"index\":11,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Florence - Venice\",\"date\":\"10-05-2024 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Boat on Venice\\u2019s Canal. Visit and admission to the St. Mark\\u00b4s Basilica. Admire the technique of crafting Murano Glass . Today we enjoy stunning mountain landscapes while crossing the Apennine Mountains. We will arrive in VENICE and take the boat and cross the Giudecca to the Island of Venice. With a local guide, we will visit the marvelous St. Mark\\u00b4s Square and enter the Basil - ica (entrance included). Afterwards, we will visit the Murano Glass Factory. It is fascinating to see the tech - nique of how this ancient glass is made. Enjoy some time at leisure to explore. Accommodation in the Me - stre district.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":13,\"index\":12,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Venice - Innsbruck- Kitzbuhel\",\"date\":\"11-05-2024 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Breathtaking landscapes. Dinner included. We will depart from Venice, travelling to Austria! Ar - rival in INNSBRUCK, time to stroll in the historic city center and have lunch. After this, we travel along a very beautiful scenic road between the mountains to KITZB\\u00dcHEL \\u2013 Arrival and time to see this picturesque little village, a famous ski resort where we can enjoy the snow for most of the year! Free time. Dinner includ - ed (vegetarian option available).<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":14,\"index\":13,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kitzbuhel- Salzburg - St. Wolfgang- Traunsee Lake- Vienna\",\"date\":\"12-05-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Alpine cable car. Salzburg, the city of Mozart. Fantastic scenery. Cruise on a lake. Departing in the morning, we include a cable car ride in Steinplatte up to the high mountains in the alpine region, with snow 9 months a year and fantastic scen - ery. The great landscapes on the platform in the void and the exhibition of dinosaurs will leave us unfor - gettable memories. We will continue to explore Aus - tria, traveling between the mountains, and arriving in SALZBURG. Our guide will accompany us through the beautiful streets of this city\\u2019s historic center, declared a World Heritage site. We make our way between lakes and mountains in the next stage. Our next stop is in ST. WOLFGANG, a famous place of pilgrimage in Aus - tria. We continue to TRAUNKIRCHEN with its beautiful Traunsee Lake, where we take a cruise to see four cas - disembarking in GMUNDEN. After this we contin- ue to VIENNA, arriving in the evening.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":15,\"index\":14,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Vienna\",\"date\":\"13-05-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Vienna city tour. Gardens of the immense Sch\\u00f6nbrunn Palace. Today we take a scenic visit around this impressive city with a local expert. Here we experience its majestic avenues, its palaces and the vibrant city center. Then we head directly to Sch\\u00f6nbrunn Palace, where visitors can stroll around and enjoy its beautiful gardens. After lunch, enjoy an afternoon of leisure in the city center. In the evening we include a transfer to the neighborhood of Grinzing, an old wine-growing village annexed to the city and known for its traditional taverns. Free time to dine in one of its typical restaurants.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":16,\"index\":15,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Viena\",\"date\":\"14-05-2024 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast, end of our services.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Paris (CDG)\",\"name\":\"AirIndia\",\"fno\":\"143\",\"dep_date\":\"29 Apr 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"29 Apr 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"12:50 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:30 PM\",\"fare\":115476},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Vienna (VIE)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"AirIndia\",\"fno\":\"154\",\"dep_date\":\"14 May 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"15 May 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"08:30 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"07:10 AM\",\"fare\":106360}]', '[]', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <strong>Ex-Delhi.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>15 Nights </strong>Accomodation on Double Sharing basis in <strong>3* Deluxe Hotels</strong>.</li>\n	<li>All <strong>Breakfast.</strong></li>\n	<li>Travel by bus with English speaking guide, basic travel insurance, hotel, and breakfast buffet.</li>\n	<li>Includes Arrival transfer</li>\n	<li>City tour in: PARIS, ROME, FLORENCE, VENICE, VIENNA</li>\n	<li>Excursion: Versailles in Paris (entrance not included)</li>\n	<li>Boat: River Seine in Paris, Zurich lake, to the island of Venice, Traunsee lake in Traunkirchen</li>\n	<li>Evening transfer: Trastevere in Rome, Grinzing district in Vienna</li>\n	<li>Transfer: Montmartre District in Paris, Versailles Palace in Paris (entrance not included), Piazzale Michelangelo in Florence</li>\n	<li>Ticket admission: 2nd Floor Eiffel Tower in Paris, Imperial Forums of Rome, Saint Mark´s Basilica&nbsp;&nbsp; and Murano Glass Factory in Venice</li>\n	<li>Train: Rapperswil / Zurich, Piazza dei Miracoli in Pisa</li>\n	<li>Funicular: To Montmartre district in Paris, Lyon , Cable Car to Grindelwald First , Steinplatte</li>\n	<li>1 Lunch Included in: LUCERNE • 1 Dinner Included in: KITZBUHEL</li>\n	<li>Schenghen Tourist Visa.</li>\n	<li>Travel Insurance.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"17\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":221836,\"land_cost\":\"790000\",\"visa_cost\":\"60000\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":1071836,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 182212.12\",\"selling_price\":1254048.120000000111758708953857421875}', 'MZQ/0408/0102023', 1270000, 317500, 0, '2023-10-29 09:03:56', '2023-10-29 13:21:50', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(414, 'MR S PAL', 'MECON', '9470193754', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'EUROPE', '2024-04-29', 14, 0, 4, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Welcome to Paris!\",\"date\":\"29-04-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>On arrival, our Tour Manager \\/ Local Representative will meet and<br \\/>\\nwelcome you outside the airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel<br \\/>\\nand check\\u2013in.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Paris, France. (D)<br \\/>\\nNote: Joining direct passenger \\/ NRI can check-in on your own at<br \\/>\\nthe hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to<br \\/>\\nproceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case<br \\/>\\nof late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guided city tour \\u2013 Eiffel Tower (2nd level) \\u2013 Fragonard Museum \\u2013 Illumination tour of Paris \\u2013 Seine river cruise\",\"date\":\"30-04-2024 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we proceed for a guided city tour of Paris: see the Alexander<br \\/>\\nBridge, Arc de Triumph, Concorde Square, Opera House, Invalides,<br \\/>\\nChamps Elysees and much more. Later, we visit the Eiffel Tower<br \\/>\\n(2nd level). Then visit the famous Fragonard perfume museum.<br \\/>\\nIn the evening enjoy a cruise on the Seine river along with an<br \\/>\\n\\u201cIllumination Tour of Paris\\u201d and see Paris by night, with some of<br \\/>\\nthe city\\u2019s famous monuments \\/ sights lit up.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Paris, France. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Disneyland\\u00ae Paris (01 Day 01 Park)\",\"date\":\"01-05-2024 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we proceed to Disneyland\\u00ae Paris where you can visit<br \\/>\\nDisneyland\\u00ae Park OR Walt Disney Studios\\u00ae Park (Up to 5 Hours<br \\/>\\nvisit). Get charmed by Sleeping Beauty Castle, enjoy exciting<br \\/>\\nrollercoaster rides, meet Alice in Wonderland, Pinocchio and<br \\/>\\nothers in Fantasyland as well as travelling to the four corners of<br \\/>\\nthe globe in Adventureland.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Paris, France. (B, D)<br \\/>\\nNote: \\u2022 Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may<br \\/>\\ntake up to 4 \\u2013 5 hours in the queue.<br \\/>\\n\\u2022 Due to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, city tours may not<br \\/>\\ntake place for several groups in case of road closures for rehearsals<br \\/>\\n\\/ events that would be taking place from 11th July, 2024 to 23rd<br \\/>\\nSeptember, 2024.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Orientation tour of Brussels \\u2013 Photo stop at Atomium\",\"date\":\"02-05-2024 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we drive to Brussels. On arrival, enjoy an orientation tour.<br \\/>\\nSee the Grand Place and the legendary Manneken Pis statue. Later,<br \\/>\\nwe have a photo stop at the Atomium.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Belgium \\/ Netherlands. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Keukenhof \\u2013 Cheese Farm & Wooden Shoe Workshop \\u2013 Dam Square\",\"date\":\"03-05-2024 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>the world. Next, we visit a cheese farm and wooden shoe factory.<br \\/>\\nLater, we visit the famous Dam Square: see the Royal Palace,<br \\/>\\nNieuwe Kerk and War Memorial.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Belgium \\/ Netherlands. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Or<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Today, we proceed to Madurodam \\u2013 Holland in Miniature Park.<br \\/>\\nNext, we visit a cheese farm and wooden shoe factory. Later, we<br \\/>\\nvisit the famous Dam Square: see the Royal Palace, Nieuwe Kerk<br \\/>\\nand War Memorial.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Belgium \\/ Netherlands. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Cologne Cathedral \\u2013 Rhine river cruise\",\"date\":\"04-05-2024 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we drive to Cologne to visit the Cologne Cathedral. Later,<br \\/>\\nwe enjoy a scenic cruise on the River Rhine.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Germany. (B, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Visit Black Forest \\u2013 View the Rhine Falls\",\"date\":\"05-05-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we drive to Titisee and visit the heart of Black Forest, its<br \\/>\\ndense, evergreen forests &amp; picturesque villages. Next, we drive to<br \\/>\\nSchaffhausen to see the Rhine Falls.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Zurich, Switzerland. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Day at leisure OR Excursion to Jungfraujoch with Lunch and Interlaken (Optional)\",\"date\":\"06-05-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, the day is at leisure OR you can join us for a visit to<br \\/>\\nJungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We take the cable car followed<br \\/>\\nby a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe\\u2019s<br \\/>\\nhighest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx<br \\/>\\nobservatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we<br \\/>\\nvisit Interlaken.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Zurich, Switzerland. (B, D)<br \\/>\\nNote: Guests who do not opt for this Optional excursion will get<br \\/>\\npacked dinner delivered at the hotel when the group arrives.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":9,\"index\":8,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Visit Mt. Titlis \\u2013 Orientation tour of Lucerne \\u2013 Onto St. Moritz\",\"date\":\"07-05-2024 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we visit Mt Titlis. Our cable car ride includes the world\\u2019s<br \\/>\\nfirst rotating cable car, the Rotair \\u2013 to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020<br \\/>\\nmetres. Do visit the \\u201cCliff Walk\\u201d a suspension bridge along the cliff<br \\/>\\nof Mt. Titlis. Next, we proceed for an orientation tour of Lucerne:<br \\/>\\nSee the Lion Monument, and Kapellbrucke with some free time to<br \\/>\\nshop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates. Later, drive<br \\/>\\nto St Moritz, a luxurious alpine holiday resort of the world\\u2019s rich and<br \\/>\\nfamous, situated at an elevation of 1856 meters above sea level.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in St Moritz, Switzerland. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":10,\"index\":9,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"St. Moritz \\u2013 Mt. Diavolezza \\u2013 Horse Carriage ride\",\"date\":\"08-05-2024 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we proceed to the train station to board the train. Travel<br \\/>\\non the famous Bernina route to Diavolezza. Proceed by cable car<br \\/>\\nto scintillating Mt. Diavolezza summit of 2973 meters \\/ 9754 feet<br \\/>\\nabove sea level. Enjoy a breathtaking view of the Engadine range<br \\/>\\nof the Swiss Alps and the highest peak of the Eastern Alps \\u2013 Piz<br \\/>\\nBernina. Later proceed back to your hotel where you have some<br \\/>\\nfree time to explore the beautiful and rich town of Mt. Moritz<br \\/>\\nLater, we take you for a fascinating horse carriage ride.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in St. Moritz, Switzerland. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":11,\"index\":10,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Orientation tour of Innsbruck \\u2013 Swarovski Crystal Museum and shop\",\"date\":\"09-05-2024 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we drive to Innsbruck. On arrival, we enjoy an orientation<br \\/>\\ntour: see the Golden Roof and the Maria Theresien Strasse. Later<br \\/>\\nwe visit the Swarovski Crystal Museum and shop in Wattens.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Innsbruck \\/ Seefeld, Austria. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":12,\"index\":11,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Orientation tour of Venice\",\"date\":\"10-05-2024 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we drive to Italy and proceed to the pier to take a private<br \\/>\\nboat to Venice. On arrival, we visit St. Mark\\u2019s square to see the<br \\/>\\nBasilica, Doge\\u2019s Palace, Campanile and Bridge of Sighs.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Padova \\/ Ferrara, Italy. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":13,\"index\":12,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Guided city tour of Florence\",\"date\":\"11-05-2024 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we proceed to Florence for a guided walking tour: see the<br \\/>\\nDuomo, the Campanile, the Baptistery with its Gates of Paradise<br \\/>\\nand Piazza Della Signoria.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Chianciano Terme, Italy. (B, LL, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":14,\"index\":13,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Day trip to Rome - Guided tour of Vatican Museum and Sistine Chapel Guided city tour of Rome\",\"date\":\"12-05-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we go on a day trip to Rome. On arrival, we proceed for<br \\/>\\na guided city tour of Vatican &amp; Rome: Enter the Vatican City \\u2013<br \\/>\\nthe smallest country in the world (shorts or sleeveless vests not<br \\/>\\nallowed) including a visit to the Vatican Museum, Sistine Chapel,<br \\/>\\nSt. Peter\\u2019s Basilica and St. Peter\\u2019s Square. Next, we continue with<br \\/>\\nthe guided city tour of Rome: See Circus Maximus and photo-stop<br \\/>\\nat Colosseum &amp; Arc of Constantine.<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Chianciano Terme, Italy. (B, L, D)<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":15,\"index\":14,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"See Leaning Tower of Pisa \\u2013 Fly back home with pleasant memories!\",\"date\":\"13-05-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we proceed to Pisa to see the world-famous leaning tower<br \\/>\\nof Pisa. Later, we drive to Milan airport for your flight back home.<br \\/>\\nKindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour<br \\/>\\nManager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive<br \\/>\\nhome with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are<br \\/>\\nsure you will treasure for a lifetime. (B)<br \\/>\\nNote: \\u2022Due to flight connectivity, few groups may depart out of<br \\/>\\nRome instead of Milan. Kindly check with your sales staff for your<br \\/>\\nexact flight details.<br \\/>\\n\\u2022In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches<br \\/>\\nand it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour.<br \\/>\\nYour Tour Manager will try his\\/her best to stop coach wherever<br \\/>\\npossible for a photo stop.<br \\/>\\n\\u2022 Due to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, the hotel in Paris<br \\/>\\nmay be at the outskirts of the city and may attract extra surcharge.<br \\/>\\n(1st July 2024 \\u2013 31st September 2024)<\\/p>\"}]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">AIRLINE AND AIRFARE</span></span></strong></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 29<sup>th</sup> &nbsp;&nbsp;Oct, 2023.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged bythe airline will have to be borne by the passengers.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by thepassengers themselves</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">HOTELS</span></span></strong></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• All hotels will be either around the airport area or on theoutskirts.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Most hotel rooms in Europe may not be air conditioned / aircooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• The average room size of the hotels in Europe are between 16 –20 sq.mts</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Any damage caused to the hotel rooms during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">COACHES</span></span></strong></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Eating &amp; drinking is not permitted on the coach.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board alight from the coach.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">MEALS</span></span></strong></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">SIGHTSEEING</span></span></strong></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse theitinerary. However, all the services/ inclusions will remain the same.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It isadvisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• In the case of missing a paid entrance due to sudden closure or non-availability the same will be replaced by another visit of similar value and / or type or a refund will be provided.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">GENERAL</span></span></strong></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. </span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expensemust be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train,airplane, bus, ship or other services.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amendthe itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure,excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc.not utilized on your tour.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the TourManager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cashin the currency as mentioned in your tour price only. (Credit or&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Debit cards not accepted).</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Optional tours are booked &amp; paid on 100% non-refundable &amp; noncancellation policy.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will beadvised once the same is confirmed.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• The images used in this brochure are for representation purposesonly.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of thetour cost will be paid in the currency as mentioned in your touprice out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">• Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\">&nbsp;</p>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <strong>Ex-Delhi.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>15 Nights </strong>Accomodation on Double Sharing basis in <strong>3* Deluxe Hotels</strong>.</li>\n	<li>All <strong>Breakfast at Hotels.</strong></li>\n	<li>All local taxes and services as of 1st September 2023.</li>\n	<li>All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.</li>\n	<li>Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).</li>\n	<li>Schenghen Tourist Visa.</li>\n	<li>Travel Insurance.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on&nbsp; later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates &amp; ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned on 30 Days prior to departure date.</li>\n	<li>Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel &amp; Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 15 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 45 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.</li>\n	<li>Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.</li>\n	<li>Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st September 2023)</li>\n	<li>Government Taxes as applicable are extra.</li>\n	<li>The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.</li>\n	<li>No porterage included.</li>\n	<li>Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regula menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.</li>\n	<li>Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.</li>\n	<li>Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in you itinerary.</li>\n	<li>Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.</li>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"17\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":0,\"land_cost\":\"790000\",\"visa_cost\":\"60000\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":850000,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 144500\",\"selling_price\":994500}', 'MZQ/0409/0102023', 1496000, 374000, 0, '2023-10-29 13:51:31', '2023-10-29 14:03:35', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(415, 'MR SAKET SARAF', 'BNI EXPLORERS', '9835574327', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'MALAYSIA', '2023-12-26', 6, 3, 4, '[]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Kuala-lumpur (KUL)\",\"name\":\"AirAsia Airways\",\"fno\":\"62\",\"dep_date\":\"26 Dec 2023\",\"arv_date\":\"26 Dec 2023\",\"dep_time\":\"01:05 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"07:35 AM\",\"fare\":\"109667\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Kuala-lumpur (KUL)\",\"to\":\"Langkawi (LGK)\",\"name\":\"AirAsia Airways\",\"fno\":\"6302\",\"dep_date\":\"28 Dec 2023\",\"arv_date\":\"28 Dec 2023\",\"dep_time\":\"05:15 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:20 PM\",\"fare\":\"39000\"},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Langkawi (LGK)\",\"to\":\"Kuala-lumpur (KUL)\",\"name\":\"AirAsia Airways\",\"fno\":\"6329\",\"dep_date\":\"30 Dec 2023\",\"arv_date\":\"30 Dec 2023\",\"dep_time\":\"02:35 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"03:50 PM\",\"fare\":\"44001\"},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Kuala-lumpur (KUL)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"AirAsia Airways\",\"fno\":\"63\",\"dep_date\":\"01 Jan 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"02 Jan 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"10:55 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"12:20 AM\",\"fare\":\"97409\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"26\\/12\\/2023\",\"city\":\"GENTING\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Grand Ion Delemen 5*\",\"room_type\":\"One Bedroom Suite\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"28\\/12\\/2023\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"28\\/12\\/2023\",\"city\":\"LANGKAWI\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Berjaya Langkawi Resort 5*\",\"room_type\":\"Rainforest Studio\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"30\\/12\\/2023\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"30\\/12\\/2023\",\"city\":\"KUALALUMPUR\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Pullman 5*\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"01\\/01\\/2024\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":7},{\"age\":7},{\"age\":12}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <strong>Ex-Kolkata</strong>.</li>\n	<li><strong>02 Nts </strong>Accomodation on DBl Sharing @ <strong>Genting.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02 Nts</strong> Accomodation on DBl Sharing @ <strong>Langkawi.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02 Nts</strong> Accomodation on DBl Sharing @ <strong>Kualalumpur.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>20 Kgs Checkin Baggage</strong> for all Adults &amp; <strong>Hand Baggage</strong> for Adults &amp; Children.</li>\n	<li>Skytropolis Funland One Day Pass&nbsp;<b>**&nbsp;Ticket Only&nbsp;&nbsp;**</b></li>\n	<li>Under Water World - Tickets&nbsp;<b>**&nbsp;Ticket Only&nbsp;&nbsp;**</b></li>\n	<li>Langkawi Island Hoping&nbsp;<b>**&nbsp;PVT Basis&nbsp;&nbsp;**</b>&nbsp;((Entrance Fee for fresh lake upto 10 MYR is to be paid directly on tour) + Transfers &amp; Boat trip to Pregnant Maiden Island, Beras Basah Island &amp; Singa Besar Island on Seat In Coach Boat)</li>\n	<li>Half Day Langkawi Island Tour&nbsp;<b>**&nbsp;PVT Basis&nbsp;&nbsp;**</b>&nbsp;(Excludes Entrance Fee)</li>\n	<li>Batu Caves ( 20 Min Photo Stop )&nbsp;<b>**&nbsp;Ticket Only&nbsp;&nbsp;**</b></li>\n	<li>Half Day City Tour With Kl Tower&nbsp;<b>**&nbsp;PVT Basis&nbsp;&nbsp;**</b></li>\n	<li>Genting Cable Car (two Way)&nbsp;<b>**&nbsp;Ticket Only&nbsp;&nbsp;**</b></li>\n	<li>All <strong>Airport Transfers </strong>on PVT basis.</li>\n	<li>Malaysia <strong>Tourist Visa</strong>.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"16\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":290077,\"land_cost\":\"249985\",\"visa_cost\":\"24500\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":564562,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 90329.92\",\"selling_price\":654891.920000000041909515857696533203125}', 'MZQ/0410/0102023', 654800, 107000, 75600, '2023-10-31 07:18:59', '2023-10-31 07:27:33', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
