, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":7}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airfare <em><strong>Ranchi-Kolkata-Singapore-Kualalumpur-Kolkata.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><em><strong>20 Kgs Check-in Baggage </strong>for Air Asia Flight <strong>KUL-CCU.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><strong>All Airport Transfers&nbsp;- PVT</strong><b>&nbsp;Basis.</b></li>\n	<li><strong>04&nbsp;Nights</strong> Accommodation in <strong>Hotel V Lavender</strong>, Singapore.</li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nights</strong> Accommodation in <strong>Hotel Berjaya Times Square</strong>, Kualalumpur.</li>\n	<li>All <strong>Breakfasts.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Singapore Guided City Tour&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Universal Studios&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><b>Night Safari&nbsp;</b>(Complimentary Animal Show + Tram Ride)</li>\n	<li><strong>Gardens by the Bay -&nbsp;Flower Dome</strong> (Including Impressions of Monet: The Experience) + <strong>Cloud Forest&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Sentosa Island -&nbsp;</strong>Cable Car + WOT + S.E.A Aquarium + Sky Helix&nbsp;</li>\n	<li><strong>Marina Bay Sands</strong> SkyPark Observation Deck</li>\n	<li><strong>Full-Day Genting Tour </strong>with En-Route Batucaves + Two-Way Cable Car.</li>\n	<li><strong>Kuala Lumpur Night Tour</strong> with KL Tower Observation Deck.</li>\n	<li><em><strong>01 Coach Ticket Singapore- Kualalumpur.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><strong>Malaysia &amp; Singapore Visa</strong>.</li>\n	<li>All Taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"22\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":111809,\"hotel_cost\":73458,\"transport_cost\":null,\"visa_cost\":\"8950\",\"land_cost\":\"74230\"},\"extra\":[{\"name\":\"KUL LAND\",\"amount\":\"20740\"}],\"cost_price\":289187,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 63621.14\",\"selling_price\":352808.140000000013969838619232177734375}', 'MZQ/0579/0102024', 353862, 117954, 117954, '2024-10-02 13:33:48', '2024-10-24 07:59:49', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(589, 'Mr. Rakesh Mohan', 'CDG', '9810621916', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'Srilanka 4*', '2024-12-10', 6, 0, 4, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"AIRPORT TO KANDY\",\"date\":\"10-12-2024 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>AIRPORT TO KANDY<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Arrive at Bandaranaike International Airport, met by Our representative, proceed to Kandy, En route visit Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage and Spice garden<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>ELEPHANT ORPHANAGE<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>The orphanage was originally founded to afford care and protection to the many orphaned Elephants found in the jungles of Sri Lanka. The elephants are taken to the river twice a day for a bath, and all the babies less than three years of age are still bottle-fed by the mahouts and volunteers.&nbsp; The main attraction is clearly to observe the elephants bathing which is quite a spectacle.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>SPICE HERBAL GARDEN&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Where aromas of cinnamon, cardamom, nutmeg, pepper, and mace romanticize the air, tantalizing the senses \\u2013 a spice garden is what it is; giving every visitor an in-depth view of an ancient spice-producing industry; which had enticed many Arab and European traders who docked at every port of ancient Ceylon. Some gardens offer Ayurveda massages with oils made with herbs and spices for complete rejuvenation and relaxation which could be ideal for the tired visitor.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Next, proceed to the hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Dinner and Overnight stay at Hotel in Kandy.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"KANDY CITY TOUR\",\"date\":\"11-12-2024 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Kandy<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Breakfast at the Hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Next visit the Temple of Tooth, Gem museum, Kandy city tour, Kandy viewpoint, and the&nbsp; Cultural Show.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>TEMPLE OF TOOTH RELIC OF LORD BUDDHA<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Temple of the Tooth Brief History of the Temple of the Sacred Tooth Relic is a world-renowned place of worship, where the left Canine tooth of Gautama Buddha is enshrined. This temple was named a world heritage by UNESCO in 1988.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>LOAD KADHIRAGAMAN TEMPLE \\u2013 KANDY<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Kartikeya, also known as Murugan, Skanda, Kumara, and Subrahmanya, is the Hindu god of war. He is the son of Parvati and Shiva, brother of Ganesha, and a god whose life story has many versions in Hinduism. An important deity around South Asia since ancient times, Kartikeya is particularly popular and predominantly worshipped in South India and Sri Lanka as Murugan.Kartikeya is an ancient god, traceable to the Vedic era. Archaeological evidence from 1st-century CE and earlier, where he is found with Hindu god Agni , suggests that he was a significant deity in early Hinduism. He is found in many medieval temples all over India, such as at the Ellora Caves and Elephanta Caves.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>GEM MUSEUM<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;All the visitors to the exclusive geological gem museum are invariably given an A to Z knowledge on how Sri Lanka originated 4.6 billion years ago engulfing the wonderful minerals and gemstones outshining the ones in other parts of the world. in the museum, you will see the rarest minerals in the world located and found in Sri Lanka, and also the oldest fossils of living beings which originated in the Cambrian (541-485 million years) Era.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Kandy City Tour<\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Including Gem Museum Art and Craft Center,<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Upper Lake Drive (boat ride across the lake)<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The market<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p>Next, Enjoy a Cultural Show<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>The Kandy CULTURAL SHOW is a popular traditional performance in Sri Lanka, often held in Kandy, a city known for its rich cultural heritage. The show typically features traditional music, drumming, dance, and other forms of cultural expression, providing visitors with a glimpse into Sri Lanka\'s vibrant cultural traditions. It\'s a must-see for tourists interested in experiencing the country\'s cultural heritage<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>KANDY VIEWPOINT<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Kandy\\u2018s viewpoint is regarded as the highest point in the city. Visiting Kandy Viewpoint is not just about its picturesque beauty but also provides a quick simple adventure - a short hike through the steep slopes on the way to Kandy Viewpoint to admire the magnificent panoramic view of the surroundings with an occasional misty breeze.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Dinner and Overnight stay at Hotel in Kandy.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"KANDY - NUWARA ELIYA\",\"date\":\"12-12-2024 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Breakfast at the Hotel. Leave for Nuwara Eliya En route&nbsp; visit Bhakta Hanuman Temple, Ramboda falls, the Tea factory &amp; Tea plantation.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>PERADENIYA&nbsp; BOTANICAL GARDEN<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Royal Botanical Gardens in Peradeniya are the oldest formal garden in Sri Lanka. The garden includes more than 4000 species of plants, including orchids, spices, medicinal plants, and palm trees, and is renowned for its collection of orchids and the long, palm-framed pathways. It is managed by the Division of National Botanic Gardens of the Department of Agriculture and the National Herbarium of Sri Lanka is attached to it as well. It encompasses a total area of 147 acre<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Next<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>BHAKTA HANUMAN TEMPLE<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>It is believed that Hanuman was searching for Sita Devi and still there are some Ramayana facts available in this area e.g. a village called \\u201cRavana Goda\\u201d close to this Bhakta Hanuman Temple. The Tamil word for Ramboda, Rampadai, means \\u201cRama\\u2019s force\\u201d. Also, it is believed this was the place where Lord Hanuman took a rest while on his way to search Sita as per the Ramayana yatra Sri Lanka.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>RAMBODA FALLS<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Ramboda oya, which flows majestically through Ramboda valley creates this beautiful trilogy of waterfalls within the perimeter of a few kilometers, closer to Colombo \\u2013 Kandy \\u2013 Nuwara Eliya main road.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>VISIT TEA FACTORY AND PLANTATIONS<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Nuwara Eliya is the best-known tea-growing district of Sri Lanka with its impressive lush green tea plantations. When you visit Sri Lanka, you can\\u2019t miss exploring its incredible tea plantations and learning about tea production.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Nuwara Eliya City tour<\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Sri Lanka\\u2019s oldest post offices<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>colonial buildings<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>St. Xavier\\u2019s Church,<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Victoria Park<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Nuwara Eliya Race Course<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Lake Gregory<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>paddle boats and other water sports<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p><strong>Dinner and Overnight stay at Hotel in Nuwara Eliya.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"NUWARA ELIYA  -  BENTOTA\",\"date\":\"13-12-2024 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Breakfast at the Hotel. Next visit Sita Amman Temple, Ashoka Vathika and&nbsp; Nuwara Eliya City tour<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>SITA AMMAN TEMPLE<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>With reference to the Ramayana proof of Sri Lanka it is believed that the Sita devi was kept captive at this site by King Ravana. There is a stream by the side of the temple where that runs from the hill, catered to the needs of Sita Devi during her stay at Ashok Vatika. She is also said to have bathed in this stream. About a century ago of three idols were discovered in the stream. The soil here is black in colour. According to the epic of Ramayana it is the believed that Hanumanji burnt this area before he left Sri Lanka. The foot prints of Lord Hanuman\\u2019s can be seen even today.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>ASHOKAVANAM \\/ ASHOK VATIKA<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Ashok Vatika is one of the significant places mentioned in Ramayana Yatra Sri Lanka. Ashoka Vatika is the place where Sita Devi was in captivity under Sri Lankan king Ravana during Ramayana yatra in Sri Lanka. She was preferred to stay in this garden instead of at Ravana\\u2019s majestic castle. There was a wonderful Ashoka tree here, which provided the distressed Sita, shelter and comfort. It is believed that the considerable area of Ashok Vatika were burnt and destroyed by monkey god Hanuman when he arrived in the island and found the lost princess Sita Devi. Sita Devi was in Ashok Vatika until end of the battle between Ravana &amp; Rama which resulted in the death of Ravana, the Sri Lankan King.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Dinner and Overnight stay at Hotel in Bentota.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"BENTOTA - CITY AREA & GALLE\",\"date\":\"14-12-2024 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Bentota to Colombo. Breakfast at the Hotel and Leave for City tour of Bentota<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Optional water sports and Bentota beaches.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>WATER SPORTS ACTIVITIES - OPTIONAL<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>From serene lagoons and a gentle river to a coral-laden coastline, Bentota is Lanka\\u2019s best destination for water sports on the west coast. One can enjoy exhilarating river cruises, diving, snorkeling, water skiing, speed boating, kitesurfing, windsurfing, banana boating, and tubing on Bentota Beach, Aturuwella, and Bentota River. In addition, there are several institutions, like Bentota Water Sports Centre, and River Adventures, offering tandem courses and guides.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Next<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>MADHU RIVER WITH SAFARI<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>The Madu Ganga and Bentota River safari reward you with an enthralling experience. As you sail through the rippling waters, watch out for water monitors, blue-eyed cormorants perched atop floating branches, fruit bats hanging asleep, upside down, and the endearing sight of infant monkeys clinging onto fishermen as they sail across the river on narrowboats. You might even spot a few crocodiles and water snakes along your jungle cruise.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>TURTLE HATCHERY<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Turtle Hatchery was started by the Sri Lankans to protect the turtles from extinction With the commencement of the Turtle Hatchery, these eggs were fed and cared for until they were 2 to 4 years old. You can find different species of turtles such as Green Turtle, Leatherback, and Olive Ridley.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Proceed to Galle.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>GALLE FORT<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Built several years ago on a massive piece of land in Galle, the Galle Dutch Fort was used by the Portuguese until the Dutch took over it. The British finally sealed the fort as theirs with a lot of rebuilding and renovation. The unique blends that led to the standing of this monumental structure are now listed under the UNESCO World Heritage Sites thus deserving a substantial place on the list of places to visit in Galle.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>GALLE LIGHTHOUSE<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Nestled in the premise of the Galle Dutch Fort, the Galle Lighthouse is an imperial beauty. The captivating architecture, tall building , and the breeze it echoes are all unforgettable scenes that even a camera cannot capture at its best. One can see the far-off oceans that face the lighthouse, which is factually the oldest one in the country. It was a sigh of relief for ancient mariners and is a scintillating sight for tourists today.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>ARIYAPALA MASK MUSEUM<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Ariyapala Mask Museum is the ultimate place to explore in Sri Lanka, especially for artists. As said before, Ambalangoda is a town that is reviving the old forms of making masks, this museum is one of those places where you can admire different kinds of masks and puppets. Falling in different price ranges, there are masks that one can buy easily without burning a hole in the pocket. You will also find a gift shop where you can buy gifts for your family and friends.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>MEETHIYAGODA MOONSTONE<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Discover this ancient moonstone mine shrouded by the lush jungles of Mitiyagoda. Learn the fascinating process of how moon stones are mined and filtered before being shined and sold.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Returned Hotel in Bentota.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Dinner and Overnight stay at Hotel in&nbsp; Bentota<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"BENTOTA  - COLOMBO\",\"date\":\"15-12-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After Breakfast Leave for Colombo.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>COLOMBO CITY TOUR<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>While on your city tour in Colombo, you may visit famous places including<\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Galle Face Green,<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Kovil<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Viharamahadevi Park,<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>National Museum,<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Twin World Trade Center towers,<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Old Parliament Building,<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Fort district,<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Independence Hall at Independence Square and<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>prominent Buddhist, Hindu, Islam, and Christian places of worship. (Entrance fees to sites not included).<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p>For shopping, you may visit Odel, House of Fashion, Beverly Street, Majestic City, Noritake, etc.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Late evening enjoys the night life Colombo visiting Casino and Pubs in Colombo.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Dinner and Overnight stay at Hotel in&nbsp; Colombo.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DEPARTURE COLOMBO\",\"date\":\"16-12-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast leave for&nbsp;Airport for Departure.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Bangalore (BLR)\",\"to\":\"Colombo (CMB)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"1167\",\"dep_date\":\"10 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"10 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"11:20 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"12:55 PM\",\"fare\":75628},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Colombo (CMB)\",\"to\":\"Bangalore (BLR)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"1168\",\"dep_date\":\"16 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"16 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"01:55 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"03:20 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"10\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"Kandy\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Royal Kandyan\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"12\\/12\\/2024\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"12\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"N\\u2019 ELIYA\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Oakray Tea Bush\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"13\\/12\\/2024\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"13\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"BENTOTA\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel The Palms\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"15\\/12\\/2024\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"15\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"COLOMBO\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Pegasus Reef\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"16\\/12\\/2024\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airfare<strong> Ex-Bengaluru.</strong></li>\n	<li>Airport <strong>Pick up &amp; Drop.</strong></li>\n	<li>Meeting arrangements at the airport on arrival and departure.</li>\n	<li>Transfers in an exclusive air conditioned vehicle as per Group Size with English Speaking Chauffeur Guide (See vehicle pictures in end )</li>\n	<li><strong>Hotel Accommodation </strong>as per selected Category</li>\n	<li><strong>Breakfast and Dinner.</strong></li>\n	<li>All Taxes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"12\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":75628,\"land_cost\":\"122060\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":197688,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 23722.56\",\"selling_price\":221410.5599999999976716935634613037109375}', 'MZQ/0580/0102024', 222560, 55640, 0, '2024-10-04 07:35:45', '2024-10-04 08:33:59', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `quotation` (`id`, `guest_name`, `ref_name`, `mobile_no`, `email`, `destination`, `tentative_date`, `nights`, `children`, `adults`, `itineraries`, `flights`, `trains`, `hotels`, `terms_conditions`, `children_ages`, `inclusion`, `exclusion`, `payment_policy`, `cancellation_policy`, `costing`, `ref_id`, `total`, `adult_cost`, `child_cost`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_confirmed`, `hide_note`, `other_details`, `is_feedback_sent`, `is_feedback_received`) VALUES
(590, 'Mr. Amaan', 'Mr. Saddam', '7008827014', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'Manali 3*', '2024-10-27', 4, 0, 10, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Delhi \\u2013 Manali (overnight Volvo bus)\",\"date\":\"27-10-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After you arrive in Delhi, (you are required to reach Kashmiri Gate on your own), you will board the overnight Volvo bus to Manali. (Manali is located at a distance of around 553 km from Delhi).<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Enjoy an overnight journey in a Volvo bus.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Manali Sightseeing\",\"date\":\"28-10-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Pick up from Manali Volvo Bus Stand and transfer to Hotel,check in to Hotel in Manali (Hotel check-in time is 12:00 noon, some time you will get early check-in and some time you have to wait for check-in). After fresh-up take rest in hotel and afternoon Half Day Manali local sightseeing of Manali,visit places like HidimbaTemple,VashishtTemple,Tibetan Monastery, Van Vihar and Manu Temple and after sight-seeing spend some time on Mall Road Manali.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Afterward, return to the hotel for an overnight stay.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Solang Valley Day Trip\",\"date\":\"29-10-2024 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today morning after breakfast full fun in Solang Valley. Dinner &amp; overnight stay in Manali. SolangNala (Valley) drives its name from combination of words Solang (Nearby village) and Nullah (water stream). It is a side valley at the top of the Kullu Valley in Himachal Pradesh, India 14 km northwest of the resort town Manali on the way to Rohtang Pass, and is known for its summer and winter sport conditions. The sports most commonly offered are Ropeway, parachuting, paragliding, skating and zorbing. Snow melts during the summer months starting May and skiing is then replaced by zorbing (a giant ball with room for 2 people which is rolled down a 200 metre hill), paragliding, parachuting and horse riding.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Afterward, return to the hotel for an overnight stay.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Manali \\u2013 Kullu \\u2013 Manali\",\"date\":\"30-10-2024 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast travel to Nagar halting before Kullu for river rafting and than visit places like Viashno Devi Temple, KulluSahwal factory, Bhuntar, Kasol Valley, nagar art gallery nagar castel and we can do river rafting in beas river.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>overnight stay at the hotel in the evening.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Manali \\u2013 Delhi\",\"date\":\"31-10-2024 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Get ready for some wonderful and exciting shopping in Manali. Some of the famous markets of Manali at Mall Road, Old Manali, and Tibetan Markets. You can purchase shawls, caps, Tibetan carpets, Buddhist paintings and artifacts, dry fruits, apples, pullovers made of yak wool, jellies, jam, and other things in these markets. Later in the evening,<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong>Board your overnight Volvo bus to Delhi.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Delhi\",\"to\":\"Manali\",\"name\":\"By Bus\",\"fno\":\"Volvo\",\"dep_date\":\"27 Oct 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"28 Oct 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"07:45 Pm\",\"arv_time\":\"08:00 Am\",\"fare\":\"40000\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Manali\",\"to\":\"Delhi\",\"name\":\"By Bus\",\"fno\":\"Volvo\",\"dep_date\":\"31 Oct 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"01 Nov 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"05:30 Pm\",\"arv_time\":\"07:30 Am\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"28\\/10\\/2024\",\"city\":\"Manali\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Manali Grand\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":5,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"31\\/10\\/2024\",\"rate\":\"36000\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>RoundTrip Volvo Bus Tickets Ex-Delhi.</li>\n	<li><strong>03 Nights</strong> Accomodation in <strong>Hotel Manali Grand, Manali.&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>05&nbsp;Rooms&nbsp;on DBL Sharing basis.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Breakfast </strong>at respective Hotel.</li>\n	<li>Enjoy a sightseeing tour in Manali.</li>\n	<li>Excursion to Kullu.</li>\n	<li>01 Tempo Traveller for all Sightseeings on PVT.</li>\n	<li>All Taxes</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind o