 Island Tour</strong> with Local Lunch by Speed Boat with Sea Canoe (Excluding National Park Fee) - SIC</li>\n	<li><strong>Krabi 4 Island Tour </strong>with Lunch by Speed Boat (Excluding National Park Fee) - SIC</li>\n	<li><strong>Tiger Kingdom</strong> Medium Tiger - PVT</li>\n	<li><strong>Chaophraya Princess </strong>Dinner Cruise Indian Buffet - PVT</li>\n	<li><strong>Safari World + Marine Park</strong>&nbsp;with Lunch - SIC</li>\n	<li>Phuket Airport to Phuket Hotel on PVT</li>\n	<li>Krabi Hotel to Krabi Airport on PVT</li>\n	<li>Krabi Hotel to Krabi Airport on PVT</li>\n	<li>Don Muang Airport to Bangkok Hotel on PVT</li>\n	<li>Bangkok Hotel To Bangkok Airport on PVT</li>\n	<li>All taxes</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Free <strong>THAILAND Visa</strong> on Ariival&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"25\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":82986,\"hotel_cost\":70400,\"land_cost\":\"51000\",\"transport_cost\":null},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":204386,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 51096.5\",\"selling_price\":255482.5}', 'MZQ/0595/0112024', 255780, 127890, 0, '2024-11-07 12:04:54', '2024-11-09 10:47:05', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `quotation` (`id`, `guest_name`, `ref_name`, `mobile_no`, `email`, `destination`, `tentative_date`, `nights`, `children`, `adults`, `itineraries`, `flights`, `trains`, `hotels`, `terms_conditions`, `children_ages`, `inclusion`, `exclusion`, `payment_policy`, `cancellation_policy`, `costing`, `ref_id`, `total`, `adult_cost`, `child_cost`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_confirmed`, `hide_note`, `other_details`, `is_feedback_sent`, `is_feedback_received`) VALUES
(605, 'Mr Rajeev Ranjan', 'Lupin Maxter', '8405005588', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'SRILANKA', '2024-11-13', 5, 0, 5, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Meet & Pick up at the Airport \\u2013 Transfer to Kandy\",\"date\":\"13-11-2024 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Arrival Colombo &amp; proceed directly for Kandy. After arrival Check-in to Hotel &amp; Relax.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Temple of Tooth \\u2013 Peradeniya Botanical Garden \\u2013 Gem Gallery \\u2013 Cultural Show\",\"date\":\"14-11-2024 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<table>\\n\\t<tbody>\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>KANDY TEMPLE OF TOOTH (1 hrs)<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>(Please Note: No shorts, sleeveless or body revealing attire is allowed)<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The Dalada Maligawa, also known as, the Temple of the Tooth, is one of the landmark sites in the city of Kandy. It is located in the heart of Kandy town surrounded by the lake and the commercial district. The Maligawa was once the royal palace inhabited by the king and his consorts, but after the demise of the Kandyan Kingdom, the palace was transformed into a Buddhist temple that holds Buddha\\u2019s tooth. It is a must-visit location for all tourists. Visitors can catch a glimpse of Buddhist rituals, explore the museum that includes several ancient artifacts, and pay tribute to the tooth relic at one of the Buddhist ceremonies held at the premises. The architectural splendor and the historical importance of the Dalada Maligawa are sure to amaze you. The Aluth Maligawa, Audience Hall and the World Buddhism, Museum are points of interest. Before preparing for your visit, remember that the Maligawa is a Buddhist shrine and you will need to wear attire covering your shoulders and legs.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<h5>The temple is open for devotees every day from 5.30 a.m. till 8.00 p.m. (+0530 GMT)<\\/h5>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<h5>Theva time table<\\/h5>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Morning Service&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; -&nbsp; 5.30 a.m. - 7.00 a.m.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Midday Service&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; -&nbsp; 9.30 a.m - 11.00 a.m.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Evening Service&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; -&nbsp; 6.30 p.m - 8.00 p.m.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>ROYAL BOTANICAL GARDEN (Opening 07:30 AM to 05:00 PM \\/ 01 hrs will be gone for cover)<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Started in 1374 as a pleasure garden of the Kings of Gampola and Kandy.&nbsp; There are more than 4,000 species of trees, plants and creepers. Some rare and endemic as well as flora from the tropical world are found in the gardens.&nbsp; Spice Garden and Orchid House are popular with tourists.There are 5 Palm Avenues beautifying the gardens, the earliest and tallest Palm Avenue (Royal Palm Avenue) was planted in 1905 and the Double Coconuts from the Seashells Island, with the largest seed of all plants in the world are one such avenue.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>GEMS OF SRI LANKA (30 Minutes)<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The world\\u2019s best gems are available in Sri Lanka such as Blue and Yellow Sapphire, Star Ruby and Star Sapphire, Chrysoberyl Cat\\u2019s Eye, Alexandrite, Topaz, Amethyst, Quartz, Garnet, Aquamarine, Moonstone, Tourmaline When comparing with other countries you will be lucky to buy pure and valuable gems at Sri Lanka for a competitive price. You can get the education about gems, making jewelries and other requests with them. You can buy gold, white gold and silver jewelry at your choice. You can even get them Tailor Made as per your preference Evening witness the Cultural Dance Show featuring various dancing types of Sri Lanka\\u2026<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>KANDY CULTURAL SHOW (Starting Time of the Show \\u2013 5:00 PM to 6:00 PM)<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The Kandy Lake Club Cultural Dance Show is a stimulating Sri Lankan Arts, Dance &amp; Cultural Heritage Show that is a must see for any visitor who visits the historic city of Kandy. The Kandy Lake Club Dance started in 1982 with the view of having a cultural dance performance bringing together all Sri Lankan dance types to one platform. It is the first Cultural Dance Show of its kind to be established in Sri Lanka. It has since become a tourist attraction for many people visiting the country and keen on a glimpse of its rich cultural heritage. Hence it has been performing continuously for the last 35 years.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\n\\t<\\/tbody>\\n<\\/table>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Transfer to Bentota \\u2013 En Route Spice Garden at Mawanella \\u2013 En Route Pinnawala Elephant orphanage \\u2013 Checking to the Hotel & Relax\",\"date\":\"15-11-2024 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<table>\\n\\t<tbody>\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>SPICE GARDEN SRI LANKA (OPEN FROM 07:00 AM TO 07:00 PM) 45 MINUTES<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>You will see many spice gardens at Bentota where Cinnamon, Cardamom, Pepper Creepers and all other spice trees, plants and creepers are planted for visitors to see them. Spice products are also available for those who would like to buy them. At all Spice Gardens visitors are taken round explaining each tree and plant and at the end explaining the use of them in food preparations.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>PINNAWALA ELEPHANT ORPHANAGE (from Aiport to Pinnawala 02:15 hrs)<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>App. 55 miles from Colombo, off the Colombo-Kandy Road is Pinnawala, where an orphanage was started in 1975 to house the abandoned and the wounded elephants. The number of elephants has increased to more than 65 now, including Baby Elephants brought from various parts, as well as some of the more than 25 babies born as a result of the captive breeding program. The best time to visit is the feeding time from 0930-1000 hrs. and 1330 1400 hrs. and the bathing time from 1000-1030 hrs. and 1400-1430 hrs. when all the elephants are taken to the river close by.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The Pinnawala Elephant orphanage timetable is laid down as follows for your convenience.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<ul>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>08.30 am \\u2013 Opens for the visitors<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>09.00&nbsp;am \\u2013 09.45&nbsp;am Fruit feeding<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>09.15&nbsp;am \\u2013 09.45&nbsp;am Milk feeding<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>10.00&nbsp;am \\u2013 12.00 pm Herd to the river (Bathing Time)<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>12.00&nbsp;pm \\u2013 01.45&nbsp;pm Fruit feeding<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>01.15&nbsp;pm \\u2013 01.45&nbsp;pm Milk feeding<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>02.00&nbsp;pm \\u2013 04.00&nbsp;pm Herd goes to the river (Bathing Time)<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>05.00&nbsp;pm \\u2013 Milk feeding<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>05.30&nbsp;pm \\u2013 Ticket counter closes<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<li>06.00&nbsp;pm \\u2013 Closes for the day<\\/li>\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/ul>\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\n\\t<\\/tbody>\\n<\\/table>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Madu Ganga Boat Ride \\u2013 Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery \\u2013 Optional Bentota Water Sports\",\"date\":\"16-11-2024 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<table>\\n\\t<tbody>\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>THE MADHU GANGA RIVER LAGOON<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The Madu River Lagoon is popularly known as the Madu Ganga. The town of Balapitiya which lies about 80km from Colombo is the waters-meet for the Madu Ganga. It is located in southwest Sri Lanka. The \\u2018Amarapura Nikaya\\u2019 a Buddhist sect, held its first higher ordination ceremony balanced on a fleet of boats that were anchored, in 1803. The Madu Ganga wetland with its estuary and mangrove islets makes up a coastal wet-land ecosystem. It is home to about 303 species of plants and 248 species of vertebrate animals. It is considered one of the last expanses of immaculate mangrove forests in Sri Lanka. The boat weaves through the dense mangrove forest and surrounding islets, and you can witness the varying species of Mangrove, about 10 of which are endemic to Sri Lanka. On your way, you will also be treated to a view of a wide variety of flora and fauna, such as monitor lizards and a number of beautiful birds. The Mangrove Forest is a vital part of the ecosystem, nourishing and sustaining the environment.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>KOSGODA TURTLE HATCHERY<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Where you can see five species of turtles-Green Turtles (Cheloniamydas), Hawksbill Turtle (Eretmochelysimbricata), Loggerhead Turtle (Carettacaretta), Leatherback Turtle (Dermochelyscoriacea) and Olive Ridley Turtle (Lepidochelysolivacea). The eggs collected by the Villagers and Fishermen are purchased by the Kosgoda Hatchery and kept in sandy pens until they are hatched. The newly hatched ones are kept in seawater tanks and released to the sea in the night. This Hatchery alone has released more than 1,750,000 young turtles to the sea. An endowment by the Hasselblad Estate was responsible for the establishment of this hatchery. The island citizens of these islets produce peeled cinnamon and cinnamon oil and you are sure to have the opportunity to experience this indigenous production.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\n\\t<\\/tbody>\\n<\\/table>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Transfer to Colombo -- Gangarama Temple \\u2013 Lotus Tower \\u2013 Colombo City tour - Shopping Tour \\u2013 Checking to the Hotel & Relax\",\"date\":\"17-11-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<table>\\n\\t<tbody>\\n\\t\\t<tr>\\n\\t\\t\\t<td>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>COLOMBO (2 to 3 HRS)<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Colombo is the business and commercial center and the new capital is Sri Jayewardenepura Kotte, only a few miles away. Colombo was only a small seaport, which came into prominence in the 16th Century with the arrival of the Portuguese in 1505, and the development of it as a major Harbor took place during the British period. Colombo became the capital of Sri Lanka in 1815 after the Kandyan Kingdom was ceded to the British. The remains of the buildings during the period of Portuguese, Dutch, and British rule are found in every area of the city. None of the Portuguese &amp; Dutch fortifications are found today but some of their buildings and churches could be seen in the Fort &amp; Pettah areas.&nbsp; Visit Fort, the former British administrative center and military garrison, Sea Street - the Goldsmith\\u2019s quarters in the heart of Pettah, the Bazaar area where there is also a Hindu Temple with elaborate stone carvings, the Kayman\\u2019s Gate with the Belfry at the original gate to enter the Fort, the Dutch Church of Wolfendhaal dating back to 1749, Kelaniya Buddhist Temple dating to 6th C.B.C., Davatagaha Mosque, Colombo Museum and the Natural History Museum are some of the sites to be visited. Also, visit the BMICH (Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall), see the replica of Avukana Buddha in front, and the Independence Memorial.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>LOTUS TOWER (1 \\u00bd HR) (Opening 9:00 AM to 9:00 PM)<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>It has been called a symbolic landmark of Sri Lanka. As of 2019, the tower is&nbsp;the tallest self-supported structure in South Asia; the second tallest structure in South Asia after the guy-wire-supported INS Kattabomman in India; the 11th tallest tower in Asia and the 19th tallest tower in the world.<\\/p>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<\\/td>\\n\\t\\t<\\/tr>\\n\\t<\\/tbody>\\n<\\/table>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Transfer to the Airport for Departure\",\"date\":\"18-11-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>After Breakfast Check-out from Hotel &amp; proceed to Airport.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Hyderabad (HYD)\",\"to\":\"Chennai (MAA)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"531\",\"dep_date\":\"13 Nov 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"13 Nov 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"05:35 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:45 AM\",\"fare\":\"50100\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Chennai (MAA)\",\"to\":\"Colombo (CMB)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"1175\",\"dep_date\":\"13 Nov 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"13 Nov 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"11:30 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"12:50 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Colombo (CMB)\",\"to\":\"Hyderabad (HYD)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"1182\",\"dep_date\":\"18 Nov 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"18 Nov 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"03:00 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"04:55 PM\",\"fare\":51215}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"13\\/11\\/2024\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Devon\",\"city\":\"KANDY\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room + 01 Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"15\\/11\\/2024\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"15\\/11\\/2024\",\"city\":\"BENTOTA\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Aryana Queen Beach Resort Wadduwa\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Sea View Room + 01 Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"17\\/11\\/2024\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"17\\/11\\/2024\",\"city\":\"COLOMBO\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Morven\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room + 01 Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"18\\/11\\/2024\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare<em><strong> Ex-Hyderabad.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nts</strong> Accommodation at <strong>Hotel Devon</strong>&nbsp;at Kandy.</li>\n	<li><strong>02 Nts</strong> Accommodation at <strong>Hotel Aryana Queen Beach Resort Wadduwa</strong> at Bentota.</li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Nt&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation at <strong>Hotel Morven</strong>&nbsp;at Colombo.</li>\n	<li>All <strong>Breakfasts &amp; Dinners.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Arrival &amp; Departure Assistance </strong>at the Airport</li>\n	<li><strong>City Tour </strong>&amp; <strong>Shopping.</strong></li>\n	<li>All Transfers &amp; Sightseeings by <strong>A/C Vehicle on PVT basis.</strong></li>\n	<li>Services of <em><strong>English-Speaking Chauffeur Driver.</strong></em></li>\n	<li>All Taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<table>\n	<tbody>\n		<tr>\n			<td colspan=\"3\">\n			<p><strong>Supplement for the entrance fee which aren’t included in the above-mentioned costs</strong></p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td>\n			<p>ON THE WAY TO KANDY</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>USD 12 Per Person</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td rowspan=\"2\">\n			<p>KANDY</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>Temple Of Tooth (Kandy Tedmple)</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>USD 08 Per Person</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td>\n			<p>Peradeniya Botanical Garden</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>USD 12 Per Person</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td rowspan=\"3\">\n			<p>BENTOTA</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>USD 05 per person</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td>\n			<p>Madhu Ganga Boat Ride</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>USD 30 per boat (Max 06 pax per boat)</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td>\n			<p>Bentota Water Sports (Jet Ski, Banana Ride, Tube Ride)</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>USD 30 per person</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td rowspan=\"2\">\n			<p>COLOMBO</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>Gangarama Floating Temple</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>USD 03 per person</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td>\n			<p>Lotus Tower</p>\n			</td>\n			<td>\n			<p>USD 20 per person</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n		<tr>\n			<td colspan=\"3\">\n			<p>Visa for Indian nationals – (Visa Free for Indian Nationalities please visit eta.gov.lk)</p>\n			</td>\n		</tr>\n	</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>**All the entrance fees are valid only if booked at the time of confirmation, on-ground rates may vary **</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"14\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":101315,\"land_cost\":\"91375\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":192690,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 26976.6\",\"selling_price\":219666.60000000000582076609134674072265625}', 'MZQ/0596/0112024', 220800, 44160, 0, '2024-11-09 10:23:23', '2024-11-09 10:23:23', 0, 1, '\"<p><strong>Value Additions (Complimentary) by Multi Zone Travels<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>500ml X 02 Mineral Water Bottles \\u2013 per person per day throughout the tour<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>5% worth of discount voucher for ODEL<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Complimentary SIM card on arrival (Need to do the top-up charges)<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Wheelchair for differently\\u2013abled people. This should be notified prior the arrival.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Complimentary King Coconut per person on a selected day in the itinerary<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Complimentary shoulder &amp; head massage along with Herbal Tea @ Recognized Spice Garden<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"', 0, 0),
(606, 'Ms Kamini', 'MZ CDG', '9855034443', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'NEPAL', '2024-12-21', 4, 0, 2, '[]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Kathmandu (KTM)\",\"name\":\"AirIndia\",\"fno\":\"213\",\"dep_date\":\"21 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"21 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"07:10 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"09:05 AM\",\"fare\":\"43326\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Kathmandu (KTM)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"AirIndia\",\"fno\":\"2156\",\"dep_date\":\"25 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"25 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"05:00 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:30 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"21\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"POKHARA\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Dahlia Boutique\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"23\\/12\\/2024\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"23\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"KATHMANDU\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Anuttara Lords Plaza\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"25\\/12\\/2024\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare<em><strong>&nbsp;Ex-Delhi.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><strong>02</strong> Internal Domestic Flights<strong> Kathmandu-Pokhara-Kathmandu.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nts&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation at <b>Pokhara</b>.</li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nts</strong>&nbsp;Accommodation at <strong>Kathmandu.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>01 Room</strong> on<strong> DBL&nbsp;</strong>Sharing<strong>.</strong></li>\n	<li>All&nbsp;<strong>Breakfasts.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>All Arrival &amp; Departure Assistance&nbsp;</strong>at the Airport.</li>\n	<li>All Transfers &amp; Sightseeings by&nbsp;<strong>A/C Vehicle on PVT basis.</strong></li>\n	<li>All Taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Services other than specified.</li>\n	<li>Entrance fee at the monumental sites during the sightseeing</li>\n	<li>Guide during the sightseeing</li>\n	<li>Any expenses of personal nature such as drinks, laundry, telephone/fax calls.</li>\n	<li>Any expenses caused by reasons beyond our control such as flight delays, rescheduling or cancellations, any accidents, medical evacuations, riots, strikes, etc.</li>\n	<li>Any tips to drivers, hotel staff, any meals apart from the ones mentioned above.</li>\n	<li>Any other tax or service charge that could be enforced during this period will be extra &amp;amp; need to borne by you.</li>\n	<li>NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"29\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":43326,\"land_cost\":\"97350\",\"hotel_cost\":null,\"transport_cost\":null},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":140676,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 40796.04\",\"selling_price\":181472.04000000000814907252788543701171875}', 'MZQ/0597/0112024', 181654, 90827, 0, '2024-11-09 11:46:09', '2024-12-19 10:52:53', 0, 1, '\"<p><b>Vehicle allocation:<\\/b><\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li><b>2 pax Car : Swift Dezire\\/ Skoda Rapid\\/Similar&nbsp;<\\/b><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p><b>Hand-phone SIM card:<\\/b><\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Upon arrival in Kathmandu at the International Airport better known as \\\"Tribhuwan International Airport\\\". After collecting your baggage there are Two Telephone companies known as&nbsp;<b>\\\"NCell &amp; NTC<\\/b>&nbsp;( Nepal Telecommunication). They have a Stall each. One Passport size photo and a copy of the passport will be required. One can purchase a Sim. Activation time is 10 mins on an average. Cost is Inr 150 per Sim which can be topped off as per requirement. It will be a 3G card. We are not in a position to take out the Sim in advance. Above is subject to change as per the Telecommunication &nbsp;Regulations.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><b>Please note :<\\/b><\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Vehicle will not be at disposal <\\/strong><\\/em>but will perform its respective duties, as per the itinerary&nbsp;only. No additional running for shopping \\/ lunches \\/ dinners\\/ additional sightseeing etc. will not be allowed. The vehicle will strictly be from Point to Point basis only.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em>The above <strong>rates are valid for Indian Nationals holding Indian Passport \\/ Voter\'s ID only.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>The above rates will not stand good<\\/strong> for any other nationality, <strong>OCI and PIO card as it is not valid in Nepal <\\/strong>and cannot be used as an identification by any Nationals.<\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li><b>Hotel Check - in Time:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1500 hrs<\\/b><\\/li>\\n\\t<li><b>Hotel Check - out Time:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1100 hrs<\\/b><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p><b>The above cost excludes:<\\/b><\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Services other than specified.&nbsp;<b>Entrance fee at the monumental sites during the sightseeing<\\/b>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<b>Guide during the sightseeing<\\/b><\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Any expenses of personal nature such as drinks, laundry, telephone\\/fax calls.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Any expenses caused by reasons beyond our control such as flight delays, rescheduling or cancellations, any accidents, medical evacuations, riots, strikes, etc.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Any tips to drivers, hotel staff, any meals apart from the ones mentioned above.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Any other tax or service charge that could be enforced during this period will be extra &amp; need to borne by you.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"', 0, 0),
(607, 'Mr Nikhil (Ex-CCU)', 'CARE NIKITA', '8183708487', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'ANDAMAN', '2024-12-19', 4, 2, 2, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Airport Pickup Later Corbyns Cove Beach and Light and Sound Show at Cellular Jail\",\"date\":\"19-12-2024 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Arrive at Port Blair in the morning\\/afternoon by flight and our representative will be waiting outside the airport holding a placard with your name on it. You will be taken to your hotel where you rest and relax. Later we proceed to Corbyns Cove. Coastal drive to this beach is awesome, a stretch of around 4 Km with an open sea towards your left is a sight to experience.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Take pit stops during this ride to click pictures and to explore the beauty. Later proceed to attend the enthralling Sound and Light Show at Cellular Jail - where the heroic saga of the Indian freedom struggle is brought alive. Enacting of freedom fighters and their struggle for Indias Independence is enacted during this trip. Post completion of this trip, we drop you back at your hotel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Port Blair To Havelock in Cruise Later Radhanagar Beach visit Until Sunset\",\"date\":\"20-12-2024 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today we depart to the Andaman Islands most amazing destination, Havelock Island. This destination is rated as the best island in India. Depart from Port Blair to Havelock Island on a ferry. Upon reaching Havelock, our representative attends you and will drop you at your hotel. Later we begin our journey to one of Asias best beaches, Radhanagar Beach. Explore this white sand beach and bask in the beauty of this natural wonder. You stay at this beach until sunset. Post this we drop you back to your resort where you relax and unwind.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Elephant Beach Boat Ride Tour and Complimentary Snorkelling with Hotel Pickup and Drop\",\"date\":\"21-12-2024 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Well, how about exploring something underwater. Today, we begin our journey to the most visited snorkeling destination in Havelock Island, Elephant Beach. Around 30 Minutes by boat, Elephant Beach flaunts one among the best reefs in Havelock Island. The great thing is that the reef here starts at a depth of less than a meter. Upon reaching Elephant beach, we rest and relax. Later, a guide takes you to provide a complimentary snorkeling session at Elephant Beach (Snorkeling at Havelock Island depends upon the association guidelines). After the trip, we return back from Elephant beach to the Havelock dock in a boat. At the dock, our team attends you and drops you at your hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Note: Our team at Havelock will guide you in case you require any assistance on the ground<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kalapathar Beach Visit Later Havelock To Port Blair in Cruise and Port Blair Hotel Drop\",\"date\":\"22-12-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today, we visit Kalapathar Beach at Havelock Island. The journey to reach this beach is beautiful. Post this trip we return back to take a ferry in the afternoon from Havelock Island to Port Blair.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;Upon reaching Port Blair our representative will meet you and will drop you at your hotel for an overnight stay.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;Note: Please note that many hotels in the Andaman Islands have early check-out timing around 8:00 AM. In case your ferry is later in the afternoon, then you may avail water activities at Havelock. Our team will be available to assist you with any activities at Havelock.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Drop to the Airport\",\"date\":\"23-12-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Check out from the hotel and proceed to the airport to return home with sweet memories of this exotic destination.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Do note that hotels have an early check-out time. Guest will need to keep their luggage in the reception kiosk if your scheduled flight is in the afternoon. If you wish to visit any attraction during your free time then do let us know.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Portblair (IXZ)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"345\",\"dep_date\":\"19 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"19 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"09:05 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"11:20 AM\",\"fare\":\"25200\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Portblair (IXZ)\",\"to\":\"Bangalore (BLR)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"993\",\"dep_date\":\"23 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"23 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"07:45 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"10:20 AM\",\"fare\":\"29100\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"19\\/12\\/2024\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel The Luxor\",\"room_type\":\"Executive Room\",\"city\":\"PORTBLAIR\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"20\\/12\\/2024\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"20\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"HAVELOCK\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Aquays Beach Resort\",\"room_type\":\"Havelock Plaza\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"22\\/12\\/2024\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"22\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"PORTBLAIR\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel The Luxor\",\"room_type\":\"Executive Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"23\\/12\\/2024\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":6},{\"age\":2}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airfare&nbsp;<strong>Kolkata-Portblair-Bangalore.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02 Nts Accommodation</strong>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<strong>Double sharing&nbsp;</strong>at <strong>Port Blair </strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02 Nts Accommodation</strong>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<strong>Double sharing&nbsp;</strong>at&nbsp;<strong>Havelock.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Breakfast and Dinner</strong>&nbsp;at respective hotels.</li>\n	<li>Meet and greet service&nbsp;at the airport.</li>\n	<li><strong>Airport&nbsp;pickup and drop.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>All sightseeing by&nbsp;Private AC Vehicle&nbsp;at all the islands.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>All side&nbsp;Ferry Tickets&nbsp;Included&nbsp;02 Side Cruises&nbsp;to Havelock.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>All&nbsp;entry tickets, ferry tickets, and permit charges.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>One session for snorkeling&nbsp;is complimentary.</strong></li>\n	<li>Parking charges.</li>\n	<li>Travel assistance&nbsp;by&nbsp;<strong>Multi Zone Travel&nbsp;experts</strong>&nbsp;in all the islands.</li>\n	<li>All Taxes</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"22\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":54300,\"land_cost\":\"63545\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":117845,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 25925.9\",\"selling_price\":143770.89999999999417923390865325927734375}', 'MZQ/0598/0112024', 143534, 49387, 22380, '2024-11-12 11:40:26', '2024-11-13 06:57:34', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
