(623, 'Mr Chandan', 'Kailash Crockery', '9470130687', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'SINGAPORE + CRUISE', '2025-02-08', 6, 0, 2, '[]', '[{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Singapore (SIN)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"1015\",\"dep_date\":\"08 Feb 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"08 Feb 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"02:30 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"09:20 AM\",\"fare\":\"27088\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Singapore (SIN)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"Singapore Airlines\",\"fno\":\"516\",\"dep_date\":\"15 Feb 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"15 Feb 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"08:40 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"10:25 PM\",\"fare\":\"29216\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"08\\/02\\/2025\",\"city\":\"SINGAPORE\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Boss\",\"room_type\":\"Superior Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"11\\/02\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"29163\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"11\\/02\\/2025\",\"city\":\"CRUISE\",\"check_out\":\"14\\/02\\/2025\",\"hotel_name\":\"Genting Dream RWC\",\"room_type\":\"Ocean View StateRoom\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"ap\",\"nights\":3,\"rate\":\"85426\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"14\\/02\\/2025\",\"city\":\"SINGAPORE\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel V lavender\",\"room_type\":\"Superior Room\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"15\\/02\\/2025\",\"meal\":\"cp\",\"rooms\":1,\"rate\":\"10406\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li><strong>03 Nights&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation in&nbsp;<em><strong>Hotel Boss, Singapore.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Night&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation in&nbsp;<em><strong>Hotel V lavender, Singapore.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><strong>01 Room</strong>&nbsp;on DBL Sharing</li>\n	<li><strong>All Breakfasts</strong>&nbsp;@ Singapore Hotel.</li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Airport Transfer</strong>&nbsp;on PVT</li>\n	<li><strong>02 Cruise Terminal&nbsp;Transfers&nbsp;</strong>on PVT</li>\n	<li><strong>Singapore City Tour&nbsp;</strong>on SIC</li>\n	<li>Full Day<strong>&nbsp;Universal Studios&nbsp;</strong>on SIC</li>\n	<li><strong>Gardens by the Bay</strong>: 2 Conservatories (Cloud Forest + Flower Dome)&nbsp;on SIC</li>\n	<li><strong>Night Safari + River Wonder </strong>(Complimentary Animal Show + Tram Ride)<strong>&nbsp;</strong>on PVT</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>CRUISE INCLUSIONS :</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>03 Nights</strong> accommodation on Double Sharing in <em><strong>Ocean View StateRoom.</strong></em></li>\n	<li>Port Charges</li>\n	<li><strong>04 Complimentary meals </strong>Per day – at the following Restaurants</li>\n	<li>Dream Dining Lower/ Deck 7 FWD ( International Cusine)</li>\n	<li>Dream Dining Upper/ Deck 8 FWD ( Chinese Cusine)</li>\n	<li>The Lido/ Deck 16 AFT -24 Hours Snacks (Finger Food) Counter</li>\n	<li>( Indian Cusine, jain meals available )</li>\n	<li>3 more venues (Blue Lagoon, Crystal Life Cuisine and Function 8) for inclusive meals services:</li>\n	<li>Blue Lagoon inclusive meal set will be an extension from Dream Dinning Upper for lunch and dinner.</li>\n	<li>Crystal Life Cuisine will serve breakfast, lunch and dinner with simple set menu.</li>\n	<li>Usage of specified cruise facilities (As per Daily Programme List)</li>\n	<li>Participation in our specified cruise activities (As per Daily Programme List)</li>\n	<li>Usage of Rope Course, Zip Lining, Rock Climbing, Swimming Pool, Jacuzzi, Gymnasium, Water Slides, Mini Golf, Basketball</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":null,\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":56304,\"hotel_cost\":124995,\"land_cost\":\"43517\",\"visa_cost\":\"5990\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":230806,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 0\",\"selling_price\":280000,\"profit_figure\":\"49194\",\"percent_of_amount\":\"21.00%\"}', 'MZQ/0614/0122024', 280000, 140000, 0, '2024-12-17 14:31:25', '2025-02-05 08:12:59', 0, 1, '\"<p><strong>IMPORTANT INFORMATION<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;Each stateroom must have at least one passenger who is age 18+<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;Age of Infant: 6 months to less than 2 years old. Infants must be at least 6 months old on date of sailing to be allowed to board.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;All passports must have at least 6 months validity from the date of sailing<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;Passengers are responsible to ensure that all travel documents and visas are in order prior to departure from their home country<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;RW Cruise Pte Ltd will not accept passengers who have entered their 24th week of pregnancy by the beginning of, or at any time during their cruise vacation<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;RW Cruises Pte Ltd reserves the right to cancel or substitute any scheduled port of call\\/itinerary\\/price\\/programme at any time without prior notice<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;Distance from the airport to the departure port is approx. 25-45 Mins. (Depending on the traffic)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;Check-in starts 4 hours prior to the sailing time and closes 2 hours before the sailing time.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;Your cabin key is also a currency card for the cruise, all the onboard purchases\\/gratuities will be added in the same and the final amount would have to be settled at the time of check out<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;You would get a Daily Programme List once you check in, the same would contain the details of all the onboard activities and entertainment shows<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;Wi-Fi packages available on board at additional cost<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;You can\'t carry alcohol on board, liquor packages can be booked on board<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;A swimming costume is mandatory to access the swimming pool<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u00b7&nbsp;&nbsp;Check out formalities takes almost two hours (please plan your return Flight accordingly)&nbsp;<\\/p>\"', 0, 0),
(624, 'Mr.  Manoj Kumar', 'Saurabh Satellite', '8986880455', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'DUBAI', '2025-03-20', 6, 0, 4, '[]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"5043\",\"dep_date\":\"20 Mar 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"20 Mar 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"09:10 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"11:15 AM\",\"fare\":\"19400\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Dubai (DXB)\",\"name\":\"AirIndia\",\"fno\":\"915\",\"dep_date\":\"20 Mar 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"20 Mar 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"04:25 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"07:00 PM\",\"fare\":\"108842\"},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Dubai (DXB)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"AirIndia\",\"fno\":\"916\",\"dep_date\":\"26 Mar 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"27 Mar 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"08:40 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:25 AM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"5044\",\"dep_date\":\"27 Mar 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"27 Mar 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"06:55 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"08:40 AM\",\"fare\":\"18437\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"20\\/03\\/2025\",\"city\":\"DUBAI\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Ascot Bur Dubai\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":6,\"check_out\":\"26\\/03\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"77500\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare&nbsp;<strong>Ex-Ranchi.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>06&nbsp;Nights</strong>&nbsp;Accommodation in<strong>&nbsp;Hotel Ascot Bur Dubai.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02 Rooms on DBL.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Daily Breakfast&nbsp;</strong>at the Hotel.</li>\n	<li><strong>Dubai Airport transfers</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>-PVT</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Half-Day Dubai City Tour</strong>&nbsp;with&nbsp;<strong>Dubai Mall</strong>&nbsp;&amp;<strong>&nbsp;Fountain Show. -SIC&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Burj Khalifa 124-125th Floor. -SIC&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Deluxe Marina Dhow Cruise.&nbsp;-SIC&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Deluxe Desert Safari&nbsp;Lama Camp</strong>&nbsp;with VIP Seating or Similar<strong>&nbsp;</strong>with BBQ Dinner, Belly Dance Show, and other camp activities.&nbsp;<strong>-SIC&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Abu Dhabi City Tour with&nbsp;Ferrari World. -PVT</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>BAPS Hindu Temple. -PVT&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Dubai Frame. -PVT</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Museum of the Future -PVT</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Global Village&nbsp;-PVT</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Miracle Garden&nbsp;-PVT</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Dubai Tourist Visa&nbsp;</strong>with&nbsp;Insurance.</li>\n	<li><strong>All Taxes.</strong></li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"10\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":146679,\"hotel_cost\":77500,\"land_cost\":\"125500\",\"visa_cost\":\"27200\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":376879,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 37687.9\",\"selling_price\":414566.900000000023283064365386962890625,\"profit_figure\":null,\"percent_of_amount\":\"11.00%\"}', 'MZQ/0615/0122024', 414680, 103670, 37500, '2024-12-19 11:28:22', '2024-12-20 12:39:53', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(625, 'MR SAKET SARAF', 'BNI EXPLORERS', '9835574327', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'VIETNAM', '2024-12-27', 8, 2, 5, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DEPARTURE RANCHI\",\"date\":\"27-12-2024 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Depart from Ranchi for a memorable trip of Vietnam.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HO CHI MINH ARRIVAL \\u2013 CU CHI TUNNELS \\u2013 HCM CITY TOUR\",\"date\":\"28-12-2024 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Our car and tour guide will pick you up from HCM airport to the hotel for check-in and refreshment. After that visit Cu Chi Tunnels The Cu Chi Tunnels are an underground labyrinth of passageways, used by the Viet Cong during the Vietnam War as protection against American air raids. Those inclined are invited to crawl through selections of the tunnels to better understand what life was like for the Vietnamese soldiers during wartime. In the afternoon, take the city tour around HCM city:<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2726 Independence Palace: the former headquarters of the United States located in South Vietnam.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2726 Notre Dame Cathedral: an architectural masterpiece - a typical work contributing to the urban appearance of Saigon - Ho Chi Minh City. The work also records the introduction, exchange and acculturation of East-West culture and architecture.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2726 City Post Office: is an indispensable destination for tourists when coming to Ho Chi Minh City, an ancient architecture, more than 120 years old.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2726War Remnants Museum. After that, guests can take a coffee chill at Cong caf\\u00e9 and try our famous coconut coffee (at their own expense).<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Meal: Breakfast<br \\/>\\nOvernight in HCM<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HCM CITY \\u2013 MEKONG DELTA \\u2013 DA NANG\",\"date\":\"29-12-2024 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Our guide and driver will pick you up at your hotel and drive 2,5 hours to Mekong River. We will stop along the way for refreshments and toilet. Here are some activities on the trip: \\u2022 Visit a flea market and cruise along a vast network of canals and channels of Mekong River.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2022 Have some fresh fruits and visit some local cottage industries (coconut candy workshop, snake wine, pop-rice, or rice paper)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2022 Visit an island named Tan Phong and a tropical fruit garden, listen to Vietnamese traditional music, and enjoy getting in touch with local life. Get back to the house, say goodbye to your hosts. Arrive Ho Chi Minh, be dropped off at your hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Check out the hotel and prepare to fly to Da Nang city.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Meal: Breakfast<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Da Nang<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DA NANG \\u2013 HOI AN COCONUT TOUR \\u2013 HOI AN ANCIENT TOWN\",\"date\":\"30-12-2024 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Breakfast at hotel. Tour guide picks up guests at Cua Dai Bridge, Hoi An. Guests Walk along the village path for 5 minutes to the marina.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Visitors visit Bay Mau Coconut Forest on basket boats, a typical vehicle of the fishing village of Van Lang village. You can see with your own eyes the local people casting their nets on the river to catch fish and can experience their own casting skills. Then, watch the unique basket-shaking performance of the basket-shaking artisan of Van Lang village. The group of baskets arrive at the Eco-Restaurant, rest on the leaf house. You can freely visit the space of the eco-tourism area, then gather to participate in folk games with fun prizes: Go monkey bridge, break pots, jump sacks, tunnel, ... Farewell to the tourist area, wooden boats take guests to Cua Dai Bridge. Back to Hoi An Go to Hoi An ancient town for the late afternoon.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong><em>Meal: Breakfast<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Da Nang<\\/em><\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"BANA HILLS FULL DAY\",\"date\":\"31-12-2024 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning Breakfast at the hotel then guide will pick up for Bana Hills. - Check in at the Suoi Mo Cable Car Station and transfer to Marseille Station.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>- Explore Golden Bridge (The Hands of The Gods) - majestic and impressive as a scene in \\u201cGame of Thrones\\u201d or \\u201cThe Lords of the Rings\\u201d.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>- Drop by Le Jardin D\\u2019Amour (the Flower Garden of Love) with 9 gardens of Le Jardin D\\u2019Amour are 9 amusing tales in 9 varying architectures, which harmonize so well in a visual sonata of beauty.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>- Continue the trip with Debay Wine Cellar.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Meal: Breakfast<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Da Nang<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"DA NANG CITY TOUR \\u2013 HANOI CITY\",\"date\":\"01-01-2025 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Breakfast at the hotel, then guests will be taken by tour guide and driver to visit Da Nang city First is the Marble Mountain, a cluster of five hills made from limestone and marble in Da Nang. It\'s also a well-known pilgrimage site with peaks, caves, and tunnels. Next is Son Tra Peninsula &amp; Linh Ung Pagoda Drive to the Monkey Mountain and visit the 67-meter Lady Buddha statue. Soak in the panoramic views of Da Nang city. Rest at noon, visit Han Market where guests will get free time to buy souvenirs or chill at the coffee shop.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>After that, go back to the hotel to get your belongings and head for Da Nang airport to catch the flight to Hanoi city. Get picked up by our driver and tour guide.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong><em>Meal: Breakfast<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Hanoi<\\/em><\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HANOI CITY TOUR\",\"date\":\"02-01-2025 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Breakfast at the Hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Then our tour guide and driver will pick guests for the Hanoi tour Visit Ho Chi Minh Complex and enjoy the architectural and historical aspects of Uncle Ho\\u2019s final resting-place. Just next door is Ho Chi Minh\\u2019s house on stilts. Lying to one side of the Mausoleum is the One Pillar Pagoda; founded by King Ly Thai To in 1049 the structure has become an important symbol for the people of Hanoi. Continue to visit Buddhist Tran Quoc Pagoda by the side of West Lake (One of the oldest in Vietnam). Visit the Literature Temple and Quoc Tu Giam- the first National university in Vietnam, which was constructed in 1070, its gardens and well-preserved architecture offers a relaxing glimpse into Vietnam\\u2019s past. And visit One Pillar Pagoda, Hoan Kiem Lake, Presidential Palace We return to the OLD QUARTER and walk around for shopping.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong><em>Meal: Breakfast<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Hanoi<\\/em><\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HANOI \\u2013 NINH BINH\",\"date\":\"03-01-2025 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Breakfast and lunch on Cruise4 then Tour guide and Driver will pick you up to travel to Ninh Binh Hoa Lu temples of the Dinh &amp; Le Dynasties Hoa Lu is the ancient capital of Vietnam in the Ly, Tien Le dynasties (10th century). It is a large area with many areas surrounded by Rocky Mountains. Getting to Hoa Lu, you will visit 2 sacred temples worshipping King Dinh and King Le. You can also learn many historical values and listen to stories about kings who have built and defended the country during its long history.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Tam Coc \\u2013 Bich Dong Tam Coc is a place with 3 caves: Hang Ca, Hai Hai, and Hang Ba. All these three caves are formed by the Ngo Dong River crashing through the mountain and belong to Tam Coc \\u2013 Bich Dong landscape complex. To visit Tam Coc, visitors will sit on a bamboo boat rowed by local people, and watch the wonderful scenery of the mountains, and Ngo Dong River for about 1-2 hours. You can cycle from Tam Coc for about 5 km to visit the Bich Dong pagoda and enjoy the natural landscapes and villages. The pagoda was built on the Truong Yen limestone mountain range with extremely wonderful scenery, known as Nam Thien De Nhi Dong. It has three non-contiguous buildings along with a mountain shape. The temple is hidden in the mountains, merging with nature, mountains, caves, and pagodas, in a breathtaking natural &amp; spiritual landscape<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong><em>Meal: Breakfast &amp; Lunch<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Hanoi<\\/em><\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":9,\"index\":8,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HANOI \\u2013 HALONG BAY (SHARING CRUISE)\",\"date\":\"04-01-2025 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Breakfast at hotel.<br \\/>\\nPick up at the hotel and depart to Ha Long by shuttle bus<br \\/>\\nCheck-in the cabin and enjoy lunch while cruising through the most beautiful parts with thousands of amazing limestone islands emerging from emerald water.<br \\/>\\nTake an exhilarating kayak trip through the lagoon, have a refreshing swim or simply relax on board.<br \\/>\\nBack to Hanoi at the afternoon, head straight to Noi Bai airport to catch the flight back to your country<br \\/>\\nEnd of trip, see you soon!<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><strong><em>Meal: Breakfast &amp; Lunch<br \\/>\\nOvernight in Hanoi<\\/em><\\/strong><\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"6893\",\"dep_date\":\"27 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"27 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:35 PM\",\"fare\":\"108499\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Ho Chi Minh (SGN)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"1641\",\"dep_date\":\"27 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"28 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"08:40 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:40 AM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Ho Chi Minh (SGN)\",\"to\":\"Da Nang (DAD)\",\"name\":\"VietJet Air\",\"fno\":\"1628\",\"dep_date\":\"29 Dec 2024\",\"arv_date\":\"30 Dec 2024\",\"dep_time\":\"11:25 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"12:45 AM\",\"fare\":\"36898\"},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Da Nang (DAD)\",\"to\":\"Hanoi (HAN)\",\"name\":\"VietJet Air\",\"fno\":\"512\",\"dep_date\":\"01 Jan 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"01 Jan 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"05:20 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:40 PM\",\"fare\":\"61062\"},{\"id\":5,\"from\":\"Hanoi (HAN)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"1632\",\"dep_date\":\"05 Jan 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"05 Jan 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"03:10 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"04:55 AM\",\"fare\":\"174936\"},{\"id\":6,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Ranchi (IXR)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"7561\",\"dep_date\":\"05 Jan 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"05 Jan 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"07:40 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"08:50 AM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"27\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"HI CHI MINH CITY\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Equatorial\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room + 01 EB\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"29\\/12\\/2024\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"29\\/12\\/2024\",\"city\":\"DA NANG\",\"hotel_name\":\"Sel de Mer Hotel & Suites\",\"room_type\":\"Superior Ocean View + 01 EB\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"01\\/01\\/2025\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"01\\/01\\/2025\",\"city\":\"HANOI\",\"hotel_name\":\"Grand Mercure Hotel\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room + 01 EB\",\"rooms\":2,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"04\\/01\\/2025\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":7},{\"age\":8}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return&nbsp;<strong><em>Airfare Ex-Ranchi.</em></strong></li>\n	<li><strong>08 Nts Accommodation</strong>&nbsp;in above Hotels</li>\n	<li><strong>01 Room </strong>on Double sharing with 01 E/B + <strong>01 Room</strong> on Double Sharing.</li>\n	<li>All <strong>Breakfasts</strong>.</li>\n	<li><strong>Entrance fees</strong>&nbsp;for all visits as mentioned in the itinerary</li>\n	<li><em><strong>Experienced English speaking guide</strong></em>&nbsp;during all tours on<strong> PVT</strong> (Upgraded Complimentary).</li>\n	<li><strong>Ninh Binh </strong>Tour on SIC.</li>\n	<li><strong>Private 16-seater A/C Van</strong> for all Airport Transfers.</li>\n	<li><strong>Sharing Day Cruise with Lunch</strong> in Ha Long Bay.</li>\n	<li><em><strong>Mineral water&nbsp;</strong></em>is available as complementary.</li>\n	<li>All Taxes</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li><strong>Tip for driver and guide:</strong>&nbsp;@3 USD/pax/day &amp; 1.5 USD/Child/Day&nbsp;(Mandatory).</li>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":null,\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":\"383359\",\"visa_cost\":\"28856\",\"land_cost\":\"348700\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":760915,\"profit_figure\":\"32085\",\"percent_of_amount\":\"4.00%\",\"selling_price\":793000}', 'MZQ/0616/0122024', 793000, 122452, 92265, '2024-12-20 13:03:35', '2024-12-25 07:51:01', 0, 1, '\"<p><em><strong>Weather Tips: <\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2022 <strong>North Vietnam <\\/strong>(Hanoi, Ha Long Bay, Sapa): Expect cold, misty mornings with temperatures around 10-15\\u00b0C in Hanoi and Ha Long Bay, and slightly colder in Sapa (7-13\\u00b0C). A winter jacket, layered clothing, and comfortable walking shoes are recommended.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2022 <strong>Central &amp; South Vietnam<\\/strong> (Hue, Da Nang, Hoi An, Da Lat, Ho Chi Minh City): Generally cool, with temperatures ranging from 22-27\\u00b0C Rain Chances: Occasional light rain or drizzle can occur, especially in the north.regions. Pack a lightweight rain jacket or travel umbrella, but heavy rain is unlikely. Packing Essentials:<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>\\u2022 <strong>Sun Protection: <\\/strong>Sunscreen, sunglasses, and hats are still recommended, especially for central and southern areas where the sun can be strong. \\u2022 Layered Clothing: Prepare for varying temperatures, especially in mountainous and northern regions. A windbreaker or lightweight jacket is ideal. Please keep your belongings by your side, important documents can be kept at the hotel for most of the tour, except during flights. There are some notes about each destination, I will inform you and support you 24\\/7 with everything during your trip.<\\/p>\"', 0, 0),
