ong> to explore at your own pace.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Volcano & Ubud Tour\",\"date\":\"29-09-2025 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"125\\\" data-start=\\\"66\\\">After breakfast and check-out, depart at <strong data-end=\\\"118\\\" data-start=\\\"107\\\">9:00 AM<\\/strong> for:<\\/p>\\n\\n<ul data-end=\\\"307\\\" data-start=\\\"126\\\">\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"171\\\" data-start=\\\"126\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"171\\\" data-start=\\\"128\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"159\\\" data-start=\\\"128\\\">Kintamani Mt. Batur Volcano<\\/strong> viewpoint<\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"214\\\" data-start=\\\"172\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"214\\\" data-start=\\\"174\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"193\\\" data-start=\\\"174\\\">Ubud Art Market<\\/strong> &amp; <strong data-end=\\\"212\\\" data-start=\\\"196\\\">Royal Palace<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"248\\\" data-start=\\\"215\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"248\\\" data-start=\\\"217\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"232\\\" data-start=\\\"217\\\">Aloha Swing<\\/strong> (Adults only)<\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"281\\\" data-start=\\\"249\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"281\\\" data-start=\\\"251\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"279\\\" data-start=\\\"251\\\">Tegallalang Rice Terrace<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"307\\\" data-start=\\\"282\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"307\\\" data-start=\\\"284\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"305\\\" data-start=\\\"284\\\">Coffee plantation<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"337\\\" data-start=\\\"309\\\">Check-in to your next hotel.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Nusa Penida West Tour\",\"date\":\"30-09-2025 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"185\\\" data-start=\\\"78\\\">After breakfast at the hotel, pick-up at <strong data-end=\\\"131\\\" data-start=\\\"119\\\">07:00 AM<\\/strong> for a full-day <strong data-end=\\\"172\\\" data-start=\\\"147\\\">Nusa Penida West Tour<\\/strong>, visiting:<\\/p>\\n\\n<ul data-end=\\\"305\\\" data-start=\\\"186\\\">\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"211\\\" data-start=\\\"186\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"211\\\" data-start=\\\"188\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"209\\\" data-start=\\\"188\\\">Angel\'s Billabong<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"232\\\" data-start=\\\"212\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"232\\\" data-start=\\\"214\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"230\\\" data-start=\\\"214\\\">Broken Beach<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"257\\\" data-start=\\\"233\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"257\\\" data-start=\\\"235\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"255\\\" data-start=\\\"235\\\">Kelingking Cliff<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"277\\\" data-start=\\\"258\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"277\\\" data-start=\\\"260\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"275\\\" data-start=\\\"260\\\">Crystal Bay<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n\\t<li data-end=\\\"305\\\" data-start=\\\"278\\\">\\n\\t<p data-end=\\\"305\\\" data-start=\\\"280\\\">Enjoy a <strong data-end=\\\"303\\\" data-start=\\\"288\\\">local lunch<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n\\t<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"399\\\" data-start=\\\"307\\\">Return by boat at <strong data-end=\\\"334\\\" data-start=\\\"325\\\">16:30<\\/strong>, transfer back to the hotel, and enjoy the rest of the day free.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"440\\\" data-start=\\\"401\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"411\\\" data-start=\\\"401\\\">(B, L)<\\/strong> \\u2013 Breakfast &amp; Lunch included<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Departure\",\"date\":\"01-10-2025 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"151\\\" data-start=\\\"66\\\">After breakfast at the hotel, pick-up for transfer to the airport for your departure.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"181\\\" data-start=\\\"153\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"160\\\" data-start=\\\"153\\\">(B)<\\/strong> \\u2013 Breakfast included<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Denpasar Bali (DPS)\",\"name\":\"AirIndia\",\"fno\":\"2145\",\"dep_date\":\"24 Sep 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"25 Sep 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"09:55 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"08:10 AM\",\"fare\":\"457133\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Denpasar Bali (DPS)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"AirIndia\",\"fno\":\"2146\",\"dep_date\":\"01 Oct 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"10:35 AM\",\"arv_date\":\"01 Oct 2025\",\"arv_time\":\"03:50\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"24\\/09\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Kuta\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Risata Bali Resort \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"ap\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"27\\/09\\/2025\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"27\\/09\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Ubud\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Royal Casa Ganesha \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"ap\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"29\\/09\\/2025\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"29\\/09\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Seminyak\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Jambuluwuk Oceano \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"ap\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"01\\/10\\/2025\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":5},{\"age\":4},{\"age\":3}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <em><strong>Ex-Delhi.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><strong>03&nbsp;Nights accommodation</strong>&nbsp;at Hotel &nbsp;Aston Kuta Hotel &amp; Residence / Similar at&nbsp;<em><strong>Kuta</strong></em>.</li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nights accommodation</strong>&nbsp;at Hotel Champlung Sari / Similar at&nbsp;<strong>BALI Ubud</strong>.</li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nights&nbsp;accommodation</strong>&nbsp;at Hotel Fairfield by Marriott Legian&nbsp;/ Similar at&nbsp;<strong>BALI Legian</strong>.</li>\n	<li><strong>Tanjung Benoa Water Sports</strong>&nbsp;</li>\n	<li><strong>Uluwatu Temple with Kecak Dance&nbsp;</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>Full Day&nbsp;West Nusa penida Day trip</strong> including Local Lunch</li>\n	<li><strong>Kintamani Volcano view +&nbsp;Ubud Market</strong></li>\n	<li>All Tours &amp; Transfers by&nbsp;AC car Xenia /Avanza / Suzuki APV / with English speaking DRIVER&nbsp;on a<strong> PRIVATE basis.</strong></li>\n	<li>Entrance tickets and parking fees</li>\n	<li>Program tours as mentioned above</li>\n	<li>Meals as indicated <em><strong>(B=Breakfast, L=Lunch, D=Dinner)</strong></em></li>\n	<li>1x local lunch, .</li>\n	<li>Welcome flower garland at Airport</li>\n	<li>01 bottle mineral water &nbsp;per person per day</li>\n	<li>All taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"10\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":457133,\"land_cost\":\"273150\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":730283,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 73028.3\",\"selling_price\":803311.30000000004656612873077392578125}', 'MZQ/0668/042025', 802491, 102450, 62597, '2025-04-21 13:34:16', '2025-04-24 13:06:59', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(680, 'Mr Shashank Agarwal', 'BNI', '7979911524', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'HIMACHAL', '2025-04-26', 6, 0, 2, '[{\"title\":\"Saturday\",\"day\":\"Day 1\",\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Chandigarh \\u2013 Shimla (Approx. 120 km \\/ 4 hrs)\",\"date\":\"26-04-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"540\\\" data-start=\\\"103\\\">Upon arrival at <strong data-end=\\\"207\\\" data-start=\\\"177\\\">Chandigarh Airport<\\/strong>, you will be met by our representative\\/driver. From there, begin your scenic drive to <strong data-end=\\\"304\\\" data-start=\\\"294\\\">Shimla<\\/strong>, the former summer capital of British India, nestled in the Shivalik ranges of the Himalayas. On arrival, check in to your hotel and relax. The rest of the day is at your leisure to explore the surroundings or unwind at the property.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"584\\\" data-start=\\\"542\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"584\\\" data-start=\\\"542\\\">Overnight stay at the hotel in Shimla.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Sunday\",\"day\":\"Day 2\",\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Shimla \\u2013 Kufri Excursion & Local Sightseeing\",\"date\":\"27-04-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"465\\\" data-start=\\\"66\\\">After breakfast, head to <strong data-end=\\\"151\\\" data-start=\\\"142\\\">Kufri<\\/strong>, known for its <strong data-end=\\\"194\\\" data-start=\\\"167\\\">Himalayan National Park<\\/strong>, <strong data-end=\\\"214\\\" data-start=\\\"196\\\">pony\\/yak rides<\\/strong>, and stunning views of the Himalayas. Post-lunch, explore Shimla\'s key colonial-era landmarks: <strong data-end=\\\"327\\\" data-is-only-node=\\\"\\\" data-start=\\\"310\\\">Shimla Mosque<\\/strong>, <strong data-end=\\\"349\\\" data-start=\\\"329\\\">Vice Regal Lodge<\\/strong>, <strong data-end=\\\"368\\\" data-start=\\\"351\\\">Christ Church<\\/strong>, <strong data-end=\\\"388\\\" data-start=\\\"370\\\">Gaiety Theatre<\\/strong>, <strong data-end=\\\"408\\\" data-start=\\\"390\\\">Grindlays Bank<\\/strong>, <strong data-end=\\\"427\\\" data-start=\\\"410\\\">Scandal Point<\\/strong>, and enjoy shopping at <strong data-end=\\\"464\\\" data-start=\\\"451\\\">Mall Road<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"496\\\" data-start=\\\"467\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"496\\\" data-start=\\\"467\\\">Overnight stay in Shimla.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Monday\",\"day\":\"Day 3\",\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Shimla \\u2013 Manali via Kullu Valley (Approx. 265 km \\/ 8 hrs)\",\"date\":\"28-04-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"527\\\" data-start=\\\"94\\\">After breakfast, check out from the hotel and proceed for a beautiful drive to <strong data-end=\\\"254\\\" data-start=\\\"244\\\">Manali<\\/strong>. En route, enjoy the breathtaking views of the <strong data-end=\\\"318\\\" data-start=\\\"302\\\">Kullu Valley<\\/strong>, known for its lush greenery, river views, and traditional Himachali culture. You may choose to stop for local sightseeing, shopping for woolens or try out river rafting in Kullu (optional, at your own cost).<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"661\\\" data-start=\\\"529\\\">Arrive in <strong data-end=\\\"549\\\" data-start=\\\"539\\\">Manali<\\/strong> by evening and check in to your hotel. Spend the evening at leisure or take a stroll through the local markets.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"705\\\" data-start=\\\"663\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"705\\\" data-start=\\\"663\\\">Overnight stay at the hotel in Manali.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Tuesday\",\"day\":\"Day 4\",\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Manali \\u2013 Local Sightseeing\",\"date\":\"29-04-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"420\\\" data-start=\\\"64\\\">After breakfast, explore popular attractions in and around Manali including the ancient <strong data-end=\\\"203\\\" data-start=\\\"185\\\">Hadimba Temple<\\/strong>, <strong data-end=\\\"220\\\" data-start=\\\"205\\\">Manu Temple<\\/strong> (accessible by walk), and the natural hot springs at <strong data-end=\\\"291\\\" data-start=\\\"274\\\">Vashisht Bath<\\/strong>. Stroll through the serene <strong data-end=\\\"332\\\" data-is-only-node=\\\"\\\" data-start=\\\"319\\\">Van Vihar<\\/strong> park. In the evening, enjoy shopping and local cuisine at <strong data-end=\\\"419\\\" data-start=\\\"391\\\">Manali\\u2019s bustling market<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"451\\\" data-start=\\\"422\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"451\\\" data-start=\\\"422\\\">Overnight stay in Manali.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Wednesday\",\"day\":\"Day 5\",\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Manali \\u2013 Excursion to Solang Valley\",\"date\":\"30-04-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"409\\\" data-start=\\\"65\\\">After breakfast, proceed for an exciting excursion to <strong data-end=\\\"178\\\" data-start=\\\"161\\\">Solang Valley<\\/strong>, famous for its breathtaking views and adventure activities like paragliding, zorbing, and ropeway rides (activities optional &amp; at own cost). Spend time amidst snow-capped peaks and scenic landscapes before returning to the hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"440\\\" data-start=\\\"411\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"440\\\" data-start=\\\"411\\\">Overnight stay in Manali.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Thursday\",\"day\":\"Day 6\",\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Manali \\u2013 Chandigarh (Approx. 320 km \\/ 8\\u20139 hrs)\",\"date\":\"01-05-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"446\\\" data-start=\\\"117\\\">After breakfast, check out from the hotel and drive to <strong data-end=\\\"246\\\" data-start=\\\"232\\\">Chandigarh<\\/strong>, India\\u2019s first planned modern city, designed by French architect <strong data-end=\\\"328\\\" data-start=\\\"312\\\">Le Corbusier<\\/strong>. The city derives its name from the goddess <strong data-end=\\\"383\\\" data-start=\\\"373\\\">Chandi<\\/strong>, with the <strong data-end=\\\"416\\\" data-start=\\\"394\\\">Chandimandu Temple<\\/strong> being a significant landmark.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"583\\\" data-start=\\\"448\\\">Subject to time availability upon arrival, visit popular attractions such as the iconic <strong data-end=\\\"551\\\" data-start=\\\"536\\\">Rock Garden<\\/strong> and the serene <strong data-end=\\\"582\\\" data-start=\\\"567\\\">Sukhna Lake<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"631\\\" data-start=\\\"585\\\"><strong data-end=\\\"631\\\" data-start=\\\"585\\\">Overnight stay at the hotel in Chandigarh.<\\/strong><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Friday\",\"day\":\"Day 7\",\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Chandigarh \\u2013 Departure\",\"date\":\"02-05-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast, check out from the hotel and proceed for your <strong data-end=\\\"223\\\" data-start=\\\"170\\\">transfer to Chandigarh Railway Station or Airport<\\/strong> for your onward journey, carrying fond memories of your trip.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"to\":\"Chandigarh (IXC)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"874\",\"dep_date\":\"26 Apr 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"26 Apr 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"01:25 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"03:50 PM\",\"fare\":\"21044\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Chandigarh (IXC)\",\"to\":\"Kolkata (CCU)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"6041\",\"dep_date\":\"02 May 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"02 May 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"08:00 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"10:20 PM\",\"fare\":\"20096\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"26\\/04\\/2025\",\"city\":\"SHIMLA\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe King Room\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel The Orchid\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"28\\/04\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"15580\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"28\\/04\\/2025\",\"city\":\"MANALI\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Woodrock Luxury Boutique\",\"room_type\":\"Super Deluxe Mountain\\u00a0View\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"01\\/05\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"21000\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"01\\/05\\/2025\",\"city\":\"CHANDIGARH\",\"check_out\":\"02\\/05\\/2025\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Regenta Central Cassia\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"rate\":\"5800\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <strong>Ex-Kolkata.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nts</strong>&nbsp;Accommodation Hotel The Orchid at&nbsp;<strong>Shimla.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>03&nbsp;Nts</strong>&nbsp;Accommodation Hotel Woodrock Luxury Boutique&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>Manali.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Nts</strong>&nbsp;Accommodation Hotel Regenta Central Cassia&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>Chandigarh.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Double Room</strong>with&nbsp;<strong>Breakfast &amp; Dinner</strong><strong>.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>01 Sedan Car</strong>&nbsp;for all transfers &amp; tours on disposal basis.</li>\n	<li>Toll, Parking, driver’s Bata, road tax &amp; fuel charges.</li>\n	<li><strong>All taxes.</strong></li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"18\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":41140,\"hotel_cost\":42380,\"transport_cost\":\"26000\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":109520,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 19713.6\",\"selling_price\":129233.60000000000582076609134674072265625}', 'MZQ/0669/042025', 129600, 64800, 0, '2025-04-24 12:58:06', '2025-04-25 08:20:21', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(681, 'Mr Anju Malhotra', 'MZ CDG', '9810621916', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'KERALA', '2025-06-05', 6, 0, 4, '[]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Chandigarh (IXC)\",\"to\":\"Bangalore (BLR)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"6634\",\"dep_date\":\"05 Jun 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"05 Jun 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"08:25 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"11:30 AM\",\"fare\":38400},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Bangalore (BLR)\",\"to\":\"Cochin (COK)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"703\",\"dep_date\":\"05 Jun 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"05 Jun 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"12:45 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:55 PM\",\"fare\":0},{\"id\":3,\"from\":\"Trivandrum (TRV)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"2739\",\"dep_date\":\"11 Jun 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"11 Jun 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"12:30 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"03:55 PM\",\"fare\":38952},{\"id\":4,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Chandigarh (IXC)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"2149\",\"dep_date\":\"11 Jun 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"11 Jun 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"05:25 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:20 PM\",\"fare\":0}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"05\\/06\\/2025\",\"city\":\"MUNNAR\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Misty Mountain Resort\",\"room_type\":\"Valley View\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"07\\/06\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"19800\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"07\\/06\\/2025\",\"city\":\"ALLEPPEY\",\"hotel_name\":\"Deluxe Houseboat\",\"room_type\":\"02 B\\/R Deluxe Houseboat AC\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"ap\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"08\\/06\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"12500\"},{\"id\":4,\"check_in\":\"08\\/06\\/2025\",\"city\":\"KOVALAM\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Seaface\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room Sea View\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"11\\/06\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"31900\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airfare as mentioned above <strong><em>Ex-Chandigarh.</em></strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nights&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation at&nbsp;<strong>Munnar</strong><strong>.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Night&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation at&nbsp;<strong>Allepey.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>03&nbsp;Nights&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>Kovalam.</strong></li>\n	<li>Buffet/Fixed Menu <strong>Breakfast + Dinner @ </strong>Munnar/Thekkady, <strong>Breakfast @</strong>Kovalam,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>&amp; <strong>All Meals&nbsp;@ </strong>Allepey.</li>\n	<li><strong>Day Trip to Kanyakumari.</strong></li>\n	<li>All Tours &amp; Transfer&nbsp;by&nbsp;<strong>A/C Innova&nbsp;</strong>as per the itinerary (A/C will be switched off during hilly drives).</li>\n	<li>Toll charges, Parking charges, Driver allowances</li>\n	<li>All taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"15\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":77352,\"hotel_cost\":64200,\"transport_cost\":\"36000\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":177552,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 26632.8\",\"selling_price\":204184.7999999999883584678173065185546875,\"profit_figure\":null,\"percent_of_amount\":\"0.00%\"}', 'MZQ/0670/042025', 204560, 51140, 20958, '2025-04-25 13:09:37', '2025-04-26 06:22:21', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `quotation` (`id`, `guest_name`, `ref_name`, `mobile_no`, `email`, `destination`, `tentative_date`, `nights`, `children`, `adults`, `itineraries`, `flights`, `trains`, `hotels`, `terms_conditions`, `children_ages`, `inclusion`, `exclusion`, `payment_policy`, `cancellation_policy`, `costing`, `ref_id`, `total`, `adult_cost`, `child_cost`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_confirmed`, `hide_note`, `other_details`, `is_feedback_sent`, `is_feedback_received`) VALUES
(682, 'Mrs. Archita Gupta', 'Mrs. Dimple Gupta', '9650105888', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'BHUTAN 4*', '2025-05-23', 7, 0, 2, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"ARRIVE BAGDOGRA BY AIR & TRANSFER TO PHUENTSHOLING (180 KMS \\/ 05 \\u2013 06 HRS DRIVE)\",\"date\":\"23-05-2025 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>On arrival at Bagdogra airport, you will be met &amp; transferred to Phuentsholing followed by immigration process.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Phuentsholing is the gateway to the South, Phuentsholing is a thriving commercial centre on the northern edge of the Indian plains. Situated directly at the base of the Himalayan foothills, it is a fascinating mixture of Indian and Bhutanese, a perfect example of mingling of people and their culture.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Overnight at the hotel in Phuentsholing<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"PHUENTSHOLING \\u2013 THIMPHU (180 KMS \\/ 06 \\u2013 07 HRS DRIVE)\",\"date\":\"24-05-2025 Saturday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>After early breakfast; check out from the hotel &amp; drive to<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>On arrival in Thimphu, check into the hotel. The capital town of Bhutan and the centre of Government, religion and commerce, Thimphu is a unique city with unusual mixture of modern development alongside ancient traditions. With the population of about 90,000 it is perhaps still the world\\u2019s only capital city without a traffic light.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Afterwards visit to Buddha Point (Kuensel Phodrang). Located at a short drive from Thimphu city centre, visitors can get a good overview of the Thimphu valley from the Buddha point (KuenselPhodrang). You can pay your obeisance and offer prayers to the Buddha, the largest statue in the country and then walk around and take a glimpse of the valley.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>King\'s Memorial Chorten continuously circumambulated by people, murmuring mantras and spinning their prayer wheels. Construction of this landmark was the idea of Bhutan\\u2019s third king, His Majesty Jigme Dorji Wangchuk (\\u201cthe father of modern Bhutan\\u201d) who has wished to erect monument to world peace and prosperity. Completed in 1974 after his untimely death, it serves both as a memorial to the Late King and as a monument to peace.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Later visit to Trashichhoedzong: This impressive fortress\\/monastery houses Secretariat building, the throne room of His Majesty, the King and various government offices. It is also the summer residence of Chief Abbot and central monk body.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Evening an exploratory walk around Thimphu Main Street and market area. Also visit the Local Crafts Bazaar, to browse through example of Bhutan\'s fine traditional arts. Here you can buy hand-woven textiles, Thangkha paintings, masks, ceramics, slate and wood carvings, jewellery, interesting items made from local materials.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Overnight at the hotel in Thimphu (Altitude 2400m).<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"THIMPHU SIGHTSEEING:\",\"date\":\"25-05-2025 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>After breakfast, sightseeing in Thimphu valley including visit to the following: The National Library, housing an extensive collection of priceless Buddhist manuscripts; the Institute for Zorig Chusum (commonly known as the Painting School) where students undergo a 6-year training course in Bhutan\\u2019s 13 traditional arts and crafts. Later visit Textile Museum, which provides insight into Bhutan\\u2019s one of the most distinct art form. Also visit Simply Bhutan, a living museum and studio encapsulating the cultural heritage of the Bhutanese people.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>After lunch,&nbsp;take a short drive (15 km) to Pangri Zampa, 16th century one of the oldest monasteries in Bhutan located just north of Thimphu. Here is a monastic school where Buddhist student\\u2019s monks learn Lamaism and astrology based on Buddhist philosophy.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Afternoon visit, Zilukha Nunnery is also known as Druthob Goemba. Housing around 60 nuns in its premises, a visit to the site energizes the soul because of its peaceful surroundings, which lures one\'s mind to never leave the site. This is the biggest nunnery in Bhutan and the interactive session with nuns is very informative. It is a good experience to know about their lifestyle from themselves. Knowing about their experiences, beliefs and education is quite a fun activity.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Overnight at the hotel in Thimphu<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"THIMPHU \\u2013 PUNAKHA (75 KMS \\/ 03 HRS DRIVE)\",\"date\":\"26-05-2025 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>After breakfast at hotel, drive to Punakha across Dochula pass (3O8Om). In Bhutan, the passes are marked by a large Bhutanese Chorten and prayer flag. Dochula pass offers the most spectacular view over the high peaks of the eastern Himalayas on a clear day.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Enroute proceed for the day excursion to Chimi Lhakhang (from hotel it is about 15 minutes\\u2019 drive till motorable road and then walk starts through paddy fields and villages. This is total about 1\\u00bd hour walk, including both way). The Chimi Lhakhang, situated on a hillock in the centre of the valley, also known as the temple of fertility. It is widely believed that couples who do not have children and wanting one, if they pray at this temple, they are usually blessed with a child very soon. The trail leads across rice fields to the tiny settlement of Pana, meaning \\u2018field\\u2019. A walk through the village near the temple will give you rare glimpses into the daily life and lifestyle of the villagers.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>After checking into hotel, proceed to visit Punakha Dzong, a massive structure built at the junction of two rivers. It was the capital of Bhutan until 1955, and still serves as the winter residence of the monk body.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Evening can be spent exploring Punakha village located right on the bank of river.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Overnight at the hotel in Punakha.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"PUNAKHA \\u2013 PARO (120 KMS \\/ 4\\u00bd HRS DRIVE APPROX)\",\"date\":\"27-05-2025 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>After breakfast, drive to Paro along scenic highway, enroute visit SimtokhaDzong, the oldest fortress of the country built in 1627 which now houses the School for Buddhist studies.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>On arrival in Paro, check into the hotel. After lunch, proceed to visit Ta Dzong, originally built as Watchtower, which now houses National Museum. The extensive collection includes antique Thangkha paintings, textiles, weapons &amp;armour, household objects and a rich assortment of natural and historic artifacts.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Ta Dzong visit immediately followed by a short walk down the trail to visit Rinpung Dzong (ParoDzong), meaning (\\u201cfortress of the heap of jewels\\u201d), which has a long and fascinating history. Along the wooden galleries lining the inner courtyard are fine wall paintings illustrating Buddhist lore such as four friends, the old man of long life, the wheel of life, scenes from the life of Milarepa, Mount. Sumeru and other cosmic Mandala.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Overnight at the hotel in Paro.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"PARO ---TREKING TO TAKSHANG MONASTERY ALSO CALLED TIGER NEST.\",\"date\":\"28-05-2025 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>After breakfast excursion to Taktshang Monastery or Tiger\\u2019s Nest (approx. 5 hours walk):&nbsp; It is one of the most famous of Bhutan\\u2019s monasteries, perched on the side of a cliff 900m above the Paro valley floor. It is said that Guru Rinpoche arrived here on the back of a tigress and meditated at this monastery and hence it is called \\u2018Tiger\\u2019s Nest\\u2019. This site has been recognised as a most sacred place and visited by ShabdrungNgawangNamgyal in 1646 and now visited by all Bhutanese at least once in their lifetime. On 19 April, 1998, a fire severely damaged the main structure of building but now this Bhutanese jewel has been restored to its original splendour.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p>Or<\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>PARO \\u2013 HAA VALLEY EXCURSION \\u2013 PARO---@ ADDITIONAL 8500 AS IT IS OUT OF CITY.<br \\/>\\n\\tStart the day early for a full day excursion to Haa via Chele-la pass (3800Mts \\/ 12465Fts, 65 Kms \\/ 02 to 03Hrs \\u2013 One way) with packed or early breakfast. Visit Haa Dzong, Lhakhang Karpo, Lhakhang Nagpo, Wangchulo Dzong. Evening you drive back to Paro. Overnight at the hotel<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Overnight at the hotel in Paro.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":7,\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"PHUENTSHOLING (170 KMS \\/ 06 \\u2013 07 HRS DRIVE)\",\"date\":\"29-05-2025 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li>After breakfast; check out from the hotel &amp; enjoy the scenic drive to Phuentsholing.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Upon arrival; check into the hotel. The gateway to the south, Phuentsholing is a thriving commercial centre on the northern edge of the Indian plains. Situated directly at the base of the Himalayan foothills, it is a fascinating mixture of Indian and Bhutanese, a perfect example of mingling of people and their culture.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Overnight at the hotel in Phuentsholing<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":8,\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"PHUENTSHOLING \\u2013 BAGDOGRA (180 KMS \\/ 05 \\u2013 06 HRS DRIVE).\",\"date\":\"30-05-2025 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<ul>\\n\\t<li class=\\\"section1\\\" style=\\\"text-align:justify\\\"><em><strong><span style=\\\"font-size:12pt\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\\\"><span style=\\\"font-size:10.0pt\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\\\">Breakfast at the hotel followed by the immigration clearance, you will be dropped at Bagdogra airport to board your flight for onward journey.<\\/span><\\/span><\\/span><\\/span><\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Bangalore (BLR)\",\"to\":\"Bagdogra (IXB)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"6018\",\"dep_date\":\"23 May 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"23 May 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"03:40 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"06:30 PM\",\"fare\":13496},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Bagdogra (IXB)\",\"to\":\"Bangalore (BLR)\",\"name\":\"Akasa Air\",\"fno\":\"1373\",\"dep_date\":\"30 May 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"30 May 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"10:55 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"02:10 PM\",\"fare\":20334}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"23\\/05\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Phuentsholing\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Tashi Namgyel \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"25\\/05\\/2025\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"25\\/05\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Thimphu\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Ariya \\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"27\\/05\\/2025\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"27\\/05\\/2025\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Himalayan Key Forest Resort \\/ Similar\",\"city\":\"Paro\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"28\\/05\\/2025\"},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"28\\/05\\/2025\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Rkpo Green Resort \\/ Similar\",\"city\":\"Punakha\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"map\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"30\\/05\\/2025\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare <em><strong>Ex-Bangalore.</strong></em></li>\n	<li>07 night accommodation on double sharing basis.</li>\n	<li>Tourist permit for Bhutan.</li>\n	<li>SUV within Bhutan , Electric BYD or MG or similar</li>\n	<li>Pick up/drop from Bagdogra Airport in Breeza or Dezire</li>\n	<li>Daily 2 meals (Breakfast &amp; Dinner) at hotel.</li>\n	<li>A qualified &amp; Licensed English-speaking guide</li>\n	<li>Sustainable Development Fee (SDF) for permit</li>\n	<li>All sightseeing as per tour plan.</li>\n	<li>02 Bottled per day&nbsp; mineral water at the start of the tour</li>\n	<li>Full service &amp; assistance before, during and after you Bhutan trip.</li>\n	<li>GST</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"15\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":33830,\"land_cost\":\"140800\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":174630,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 26194.5\",\"selling_price\":200824.5}', 'MZQ/0671/042025', 200884, 100442, 0, '2025-04-28 13:18:40', '2025-04-28 15:02:05', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(683, 'Mr. Akram', 'BNI Josh', '9709100140', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'VIETNAM 4*', '2025-06-09', 7, 0, 2, '[{\"title\":\"Monday\",\"day\":\"Day 1\",\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HANOI ARRIVAL - HANOI - HA LONG OVERNIGHT ON BOAT - TRANSFER BY SHUTTLE BUS\",\"date\":\"09-06-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Upon arrival at Hanoi\'s Noi Bai International Airport you will be welcomed by our driver holding a sign with your name on it. After approximately 50 minutes to 1-hour transfer, you will be at your hotel for check-in (early check-in with breakfast included).&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Leave Hanoi for a 2.5-hour drive to Ha Long Bay including a 20-minutes stop on the way. Arrive at the jetty in Ha Long City towards noon and proceed with check-in formalities. Be welcomed onboard and have lunch will be served while cruising towards the bay itself. In the afternoon, enjoy some visits and\\/or activities (depending on each boat\\u2019s itinerary) or just spend some time relaxing on board. Towards the end of the day the boat sets anchor for the night among the karst formations. Dinner is served on board.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Meal: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight on Ha Long cruise<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Tuesday\",\"day\":\"Day 2\",\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HA LONG - TRANSFER BACK HANOI BY SHUTTLE BUS - HANOI TRANSFER TO TRAIN STATION (NO GUIDE)\",\"date\":\"10-06-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Enjoy the fresh morning in the middle of the bay, the sun rises on Ha Long in the morning and breakfast is served (brunch on some boats) while the vessels cruise slowly through the magnificent rock formations and back towards port. Disembark and transfer back to Hanoi. Arrive in Hanoi late in the afternoon.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Free at leisure until transfer by our driver to the train station for overnight train to Lao Cai.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Meal: Breakfast, Lunch (Or 1 brunch)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at 2 beds VIP Cabin<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Wednesday\",\"day\":\"Day 3\",\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"SAPA ARRIVAL - HALF DAY SILVER WATERFALL & HEAVEN\'S GATE\",\"date\":\"11-06-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Early morning, arrive at Lao Cai train station, pick up by our guide &amp; driver and transfer to Sapa. (Early check-in with breakfast included)<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Transfer by car west of Sapa about 30 minutes to Silver Waterfall. The fall, drops from an altitude of 200 meters, is the upstream of Muong Hoa stream. Take a short walk to the waterfall where you can get great views of the surrounding mountains and lush forests of the Hoang Lien Son National Park. The waterfall is best seen in the rainy season from May to November.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Continue 10 minutes by car to Heaven Gate, located at the highest point of Tram Ton Pass. At 1900m this is Vietnam\\u2019s highest mountain pass, and acts as a dividing line between two weather fronts. From Heaven Gate, you\\u2019ll fantastic views of Hoang Lien Son mountain range, and Fansipan Mountain, dubbed as the roof of Indochina at the height of 3,143 meters above sea level.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;Meal: Breakfast<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel in Sapa<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Thursday\",\"day\":\"Day 4\",\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"FULL DAY CAT CAT VILLAGE & DISCOVER FANSIPAN MOUNTAIN - SAPA - TRANSFER BACK TO HANOI BY TRAIN\",\"date\":\"12-06-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Take a short car ride just 3 km out of Sa Pa to Cat Cat village inhabited by a community of the Hmong ethnic minority people. The village is known as a cultural site since many traditions and customs of the Black Hmong are still preserved to date. The traditional trades of brocade making and silver and bronze smith are still practiced nowadays by villagers after numerous generations of their ancestors. You can see Hmong women by their looms weaving fabrics, which will be later on dyed with sap from leaves for the desired coloration. Your walk through the village will take you to Tien Sa waterfall where a French-built hydropower station has been in service since 1920. Leave Cat Cat village and trek a 5 km winding trail by mountainside along a small river in a tranquil setting of hilly land with terraced paddy fields. Arrive in Y Linh Ho village, another Hmong residence characterized by simple houses built of bamboo and clay. Wander around to observe and interact with villagers dressed in elaborate silver-studded clothing and leggings.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Start the tour to the Cable Car station where you will get on cabin and take a 15-minute ride by cable car. At 6292,5m long, this is the longest non-stop three rope cable car in the world. Continue to climb about 600 steps to reach the summit of Mount Fansipan. Spend time to admire the beautiful natural landscape of Sapa, Hoang Lien Son, Muong Hoa valley and the magnificent Hoang Lien Son mountain range.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Transfer to Lao Cai train station to transfer back to Ha Noi<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Meal: Breakfast<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at 4 beds Deluxe cabin<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Friday\",\"day\":\"Day 5\",\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HANOI ARRIVAL (NO GUIDE) - HANOI DEPARTURE (NO GUIDE) - HOI AN ARRIVAL\",\"date\":\"13-06-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Our driver will wait and pick you up at Hanoi train station to transfer to Noi Bai International Airport for flight departure<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Arrival Da Nang airport, pick up by our guide &amp; driver then transfer to Hoi An.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Meal: None<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel in Hoi An<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Saturday\",\"day\":\"Day 6\",\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"FULL DAY DA NANG - BA NA HILL - GOLDEN BRIDGE - DA NANG DEPARTURE - HANOI ARRIVAL\",\"date\":\"14-06-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning, departure for Ba Na Hills, or Chua Mount (Mount of Goddess), by passing the sea-shore on Nguyen Tat Thanh Street, one of the most beautiful roads of Da Nang City and Red Beach.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;Arrive at the Cable car station at the foot of Ba Na Mountain. Enjoy the first leg Cable car, which achieves two Guinness World records as the longest non-stop cable car (5,042m) and the highest non-stop cable car (1,292m). The cable cars were built to feed the mountaintop of Ba Na Hills, but they\\u2019re also the perfect way to get spectacular views of Danang and the surrounding forests.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;Upon reaching Ba Na Hills, start the trip with a visit to Golden Bridge which is designed to connect the cable car station with the main gardens of this mountaintop. It is also to provide a scenic overlook and tourist attraction. The gold-colored walkway is lined with purple Lobelia Chrysanthemums and is 150 meters long with two giant hands, constructed of fiberglass and wire mesh. These two hands appear like stone hands that support the structure.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;After the Golden Bridge, we\\u2019ll continue to visit Le Jardin d\\u2019 Amour, remains of French Villas and Ling Ung Pagoda with 27m high Buddha status. We then leave the Le Jardin for the second cable car station to visit the top of mountain where there are remains of the old French villas found. Start conquering the Peak of Chua Mount at the height of 1,487m, viewing the whole Da Nang city under the cluster of white clouds. After the Peak of Chua Mount, visit the trail of Dreaming Stream, Rainbow Waterfall, Suspension Bridge, Golden Valley, and ruined Opera House. Play with wild monkeys and take photos. Freely until time back to Cable car Station to return to the the foot of the Mountain. Transfer back to Da Nang City.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Free at leisure until transfer to Da Nang airport for flight departure<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Upon arrival at Hanoi\'s Noi Bai International Airport you will be welcomed by our guide holding a sign with your name on it. After approximately 50 minutes to 1 hour transfer, you will be at your hotel for check-in<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Meal: Breakfast<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel in Hanoi<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Sunday\",\"day\":\"Day 7\",\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"FULL DAY HANOI CITY TOUR\",\"date\":\"15-06-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Morning, start a full day city tour beginning with the Ho Chi Minh Complex which features the life of Ho Chi Minh, the nation\\u2019s founder. Explore Ba Dinh Square, an important point of pilgrimage for many Vietnamese, the Presidential Palace, Ho Chi Minh Museum and the rural style Ho Chi Minh\\u2019s house on stilts where he lived and worked. Stop by one of Hanoi\\u2019s icons, the One Pillar Pagoda, built in the 11th Century in dedication to Bodhisattva Avalokiteshvara or Buddha of Compassion and reminiscent of a lotus blossom rising from a pond. Continue to the Temple of Literature, known as the first university of Vietnam built in 1070 by the Ly Dynasty to honor Confucius, sages and outstanding Vietnamese scholars.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Afternoon, visit Hoan Kiem Lake or \\u201cReturned Sword Lake\\u201d which originated from a legend of a sacred sword. On an islet in the lake, there locates Ngoc Son Temple which is accessible by a classically red painted wooden bridge. Touring through the Old Quarter, famous for its ancient streets representing traditional trades from the past by cyclo and enjoy a coffee at a local caf\\u00e9.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Meal: Breakfast<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel in Hanoi<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Monday\",\"day\":\"Day 8\",\"index\":7,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"HANOI DEPARTURE (NO GUIDE)\",\"date\":\"16-06-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>You are free at leisure before being transferred by our driver to Noi Bai International Airport for flight departure<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Meal: Breakfast<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Hanoi (HAN)\",\"to\":\"Da Nang (DAD)\",\"name\":\"Vietnam Airlines\",\"fno\":\"169\",\"dep_date\":\"13 Jun 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"13 Jun 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"11:45 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:10 PM\",\"fare\":\"27089\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Da Nang (DAD)\",\"to\":\"Hanoi (HAN)\",\"name\":\"Vietnam Airlines\",\"fno\":\"7168\",\"dep_date\":\"14 Jun 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"15 Jun 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"10:40 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"12:05 AM\",\"fare\":null}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"08\\/06\\/2025\",\"city\":\"HA NOI\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Minasi Premium\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"09\\/06\\/2025\",\"rate\":null},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"09\\/06\\/2025\",\"hotel_name\":\"La Pandora Cruise\",\"city\":\"HA LONG\",\"room_type\":\"Suite Balcony\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"ap\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"10\\/06\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"0\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"10\\/06\\/2025\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Pistachio Sapa\",\"room_type\":\"Superior Valley View\",\"city\":\"SA PA\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"12\\/06\\/2025\",\"meal\":\"cp\",\"rooms\":1,\"rate\":null},{\"id\":4,\"check_in\":\"13\\/06\\/2025\",\"city\":\"HOI AN\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel La Charm Hoi An & Spa\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"check_out\":\"14\\/06\\/2025\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"rate\":null},{\"id\":4,\"check_in\":\"14\\/06\\/2025\",\"city\":\"HA NOI\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Flower Garden\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"16\\/06\\/2025\",\"rate\":null}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li><strong>Airfare HAN-DAD-HAN.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>07 Nights</strong> Accommodation&nbsp;in double/ twin room with daily breakfast</li>\n	<li>Services of a driver and private air-conditioned vehicle during all tours and transfers</li>\n	<li><em><strong>Two way Hanoi – Sapa – Ha Noi by train</strong></em></li>\n	<li>One night cruise on Ha Long Bay with 2 ways transferred by shuttle bus</li>\n	<li>Meal as specified in the itinerary</li>\n	<li>Experienced English-speaking guide during all tours and transfers (except for arrival/departure from Hanoi (1st stay))</li>\n	<li>Entrance fees for all visits as mentioned in the itinerary</li>\n	<li>Mineral water is available as complimentary</li>\n	<li><em><strong>Vietnam Tourist Visa.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><em><strong>All Taxes</strong></em></li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"line-height:14.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Tipping policy: 5 USD per person per day</span></span></b></span></span></span></li>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"16\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":27089,\"hotel_cost\":null,\"land_cost\":\"146000\",\"visa_cost\":\"5000\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":178089,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 28494.24\",\"selling_price\":206583.23999999999068677425384521484375}', 'MZQ/0672/052025', 204448, 102224, 0, '2025-05-01 07:57:58', '2025-05-09 05:55:33', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(684, 'Dr. Niraj', 'Gopal Das CCL', '9430360757', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'NEPAL 4*', '2025-05-20', 5, 0, 7, '[{\"title\":\"Tuesday\",\"day\":\"Day 1\",\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu\",\"date\":\"20-05-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Meeting at railway station upon arrival by Office Personnel. Transfer to hotel. Kathmandu is the capital of Nepal and the Kathmandu Valley is the political and cultural heart of the Kingdom.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>The urban sprawl that makes up modern Kathmandu is in fact two cities, Patan and Kathmandu.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;After short relaxation at the hotel, visit one of the Hindu culture in Nepal,&nbsp;Pashupatinath.&nbsp; This is the place where holy saddhus pray. The&nbsp;Pashupatinath Temple&nbsp;is a famous, sacred&nbsp;Hindu temple&nbsp;dedicated to&nbsp;Pashupatinath&nbsp;and is located on the banks of the&nbsp;Bagmati River&nbsp;5 kilometres north-east of&nbsp;Kathmandu Valley&nbsp;in the eastern city of Kathmandu&nbsp;the&nbsp;capital&nbsp;of&nbsp;Nepal. This temple is considered one of the sacred temples of&nbsp;Hindu&nbsp;faith .The temple serves as the seat of the national deity, Lord Pashupatinath. This temple complex is on&nbsp;UNESCO World Heritage Sites\'s list Since 1979.&nbsp;This \\\"extensive Hindu temple precinct\\\" is a \\\"sprawling collection of temples, ashrams, images and inscriptions raised over the centuries along the banks of the sacred Bagmati river\\\".<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 03 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Wednesday\",\"day\":\"Day 2\",\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu-Pokhara\",\"date\":\"21-05-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Drive to Pokhara. Pokhara is 210 kms from Kathmandu and is a 7 hours drive approx.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>From Pokhara town (2,352 feet) in good weather there are splendid views right from the hotel.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>On the way you have an option at an extra cost of doing the river rafting (Inr 3000 per person ) or visit the Manakamna Temple \\u201c Goddess of Fulfilling Wishes\\u201d where you are taken by a cable ride<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>( Inr 670 per person payable directly) of 10 mins one way.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at Hotel.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Thursday\",\"day\":\"Day 3\",\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pokhara\",\"date\":\"22-05-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>This morning you will go for a excursion trip to&nbsp;Sarangkot. Sarangkot is the most popular tourist destination from where the tourists can enjoy the great view of the Pokhara Valley and the magnificent view of the Himalayas. Sarangkot is only 13 kms from Lake Side, Pokhara. It is the highest view point for a sunrise at an altitude of 1592mtsh. It is&nbsp; cooler than Pokhara. Ccan be reached easily within<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>45 to 60 minutes by a vehiclefrom Pokhara. Many tourists come to Sarangkot for sunrise.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>From Sarangkot, on the northern direction we can see Dhaulagiri in the far west. Annapurna range is visible when the weather is clear on the same side. On the southern direction the village overlooks the city of Pokhara and its lake on the north-western outskirts of the city.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 03 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>This afternoon you will visit&nbsp;Bindebasini Temple. This is one of the oldest temples in Pokhara was a part of Kaski Kingdom, the main deity of the temple,Goddess Durga, was brought from India . Apart from the peace and tranquility that can be felt in this region, the premises of the temple offers a good view of the Himalaya on a clear day. The temple is in the area of the bazaar, hence,a journey of the old bazaar can be combined with a visit to the temple. Sightseeing to&nbsp;Devi\\u2019s fall,&nbsp;also known as Patale Chango is an awesome waterfall lying 2 km southwest of Pokhara. During summer and rainy season, the waterfall takes its real form, with gushing water splashing and making its way through the rocks. Just opposite of Devi\\u2019s fall, on the other side of the road, there is&nbsp;Gupteshwor Cave. This cave is popular for the different natural forms made from limestone deposits. Photography is strictly prohibited inside the cave.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel.&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/em>( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 03 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Friday\",\"day\":\"Day 4\",\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pokhara\",\"date\":\"23-05-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Today&nbsp;you will visit Pumdikot and World Peace Pagoda.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Visit Pumdikot:<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Pumdikot view tower in Pokhara is one of the most incredible vantage points situated in Nepal. Known for its 3 tiered Shiva Statue and the picturesque views of Annapurna Himalayan Range, Machhapuchre, Dhaulagiri, Manaslu and many other neighbouring mountains, Pumdikot is attracting people in its periphery though the theme park hasn\\u2019t been completed yet.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>The Pumdikot is an emerging destination around Pokhara that features a shiva statue, natural settlement, lake view, valley view, mountains and peaceful scenery. The Shiva idol in the Phumdibhumdi village is about 108 ft tall, but the actual Shiva\\u2019s sitting statue is 51 ft tall.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>The theme park of Pumdikot is being built on 22 Ropanis of land. The total area includes 108 Shiva Lingas, 108 stairs to reach the idol, 18 shutter rooms, ticket counters, premises area and viewpoints. A plan to construct Martyr\\u2019s memorial park, model of mount Sumeru featuring Shiva and Parvati is also on the pipeline. The Pumdikot area is designed to be accessible for differently-abled people as well.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Visit World Peace pagoda:<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\\n\\n<p>The World Peace Pagoda in Pokhara is painted&nbsp; a brilliant white and sits atop &nbsp;a hill overlooking the Annapurna Mountain range which reflect off Lake Phewa Taal below. It is the thusly one of the more serene peace&nbsp; pagoda in the world.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>It is built after world war 2 by the Buddhist Monks from Japanese Nipponzan Myohoji organization&nbsp; this word Peace Pagoda is one of over 80 World Peace Pagodas in the world&nbsp;today. &nbsp;&nbsp;They are built to inspire peace for all races &amp; creeds.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 05 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Saturday\",\"day\":\"Day 5\",\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pokhara-Kathmandu\",\"date\":\"24-05-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Retracing the same path, drive back to Kathmandu and transfer to Hotel. Rest day at leisure. One can indulge in shopping or visit the casinos trying your&nbsp; lady luck on your own.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Sunday\",\"day\":\"Day 6\",\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu-Airport\",\"date\":\"25-05-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>This morning your tour will take you for a visit to&nbsp;Patan. Also known as&nbsp; Lalitpur&nbsp; , the city of beauty is separated from Kathmandu only by the Bagmati River and is the second largest town in the valley. Lalitpur is fragmented from other cities due to its substantive architectural ancient masterpieces. Patan\'s central Durbar Square is absolutely packed with temples: Its an architectural center point with a far greater concentration of temples per sq. meter than in Kathamandu or Bhaktapur. Within&nbsp; the city also lies the Tibetan refugee center, home to most of the valley\'s Tibetan population.&nbsp; While technically refugees, the Tibetans are some of the wealthiest people in the valley because of the carpet industry they operate.&nbsp; For those looking to bring home a fine Tibetan carpet, this is the place to shop. You will then go to&nbsp;Swayambhunath&nbsp;the golden spire of the 5th-century Swayambhu stupa is adorned with a colorful fluttering of prayer flags; it crowns a hill overlooking the Kathmandu Valley and offers fantastic views over the city of Kathmandu. Swayambhunath is one of the most recognizable symbols in Nepal and the painted eyes of Buddha watch all who ascend the worn stone steps.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 03 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Later, you will be transferred to the airport in time to board your railway for onward journey.<\\/p>\"}]', '[]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"20\\/05\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Kathmandu\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Mulberry\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room + Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"21\\/05\\/2025\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"21\\/05\\/2025\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Sarowar\",\"city\":\"Pokhara\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room + Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":3,\"check_out\":\"24\\/05\\/2025\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"24\\/05\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Kathmandu\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Mulberry\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room + Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":3,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"25\\/05\\/2025\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserve