condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[{\"age\":10},{\"age\":5}]', '<ul>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nights accommodation</strong> at Hotel Meerz at&nbsp;<strong>Srinagar</strong>.</li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Night&nbsp;accommodation</strong> at Houseboat Jewel in Crown Nigeen lake&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>Houseboat</strong>.</li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Night&nbsp;accommodation</strong> at Hotel Welcome Resort Kp Road Langanbal at&nbsp;<strong>Pahalgam</strong></li>\n	<li>Accommodation in&nbsp;<strong>03&nbsp;Double Rooms + 02 Extra Bed.</strong></li>\n	<li>MAP&nbsp;(<strong>Breakfast + Dinner</strong>) in Kashmir Tour.</li>\n	<li>Srinagar&nbsp;<strong>Airport Pickup &amp; Drop</strong>.</li>\n	<li><em><strong>16&nbsp;Seater URBANIA&nbsp;</strong></em>for transfers &amp; Sightseeing as per Itinerary.&nbsp;</li>\n	<li><strong>01 Hour Shikara Ride</strong>&nbsp;in Dal lake</li>\n	<li>Medical Kit in Taxi</li>\n	<li>Driver Charges, Toll, and Parking included&nbsp;</li>\n	<li>Meeting &amp; Assistance on Arrival&nbsp;/Departure.</li>\n	<li>All applicable taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Any kind of personal expenses.</li>\n	<li>Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Phone Calls, Guide Fee &amp; Camera Fee.</li>\n	<li>Anything not mentioned in the inclusions above.</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"8\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":0,\"land_cost\":\"135500\"},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":135500,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 10840\",\"selling_price\":146340,\"profit_figure\":null,\"percent_of_amount\":\"7.00%\"}', 'MZQ/0695/062025', 146247, 18245, 9266, '2025-06-10 09:06:13', '2025-06-12 07:09:06', 0, 1, NULL, 0, 0),
(707, 'Mr. Abhishek Dokania', 'BNI', '7003447986', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'NEPAL', '2025-07-13', 5, 0, 3, '[{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":1,\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu\",\"date\":\"13-07-2025 Sunday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Meeting at airport upon arrival by Office Personnel. Transfer to hotel. Kathmandu is the capital of Nepal and the Kathmandu Valley is the political and cultural heart of the Kingdom.The urban sprawl that makes up modern Kathmandu is in fact two cities, Patan and Kathmandu.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":2,\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu\",\"date\":\"14-07-2025 Monday\",\"todo\":\"<p>This morning you will be taken&nbsp; for a visit of the Hindu culture in Nepal, Pashupatinath.&nbsp; This is the place where holy saddhus pray. The&nbsp;Pashupatinath Temple&nbsp;is a famous, sacred&nbsp;Hindu temple&nbsp;dedicated to&nbsp;Pashupatinath&nbsp;and is located on the banks of the&nbsp;Bagmati River&nbsp;5 kilometres north-east of&nbsp;Kathmandu Valley&nbsp;in the eastern city of Kathmandu&nbsp;the&nbsp;capital&nbsp;of&nbsp;Nepal. This temple is considered one of the sacred temples of&nbsp;Hindu&nbsp;faith .The temple serves as the seat of the national deity, Lord Pashupatinath. This temple complex is on&nbsp;UNESCO World Heritage Sites\'s list Since 1979.&nbsp;This \\\"extensive Hindu temple precinct\\\" is a \\\"sprawling collection of temples, ashrams, images and inscriptions raised over the centuries along the banks of the sacred Bagmati river\\\". We then continue to the holiest shrine for the Buddhist culture in Nepal, Bouddhanath, with its large stupa, this is the place where all devout Buddhists come for a pilgrimage. After completion of these two spots, you will be taken take you for a visit to Patan. Also known as&nbsp; Lalitpur&nbsp; , the city of beauty is separated from Kathmandu only by the Bagmati River and is the second largest town in the valley. Lalitpur is fragmented from other cities due to its substantive architectural ancient masterpieces. Patan\'s central Durbar Square is absolutely packed with temples: Its an architectural center point with a far greater concentration of temples per sq. meter than in Kathamandu or Bhaktapur. Within&nbsp; the city also lies the Tibetan refugee center, home to most of the valley\'s Tibetan population.&nbsp; While technically refugees,<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>the Tibetans are some of the wealthiest people in the valley because of the carpet industry they operate.&nbsp; For those looking to bring home a fine Tibetan carpet, this is the place to shop. You will then go to Swayambhunath the golden spire of the 5th-century Swayambhu stupa is adorned with a colorful fluttering of prayer flags; it crowns a hill overlooking the Kathmandu Valley and offers fantastic views over the city of Kathmandu. Swayambhunath is one of the most recognizable symbols in Nepal and the painted eyes of Buddha watch all who ascend the worn stone steps.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Later visit the Budanilkantha Temple which is also known as the Sleeping Vishnu Temple.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Budhanilkantha Temple, located in&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Budhanilkantha\\\" title=\\\"Budhanilkantha\\\">Budhanilkantha<\\/a>,&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Nepal\\\" title=\\\"Nepal\\\">Nepal<\\/a>, is a Hindu open air temple dedicated to Lord&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Mahavishnu\\\" title=\\\"Mahavishnu\\\">Mahavishnu<\\/a>. Budhanilkantha Temple is also known as the Narayanthan Temple for Hindus, and can be identified by a large reclining statue of Lord&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Mahavishnu\\\" title=\\\"Mahavishnu\\\">Mahavishnu<\\/a>. However In the Buddhist community, the term \\\"Buddhanilkantha\\\" refers to one of the various manifestations of Avalokiteshvara. The name means \\\"Blue-Throated Buddha.\\\"<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<h1>&nbsp;<\\/h1>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":3,\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Kathmandu \\/ Pokhara ( 210 KMS )\",\"date\":\"15-07-2025 Tuesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Drive to Pokhara. Pokhara is 210 kms from Kathmandu and is a 7 hours drive approx. From Pokhara town (2,352 feet) in good weather there are splendid views right from the hotel. On the way you have an option at an extra cost of doing the river rafting ( Inr 3000 nett per person ) or visit the Manakamna Temple \\u201c Goddess of Fulfilling Wishes\\u201d where you are taken by a cable ride ( Inr 670 nett per person payable directly ) of 10 mins.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":4,\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pokhara\",\"date\":\"16-07-2025 Wednesday\",\"todo\":\"<p>This morning you will go for a excursion trip to&nbsp;Sarangkot. Sarangkot is the most popular tourist destination from where the tourist can enjoy the great view of the Pokhara Valley and the magnificent view of the mountains. Sarangkot is only 13 kms from Lake Side, Pokhara. Sarangkot is the highest view point for a sunrise and it is just 1592m high. Sarangkot is&nbsp; cooler than Pokhara. Sarangkot can be reached easily by 45 to 60 minutes by a car ride to the top from Pokhara. Many tourists come to Sarangkot for sunrise view and go back.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>From Sarangkot, on the northern direction we can see Dhaulagiri in the far west. Annapurna range is visible when the weather is clear on the same side. On the southern direction the village overlooks the city of Pokhara and its lake on the north-western outskirts of the city.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 03 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\n\\n<p>This afternoon you will visit Bindebasini Temple. This is one of the oldest temples in Pokhara was a part of Kaski Kingdom, the main deity of the temple, Goddess Durga, was brought from India . Apart from the peace and tranquility that can be felt in this region, the premises of the temple offers a good view of the Himalaya on a clear day. The temple is in the area of the bazaar, hence a journey of the old bazaar can be combined with a visit to the temple. Sightseeing to Devi\\u2019s fall, also known as Patale Chango is an awesome waterfall lying 2 km southwest of Pokhara. During summer and rainy season, the waterfall takes its real form, with gushing water splashing and making its way through the rocks. Just opposite of Devi\\u2019s fall, on the other side of the road, there is Gupteshwor Cave. This cave is popular for the different natural forms made from limestone deposits. Photography is strictly prohibited inside the cave.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel.<\\/strong><\\/em>( The above sightseeing is for a maximum of 03 hours after the vehicle reports at the hotel )<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":5,\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Pokhara \\/ Nagarkot\",\"date\":\"17-07-2025 Thursday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Drive back to Kathmandu. Continue drive to Nagarkot. Nagarkot is situated 32 kilometers, 1.5&nbsp; hrs drive east of Kathmandu at an altitude of 2,175 meters. The panoramic view of the major peaks including Mt. Everest can be seen from here. This place is also famous for viewing sunrise and sunset.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><em><strong>Overnight at hotel.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Day\",\"day\":6,\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Nagarkot \\/ Airport\",\"date\":\"18-07-2025 Friday\",\"todo\":\"<p>Drive straight to the airport which is 1.5 hours drive approx to board flight for onward journey.<\\/p>\"}]', '[{\"id\":1,\"from\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"to\":\"Kathmandu (KTM)\",\"name\":\"IndiGo\",\"fno\":\"1153\",\"dep_date\":\"13 Jul 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"13 Jul 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"11:05 AM\",\"arv_time\":\"01:00 PM\",\"fare\":\"15627\"},{\"id\":2,\"from\":\"Kathmandu (KTM)\",\"to\":\"Delhi (DEL)\",\"name\":\"Royal Nepal Airlines\",\"fno\":\"217\",\"dep_date\":\"18 Jul 2025\",\"arv_date\":\"18 Jul 2025\",\"dep_time\":\"01:25 PM\",\"arv_time\":\"02:50 PM\",\"fare\":\"25275\"}]', '[]', '[{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"13\\/07\\/2025\",\"city\":\"KATHMANDU\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Tibet\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room + 01 Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"15\\/07\\/2025\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"15\\/07\\/2025\",\"city\":\"POKHARA\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Pokhara Batika\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room + 01 Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"17\\/07\\/2025\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"17\\/07\\/2025\",\"city\":\"NAGARKOT\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Himalayan Villa\",\"room_type\":\"DBL Room + 01 Extra Bed\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"18\\/07\\/2025\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li>Return Airfare<em><strong>&nbsp;Ex-Delhi.</strong></em></li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nts</strong>&nbsp;Accommodation at Hotel Tibet&nbsp;at <strong>Kathmandu.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>02&nbsp;Nts&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation at Hotel Pokhara Batika&nbsp;at <b>Pokhara</b>.</li>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Nt&nbsp;</strong>Accommodation at Hotel Himalayan Villa at <em><strong>Nagarkot</strong></em>.</li>\n	<li><strong>01 Room</strong> on<strong> </strong><strong><em>DBL&nbsp;Sharing + 01 Extra Bed.</em></strong></li>\n	<li>All&nbsp;<strong>Breakfasts.</strong></li>\n	<li><strong>All Arrival &amp; Departure Assistance&nbsp;</strong>at the Airport.</li>\n	<li>All Transfers &amp; Sightseeings by&nbsp;<strong>A/C Vehicle on PVT basis.</strong></li>\n	<li>All Taxes.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\n	<li>Services other than specified.</li>\n	<li>Entrance fee at the monumental sites during the sightseeing</li>\n	<li>Guide during the sightseeing</li>\n	<li>Any expenses of personal nature such as drinks, laundry, telephone/fax calls.</li>\n	<li>Any expenses caused by reasons beyond our control such as flight delays, rescheduling or cancellations, any accidents, medical evacuations, riots, strikes, etc.</li>\n	<li>Any tips to drivers, hotel staff, any meals apart from the ones mentioned above.</li>\n	<li>Any other tax or service charge that could be enforced during this period will be extra &amp;amp; need to borne by you.</li>\n	<li>NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded</li>\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '{\"profit_percent\":\"15\",\"package\":{\"flight_cost\":40902,\"land_cost\":\"77600\",\"hotel_cost\":null,\"transport_cost\":null},\"extra\":[],\"cost_price\":118502,\"amount_of_percent\":\"Rs 17775.3\",\"selling_price\":136277.2999999999883584678173065185546875}', 'MZQ/0696/062025', 136275, 45425, 0, '2025-06-13 06:37:50', '2025-06-13 06:45:21', 0, 1, '\"<p><b>Vehicle allocation:<\\/b><\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li><b>2 pax Car : Swift Dezire\\/ Skoda Rapid\\/Similar&nbsp;<\\/b><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p><b>Hand-phone SIM card:<\\/b><\\/p>\\n\\n<p>Upon arrival in Kathmandu at the International Airport better known as \\\"Tribhuwan International Airport\\\". After collecting your baggage there are Two Telephone companies known as&nbsp;<b>\\\"NCell &amp; NTC<\\/b>&nbsp;( Nepal Telecommunication). They have a Stall each. One Passport size photo and a copy of the passport will be required. One can purchase a Sim. Activation time is 10 mins on an average. Cost is Inr 150 per Sim which can be topped off as per requirement. It will be a 3G card. We are not in a position to take out the Sim in advance. Above is subject to change as per the Telecommunication &nbsp;Regulations.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><b>Please note :<\\/b><\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>Vehicle will not be at disposal <\\/strong><\\/em>but will perform its respective duties, as per the itinerary&nbsp;only. No additional running for shopping \\/ lunches \\/ dinners\\/ additional sightseeing etc. will not be allowed. The vehicle will strictly be from Point to Point basis only.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em>The above <strong>rates are valid for Indian Nationals holding Indian Passport \\/ Voter\'s ID only.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/li>\\n\\t<li><em><strong>The above rates will not stand good<\\/strong> for any other nationality, <strong>OCI and PIO card as it is not valid in Nepal <\\/strong>and cannot be used as an identification by any Nationals.<\\/em><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li><b>Hotel Check - in Time:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1500 hrs<\\/b><\\/li>\\n\\t<li><b>Hotel Check - out Time:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1100 hrs<\\/b><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<p><b>The above cost excludes:<\\/b><\\/p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n\\t<li>Services other than specified.&nbsp;<b>Entrance fee at the monumental sites during the sightseeing<\\/b>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<b>Guide during the sightseeing<\\/b><\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Any expenses of personal nature such as drinks, laundry, telephone\\/fax calls.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Any expenses caused by reasons beyond our control such as flight delays, rescheduling or cancellations, any accidents, medical evacuations, riots, strikes, etc.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Any tips to drivers, hotel staff, any meals apart from the ones mentioned above.<\\/li>\\n\\t<li>Any other tax or service charge that could be enforced during this period will be extra &amp; need to borne by you.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\"', 0, 0),
(708, 'Mr. Abhishek Dokania', 'BNI', '7003447986', 'info@multizonetravels.com', 'UTTRAKHAND', '2025-07-13', 6, 0, 3, '[{\"title\":\"Sunday\",\"day\":\"Day 1\",\"index\":0,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Delhi \\u2013 Jim Corbett (250 km \\/ 6\\u20137 hrs)\",\"date\":\"13-07-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Your journey to the tranquil landscapes of Uttarakhand begins as you are picked up from Delhi railway station or airport. A scenic drive takes you through the plains and forests to the iconic Jim Corbett National Park, home to Bengal tigers and a variety of wildlife.On arrival, check into your forest-side resort. The rest of the day is free to relax and enjoy the peace of the surroundings. You may explore the resort\\u2019s nature trails or simply unwind by the lush greenery.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><br data-end=\\\"921\\\" data-start=\\\"918\\\" \\/>\\n<em><strong>Overnight stay in Corbett<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Monday\",\"day\":\"Day 2\",\"index\":1,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Corbett \\u2013 Kainchi Dham \\u2013 Nainital (160 km \\/ 3\\u20134 hrs)\",\"date\":\"14-07-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"433\\\" data-start=\\\"263\\\">Start your morning with a hearty breakfast at the resort in Corbett. Post breakfast, visit the sacred <strong data-end=\\\"388\\\" data-start=\\\"365\\\">Garjiya Devi Temple<\\/strong>, a revered shrine perched by the Kosi River.After your visit, begin your journey toward Nainital. En route, take a spiritual stop at the <strong data-end=\\\"551\\\" data-start=\\\"528\\\">famous Kainchi Dham<\\/strong>, the ashram of <strong data-end=\\\"587\\\" data-start=\\\"567\\\">Neem Karoli Baba<\\/strong>, nestled amidst tranquil hills and visited by devotees from across the globe, including tech icons like Steve Jobs and Mark Zuckerberg.After soaking in the peaceful vibes of the ashram, continue your drive to <strong data-end=\\\"811\\\" data-start=\\\"799\\\">Nainital<\\/strong>. On arrival, check in to your hotel. Spend the evening at leisure \\u2014 you may stroll along the Mall Road or relax by the lakeside.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"976\\\" data-start=\\\"942\\\"><em><strong data-end=\\\"976\\\" data-start=\\\"946\\\">Overnight stay in Nainital<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Tuesday\",\"day\":\"Day 3\",\"index\":2,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Nainital Local Sightseeing\",\"date\":\"15-07-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p data-end=\\\"2104\\\" data-start=\\\"1617\\\">Start your day with breakfast and head out for a refreshing sightseeing tour of the \\u201cCity of Lakes.\\u201d Visit the region\\u2019s famous water bodies including <strong data-end=\\\"1824\\\" data-start=\\\"1767\\\">Talli Taal, Malli Taal, Sat Taal, and Naukuchiya Taal<\\/strong>. Enjoy optional boating at the serene <strong data-end=\\\"1877\\\" data-start=\\\"1863\\\">Naini Lake<\\/strong>, followed by a spiritual visit to <strong data-end=\\\"1933\\\" data-start=\\\"1912\\\">Naina Devi Temple<\\/strong>, situated by the lakeside.In the evening, take a walk down the charming <strong data-end=\\\"2022\\\" data-start=\\\"2009\\\">Mall Road<\\/strong>, known for its shops, caf\\u00e9s, and lakeside views.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p data-end=\\\"2104\\\" data-start=\\\"1617\\\"><br data-end=\\\"2074\\\" data-start=\\\"2071\\\" \\/>\\n<em><strong data-end=\\\"2104\\\" data-start=\\\"2074\\\">Overnight stay in Nainital<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Wednesday\",\"day\":\"Day 4\",\"index\":3,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Nainital \\u2013 Mussoorie (300 km \\/ 6\\u20137 hrs)\",\"date\":\"16-07-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast, check out and drive towards the \\u201cQueen of Hills\\u201d \\u2014 <strong data-end=\\\"2253\\\" data-start=\\\"2240\\\">Mussoorie<\\/strong>. The route is picturesque, winding through valleys and pine-clad ridges. On arrival, check into your hotel and enjoy the cool hill breeze. The evening is free to relax or step out to explore the peaceful surroundings.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><br data-end=\\\"2474\\\" data-start=\\\"2471\\\" \\/>\\n<em><strong data-end=\\\"2505\\\" data-start=\\\"2474\\\">Overnight stay in Mussoorie<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Thursday\",\"day\":\"Day 5\",\"index\":4,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Mussoorie Local Sightseeing\",\"date\":\"17-07-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast, head out to explore Mussoorie\\u2019s natural charm. Visit <strong data-end=\\\"2649\\\" data-start=\\\"2631\\\">Mussoorie Lake<\\/strong>, enjoy the cascading beauty of <strong data-end=\\\"2697\\\" data-start=\\\"2681\\\">Kempty Falls<\\/strong>, and stroll through the colorful <strong data-end=\\\"2749\\\" data-start=\\\"2731\\\">Company Garden<\\/strong>.Later, take a walk along <strong data-end=\\\"2791\\\" data-start=\\\"2778\\\">Mall Road<\\/strong>, lined with colonial-style shops and caf\\u00e9s. For a panoramic view of the Doon Valley, opt for a thrilling ride on the <strong data-end=\\\"2931\\\" data-start=\\\"2909\\\">Gun Hill Cable Car<\\/strong> (optional).<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><br data-end=\\\"2946\\\" data-start=\\\"2943\\\" \\/>\\n<em><strong data-end=\\\"2977\\\" data-start=\\\"2946\\\">Overnight stay in Mussoorie<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Friday\",\"day\":\"Day 6\",\"index\":5,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Mussoorie \\u2013 Rishikesh (80 km \\/ 2\\u20133 hrs)\",\"date\":\"18-07-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>After breakfast, check out and drive to <strong data-end=\\\"3098\\\" data-start=\\\"3085\\\">Rishikesh<\\/strong>, the spiritual heart of Uttarakhand. En route, visit <strong data-end=\\\"3179\\\" data-start=\\\"3152\\\">Sahastradhara Waterfall<\\/strong>, <strong data-end=\\\"3200\\\" data-start=\\\"3181\\\">Sai Baba Temple<\\/strong>, and <strong data-end=\\\"3237\\\" data-start=\\\"3206\\\">Prakasheswar Mahadev Temple<\\/strong> in Dehradun.Arrive in Rishikesh and check into your hotel. Later, explore the town\\u2019s spiritual icons: walk across <strong data-end=\\\"3371\\\" data-start=\\\"3355\\\">Laxman Jhula<\\/strong> and <strong data-end=\\\"3389\\\" data-start=\\\"3376\\\">Ram Jhula<\\/strong>, and visit <strong data-end=\\\"3417\\\" data-start=\\\"3401\\\">Geeta Bhawan<\\/strong> and <strong data-end=\\\"3438\\\" data-start=\\\"3422\\\">Swarg Ashram<\\/strong> on the opposite bank of the Ganges.As the sun sets, witness the magical <strong data-end=\\\"3529\\\" data-start=\\\"3514\\\">Ganga Aarti<\\/strong> at <strong data-end=\\\"3553\\\" data-start=\\\"3533\\\">Parmarth Niketan<\\/strong>, a soulful and serene end to the day.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><br data-end=\\\"3594\\\" data-start=\\\"3591\\\" \\/>\\n<em><strong data-end=\\\"3625\\\" data-start=\\\"3594\\\">Overnight stay in Rishikesh<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Saturday\",\"day\":\"Day 7\",\"index\":6,\"image\":null,\"caption\":\"Rishikesh \\u2013 Delhi (250 km \\/ 6\\u20137 hrs)\",\"date\":\"19-07-2025\",\"todo\":\"<p>Enjoy your final breakfast amidst the spiritual calm of Rishikesh. Post check-out, begin your return journey to Delhi with beautiful memories and rejuvenated spirits.Drop-off at Delhi railway station or airport.<\\/p>\\n\\n<p><br data-end=\\\"3907\\\" data-start=\\\"3904\\\" \\/>\\n<em><strong data-end=\\\"3951\\\" data-start=\\\"3907\\\">Tour ends with a heart full of memories.<\\/strong><\\/em><\\/p>\"}]', '[]', '[]', '[{\"id\":0,\"check_in\":\"13\\/07\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Jim Corbett\",\"hotel_name\":\"Sunday Alaya Hotel & Resort \\/ Similar\",\"rate\":\"6300\",\"room_type\":\"Club Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"14\\/07\\/2025\"},{\"id\":1,\"check_in\":\"14\\/07\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Nainital\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Harshikhar A Panoramic Lake view Property\\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"16\\/07\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"14200\"},{\"id\":2,\"check_in\":\"16\\/07\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Mussoorie\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel The Palm Aryan\\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":2,\"check_out\":\"18\\/07\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"11500\",\"rooms\":1},{\"id\":3,\"check_in\":\"18\\/07\\/2025\",\"city\":\"Rishikesh\",\"hotel_name\":\"Hotel Clarks Inn Express\\/ Similar\",\"room_type\":\"Deluxe Room\",\"rooms\":1,\"meal\":\"cp\",\"nights\":1,\"check_out\":\"19\\/07\\/2025\",\"rate\":\"5800\"}]', '<ul>\n	<li>Airline seats/fare and hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of confirmation.</li>\n	<li>In case of unavailability in the listed hotels, arrangement for an alternate accommodation will be made in a hotel of similar standard.</li>\n	<li>There will be no refund for unused nights or early check-out (In case of Medical condition it completely depends on hotel policy).</li>\n	<li>Check-in and check-out times at hotels would be as per hotel policies. Early check-in or late check-out is subject to availability and may be chargeable by the hotel.</li>\n	<li>The price does not include expenses of personal nature, such as laundry, telephone calls, room service, alcoholic beverages, mini bar charges, tips, portage, camera fees etc.</li>\n	<li>Multi Zone Travels reserves the right to modify the itinerary at any point, due to reasons including but not limited to: Force Majeure events, strikes, fairs, festivals, weather conditions, traffic problems, overbooking of hotels / flights, cancellation / re-routing of flights, closure of / entry restrictions at a place of visit, etc. While we will do our best to make suitable alternate arrangements, we would not be held liable for any refunds/compensation claims arising out of this.</li>\n	<li>In case a flight gets cancelled, Multi Zone Travels will not be liable to provide any alternate flights within the same cost, any additional cost incurred for the same shall be borne by the traveller.</li>\n	<li>For more details click <a href=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/anilsam90/image/upload/v1534070888/terms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></li>\n</ul>', '[]', '<ul>\n	<li><strong>01&nbsp;Night</strong> accommodation at Hotel Sunday Alaya Hotel &amp; Resort / Simi